window.EILUNE_DATA = {"title":"Eilune Codex","subtitle":"A living archive of the world of Eilune","categories":["Lore","Characters","Factions","Places","Bestiary"],"groupOrders":{"Lore":["Major Events","Major Phenomena","Major Divinity","Calendars and Festivals","Tales and Lore","The Traveler’s Hymnal","Alliants"],"Characters":["Major Players"],"Factions":["Factions"],"Places":["Holy Empire of Runvegr","Ushana Dynasty","Wisivashu","Ember Hinterlands","Coskoreia Republic","Caaddorret Wilds"],"Bestiary":["Bestiary"]},"counts":{"Lore":41,"Characters":14,"Factions":4,"Places":44,"Bestiary":12},"featured":["the-ribbon","the-divergence","magic-and-vril","holy-empire-of-runvegr","the-tesseris","the-empress"],"entries":[{"name":"The Thirty Day War","category":"Lore","group":"Major Events","type":"text","slug":"the-thirty-day-war","hero":"assets/Background-30DayWar.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p><strong>The Thirty Day War: A Pivotal Moment in Eilune's History</strong></p><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Background-30DayWar.webp\"/><p>The Thirty Day War, fought a little over a millennium ago, stands as the last major conflict on the continent of Eilune, a testament to the volatile power struggles that have shaped the world. This brief yet intense war saw The Holy Empire of Runvegr and Efra Dorei, a once-mighty nation reduced to a shadow of its former self, clashing over the territories on the eastern portion of the continent.</p><p><strong>The Creeping Shadow of Efra Dorei</strong></p><p>Having been previously repelled by Runvegr, Efra Dorei embarked on a campaign to reclaim its lost stature, slowly annexing territories that had been claimed by the scholarly nation of Wisivashu. In response to this aggression, Wisivashu chose withdrawal over conflict, abandoning their mainland territories and retreating to their home island, thereby allowing Efra Dorei to extend its dominion across the continent with startling ease.</p><p><strong>The Final Stand and The Emergence of The Ribbon</strong></p><p>The conflict reached its zenith on the lands now known as the Wastes, where the armies of Runvegr and Efra Dorei engaged in a relentless battle that lasted for twenty-nine days without yielding an inch of ground to either side. It was on the thirtieth day, amidst the chaos of battle, that The Ribbon—a strip of impenetrable darkness—descended from the sky and onto the battleground, instantly killing those caught within its shadowy embrace. Subsequent attempts to penetrate The Ribbon by both sides resulted in silence, with no troops returning to tell the tale.</p><p><strong>Aftermath and Accusations</strong></p><p>The war ended in a stalemate, with The Ribbon serving as a deadly demarcation line between the two nations. Accusations flew from both sides, each blaming the other for resorting to forbidden magics to cleave Eilune in two, thereby creating an insurmountable barrier that would forever alter the continent's destiny.</p><p>The Thirty Day War, though brief, left an indelible mark on Eilune, its legacy enduring in the division wrought by The Ribbon and the reshaped political boundaries that followed. This conflict underscores the drastic measures nations will undertake in the pursuit of power and the unpredictable consequences of such endeavors. The war and the emergence of The Ribbon serve as a grim reminder of the destructive potential of magic and conflict, shaping the history and culture of Eilune for centuries to come.</p>","summary":"The Thirty Day War: A Pivotal Moment in Eilune's History The Thirty Day War, fought a little over a millennium ago, stands as the last major conflict on the continent of Eilune, a testament to the volatile power…","sort":0,"sourceJournal":"Major Events"},{"name":"The Divergence","category":"Lore","group":"Major Events","type":"text","slug":"the-divergence","hero":"assets/Background-Divergence.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<div><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Background-Divergence.webp\"/></div><hr/><p><strong>The Divergence: A World Transformed</strong></p><p>Occurring approximately 1,000 years ago, The Divergence remains one of the most profound mysteries of Eilune. Its origins and the full extent of its effects are subjects of endless speculation and scholarly debate among the nations of Eilune. Despite various theories about what caused this cataclysmic event, the truth remains elusive, with conjecture being the only basis for understanding.</p><p><strong>Eyewitness Accounts</strong></p><p>The few accounts of The Divergence come from elderly elves residing within Efra Dorei, making their testimonies rare and valuable. These witnesses describe an abrupt transition from day to night, accompanied by a tremendous roaring and a sensation of the sky itself being torn apart. A singular point of light in the darkness heralded the descent of what appeared to be meteors, each impact reshaping the world in unimaginable ways—mountains collapsed and rose anew; bodies of water evaporated, giving way to swamps; and entire villages disappeared as climates underwent drastic and sudden changes.</p><p><strong>Aftermath and Cosmic Shifts</strong></p><p>The immediate aftermath of The Divergence saw Eilune radically transformed. Astronomers observed entirely new constellations in the night sky, and the presence of three moons instead of the familiar single moon marked a clear departure from the known world. The cataclysm had profound implications for the practice of magic and the connection between deities and their followers. Clerics, paladins, and warlocks found themselves cut off from their divine patrons, and mages faced catastrophic consequences when attempting even the simplest spells.</p><p><strong>The Quest for Understanding</strong></p><p>In the years following The Divergence, attempts to explore beyond Eilune's borders have met with silence, further deepening the mystery of the event's global impact. Scholars and adventurers alike continue to study the phenomenon, searching for a way to reverse or understand the changes it wrought. However, without knowledge of The Divergence's true cause, such efforts often end in frustration and futility.</p><p>The Divergence stands as a testament to the unpredictable power of the universe and its capacity to alter the course of history in an instant. It has left Eilune and its inhabitants forever changed, facing a new reality far removed from the world they once knew. The event's lingering effects on the physical landscape, the cosmos, and the fabric of magic itself continue to shape the destiny of Eilune, a world reborn under the shadow of an enduring mystery.</p>","summary":"The Divergence: A World Transformed Occurring approximately 1,000 years ago, The Divergence remains one of the most profound mysteries of Eilune. Its origins and the full extent of its effects are subjects of endless…","sort":1000,"sourceJournal":"Major Events"},{"name":"The Sundering Charge","category":"Lore","group":"Major Events","type":"text","slug":"the-sundering-charge","hero":"assets/Background-SunderingCharge.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<div><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Background-SunderingCharge.webp\"/></div>\n<hr/>\n<p>There are places in Eilune where the past refuses to stay buried. In the cold shadow of Miskunnkvama, one such wound lingers: a vril echo of shattered ambition and bloodied steel.</p>\n<p data-end=\"633\" data-start=\"210\">Long ago, as the Tesseris began to tighten their grip on Runvegr, a band of Dragoons sought to claim their place as the land’s true protectors and ruling body. But strength alone was not enough. In secret, they turned to forbidden magic, forging an uneasy alliance with mages who promised them power beyond mortal limits. A ritual was devised, one meant to bind vril into their very essence, to make them more than warriors, more than men.</p>\n<p data-end=\"647\" data-start=\"635\">It failed.</p>\n<p data-end=\"1020\" data-start=\"649\">The ritual collapsed in on itself, twisting vril into a wild storm that ripped through its makers. What remains now is not their bodies, but their last moments, frozen in the air like a half-finished thought. The clash of spectral lances, the roar of voices crying out for victory that never came, and the ghostly shimmer of warriors caught in an endless, futile charge.</p>\n<p data-end=\"1213\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-start=\"1022\">To step too close is to invite the past to reach for you, to feel the weight of their desperation, their fury, their fear. And for the unlucky few, the echo does not merely play out, it <em>pulls</em>.</p>","summary":"There are places in Eilune where the past refuses to stay buried. In the cold shadow of Miskunnkvama, one such wound lingers: a vril echo of shattered ambition and bloodied steel. Long ago, as the Tesseris began to…","sort":1000,"sourceJournal":"Major Events"},{"name":"The Ribbon","category":"Lore","group":"Major Phenomena","type":"text","slug":"the-ribbon","hero":"assets/Background-The Ribbon.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<div><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Background-The Ribbon.webp\"/></div>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>The Ribbon: A Millennium of Darkness</strong></p>\n<p>A thousand years ago, the continent of Eilune was forever changed by the emergence of The Ribbon, a catastrophic event that simultaneously concluded the Thirty Day War and reshaped the world's destiny. This vast strip of impenetrable darkness slices through the heart of Eilune, severing the continent into two distinct halves and stretching its shadowy tendrils into the sea, possibly encircling the globe. The origins of The Ribbon, whether a manifestation of unleashed magic, a divine intervention, or something else entirely, remain shrouded in mystery.</p>\n<p><strong>A World Divided</strong></p>\n<p>The Ribbon serves as a stark divide, not just geographically but also culturally and politically, between the lands and peoples of Eilune. Its presence is a constant reminder of the war's end and the forces—known or unknown—that can alter the course of history. Travel and communication across this divide are fraught with danger, making The Ribbon a significant barrier to unity and exploration.</p>\n<p><strong>Horrors Within</strong></p>\n<p>The darkness of The Ribbon conceals an untold number of horrors—demons, monsters, and other malevolent entities—that roam its shadowed expanse. The land within is described as barren and dead, a no-man's land where light and sound are beacons for the unspeakable terrors that lurk in the void. These creatures are so numerous and aggressive that any attempt to penetrate The Ribbon's darkness is met with immediate and overwhelming hostility.</p>\n<p><strong>Shadewalkers: The Guides Through Darkness</strong></p>\n<p>In this world of divided lands and perpetual danger, the Shadewalkers emerge as brave, or perhaps desperate, individuals willing to navigate The Ribbon's perils. For a price, they offer to guide travelers across the dark divide, relying on their knowledge of safe paths and their ability to evade or confront the monsters within. However, the life of a Shadewalker is perilous, often brutally short, and marked by moments of betrayal, as some abandon their charges at the first sign of danger.</p>\n<p><strong>Mystery and Exploration</strong></p>\n<p>Despite its dangers, The Ribbon fascinates scholars, adventurers, and the foolhardy, drawn to its mysteries and the possibility of what lies beyond. The theories about its true nature and extent—whether it does indeed encircle the world or holds the key to understanding the cataclysm that created it—fuel expeditions and research, albeit few return from such endeavors.</p>","summary":"The Ribbon: A Millennium of Darkness A thousand years ago, the continent of Eilune was forever changed by the emergence of The Ribbon, a catastrophic event that simultaneously concluded the Thirty Day War and reshaped…","sort":0,"sourceJournal":"Major Phenomena"},{"name":"The Wild Hunt","category":"Lore","group":"Major Phenomena","type":"text","slug":"the-wild-hunt","hero":"assets/Background-WildHunt.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<div><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Background-WildHunt.webp\"/></div>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>The Wild Hunt: Specters of Doom</strong></p>\n<p>Across the continents of Eilune, few phenomena are as feared as the Wild Hunt: a terrifying procession of the dead and undead that rides the tempests, hunting the souls of the living. The mere mention of the Hunt sends shivers down the spines of all who dwell in Eilune, for to encounter them is to face a fate worse than death or to witness devastation unfathomable.</p>\n<p><strong>The Unholy Trio:</strong></p>\n<p>The Hunt is eternally led by one of three dread horsemen, distinguishable by the color of their mounts and the distinct, ominous sounds that accompany their passage:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Tialana</strong>, the fiery harbinger, rides a brilliant red horse that trails flames across the land. Her hunts are infamous for the souls snatched, dragged into the eternal torment of the Hunt.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Dovell</strong>, the harbinger of decay, commands a sickly green steed, spreading poison and blight with every step. His whims are capricious; he may choose to ravage all life in his path or pass by indifferently, leaving only the land cursed in his wake.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Vekra</strong>, the most merciless of the trio, rides a pale white horse with steps that chime like crystal bells. Where Vekra rides, death follows indiscriminately - no life is spared, no quarter given.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Defense Against the Hunt</strong></p>\n<p>There are scant few means to protect oneself from the Wild Hunt. They are beings beyond reason, impervious to pleas or bargains. Their departure is as unpredictable as their arrival, ceasing only when their insatiable hunger for destruction or souls is momentarily quelled, or when the storm they ride scatters to the winds.</p>\n<p><strong>A Harbinger of Doom</strong></p>\n<p>Though a Sorrow Storm might herald their coming, the Wild Hunt can emerge from even the most benign tempests, rendering their appearances among the most feared and unpredictable events in Eilune. Their presence is a stark reminder of the world's fragility and the thin veil that separates the living from the realms of death and despair.</p>","summary":"The Wild Hunt: Specters of Doom Across the continents of Eilune, few phenomena are as feared as the Wild Hunt: a terrifying procession of the dead and undead that rides the tempests, hunting the souls of the living. The…","sort":1000,"sourceJournal":"Major Phenomena"},{"name":"Sorrow Storms","category":"Lore","group":"Major Phenomena","type":"text","slug":"sorrow-storms","hero":"assets/Background-SorrrowStorm.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<div><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Background-SorrrowStorm.webp\"/></div>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>Sorrow Storms: The Ribbon's Offspring</strong></p>\n<p>Contrary to the devastation attributed to the Divergence, Sorrow Storms arise directly from the Ribbon itself, manifesting as fragmented echoes of this mysterious and ominous phenomenon. Connected directly to the Ribbon, these storms serve as a volatile reminder of the cataclysm that divided Eilune, carrying with them the potential for both chaos and calamity.</p>\n<p><strong>Manifestation and Characteristics</strong></p>\n<p>Sorrow Storms defy the expectations of typical weather patterns, emerging both as seemingly normal storms from afar and as sudden, unheralded tempests. Their connection to the Ribbon imbues them with unpredictable and malevolent properties, often acting as harbingers for the dreaded Wild Hunt—a manifestation of demons that brings further destruction.</p>\n<p><strong>Unpredictable Havoc</strong></p>\n<p>The true terror of Sorrow Storms lies in their capricious nature and the varied, often catastrophic, effects they have on the land and those caught within their grasp. Their passage can result in the unleashing of demons, the warping of reality, and a range of fates for individuals unfortunate enough to find themselves in the storm's path—from disappearance and rapid aging to madness or, for the lucky few, miraculous survival.</p>\n<p><strong>A Constant Threat</strong></p>\n<p>Sorrow Storms underscore the volatile magic that saturates Eilune, a land still reeling from the upheavals of the Ribbon and the Divergence. The storms' erratic behavior and destructive potential make them a source of fear and uncertainty, challenging the resilience of the continent's inhabitants and shaping the strategies of those seeking to navigate or mitigate their impact.</p>","summary":"Sorrow Storms: The Ribbon's Offspring Contrary to the devastation attributed to the Divergence, Sorrow Storms arise directly from the Ribbon itself, manifesting as fragmented echoes of this mysterious and ominous…","sort":2000,"sourceJournal":"Major Phenomena"},{"name":"Magic and Vril","category":"Lore","group":"Major Phenomena","type":"text","slug":"magic-and-vril","hero":"assets/Art - Phenomena.png","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<div><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Art - Phenomena.png\"/></div>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>Transformation of Magic Post-Divergence</strong></p>\n<p>In the wake of The Divergence, the landscape of magic in Eilune underwent a radical transformation. The established branches of arcane and divine magic, once drawn from the world and deities respectively, ceased to exist. In their place emerged a new form of energy manipulation, discovered by the Tesseris, which taps into \"vril\"—a previously unknown, omnipresent energy within Eilune.</p>\n<p><strong>Discovery and Manipulation of Vril</strong></p>\n<p>Vril manifests as shimmering silver threads that can be extracted from the environment by those with an innate ability to sense and manipulate this energy. The Tesseris, through experimentation, found that these threads could be intricately woven into specific patterns, which in turn would morph into one of the four new shades of magic, blue, red, black, and white, each representing a unique spectrum of magical capabilities.</p>\n<p><strong>Casting Spells with Vril</strong></p>\n<p>The process of casting spells with vril requires the caster to form, either physically or mentally, the precise woven pattern associated with the desired magical effect. This intricate weaving determines the spell's outcome, with the color of the vril indicating the spell's nature. Once a spell is cast, the vril unravels and disperses back into the environment, though it requires time to fully \"untangle\" and revert to a stable state.</p>\n<p><strong>Consequences of Overuse</strong></p>\n<p>The overuse of vril, whether through casting powerful spells or frequent casting within a localized area, can lead to the creation of Reactionary Storms. These phenomena occur when the residual, tangled threads of vril destabilize, affecting reality in unpredictable and often dangerous ways. This inherent risk places a natural limit on the use of magic, underscoring the need for caution and restraint among practitioners.</p>\n<p><strong>The Four Shades of Magic</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Blue Magic</strong>: Known for its mastery over the souls of monsters, Blue Magic allows practitioners to mimic or absorb the abilities of creatures they encounter. Blue Mages are skilled in fighting like monsters, making them formidable allies on the battlefield.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Red Magic</strong>: Characterized by its ability to combine both black and white magic with skilled swordplay, Red Magic enables practitioners to blend various disciplines into a versatile and effective battle style. Red mages are renowned for their versatility and flair in combat.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Black Magic</strong>: Harnessing the destructive forces of elemental magic, Black Magic allows practitioners to wield pure destructive force. Black mages are capable of causing devastation through the manipulation of water, ice, fire, lightning, and other elements.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>White Magic</strong>: Focused on healing and protection, White Magic empowers practitioners to heal injuries, cure ailments, and provide support to allies. White mages are revered for their ability to bring solace and aid to those in need, making them invaluable members of any party or community.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>","summary":"Transformation of Magic Post-Divergence In the wake of The Divergence, the landscape of magic in Eilune underwent a radical transformation. The established branches of arcane and divine magic, once drawn from the world…","sort":3000,"sourceJournal":"Major Phenomena"},{"name":"Vril Echoes","category":"Lore","group":"Major Phenomena","type":"text","slug":"vril-echoes","hero":"","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Long ago, when the world was torn from its place in the great weave of existence, the Divergence left scars that never fully healed. In the wake of that sundered reality, vril, the raw essence of magic, became the lifeblood of Eilune, filling the void where metaphysical forces once flowed. But vril is not a passive force. It churns, pulses, and remembers.</p>\n<p data-end=\"924\" data-start=\"412\">Vril Echoes are the lingering imprints of moments lost to time, fractures in the weave of magic where vril has imprinted upon itself the memory of an event, a soul, or a place. They are neither spirits nor illusions, but something in between, faint afterimages of past occurrences, playing out again and again as if the world itself is struggling to recall what was. Some whispers in the dark claim they are echoes of those who have vanished, fragments of lost travelers who stepped where the veil was too thin.</p>\n<p data-end=\"1380\" data-start=\"926\">When an Echo manifests, reality bends. Figures appear where none should stand, speaking words long since uttered. Some echoes are benign, a woman calling out for her lost child, a warrior locked in an endless duel, a traveler repeating their last steps before they were swallowed by the unknown. Others are dangerous. Twisted, unstable, capable of dragging the unwary into their rhythm, forcing them to relive the past until they, too, become part of it. As the Echo consumes its victims, it grows in strength and size.</p>\n<p data-end=\"1782\" data-start=\"1382\">The Tesseris have long sought to understand these phenomena, believing that studying them may reveal something deeper about vril’s true nature. They warn against interacting with an Echo, for those who attempt to touch the past too often find themselves ensnared in it. To most, the safest course is to leave them undisturbed, to avoid the places where the air shimmers and the past refuses to die.</p>\n<p data-end=\"2002\" data-start=\"1784\">But the wise traveler knows the signs: the sudden hush of the wind, the flicker of something just outside the light, the sense that someone, or something, is watching, not from the present, but from a moment long gone.</p>\n<p data-end=\"2065\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-start=\"2004\">And sometimes, if one listens closely, the Echo listens back.</p>","summary":"Long ago, when the world was torn from its place in the great weave of existence, the Divergence left scars that never fully healed. In the wake of that sundered reality, vril, the raw essence of magic, became the…","sort":4000,"sourceJournal":"Major Phenomena"},{"name":"Reactionary Storms","category":"Lore","group":"Major Phenomena","type":"text","slug":"reactionary-storms","hero":"","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p><strong>The Unstable Nature of Magic</strong></p>\n<p>In the post-Divergence world of Eilune, the manipulation of vril has opened new avenues of magical power. However, this power comes with inherent instability, prompting societies like Runvegr to impose strict regulations on the use and teaching of magic. This caution stems from the potential for catastrophic events known as reactionary storms, which occur as a direct consequence of the destabilization of vril.</p>\n<p><strong>Reactionary Storms</strong></p>\n<p>Unlike the Sorrow Storms of the Ribbon, which are inherently magical and contain horrors within, reactionary storms are natural disasters amplified to extreme levels by the misuse of magic. These storms emerge in areas where vril has been excessively drawn upon and where spells have been layered to the point of affecting the natural world. The concentration of unwoven vril acts as a catalyst, triggering storms of immense power.</p>\n<p><strong>Characteristics and Impact</strong></p>\n<p>Reactionary storms possess the ferocity of hurricanes magnified many times over, with the capacity to unleash devastating floods, violent winds, and intense lightning strikes. They can persist over areas of concentrated magical disturbance, wreaking havoc until the excess vril dissipates and is reabsorbed into the environment. The destruction wrought by these storms serves as a stark reminder of the volatile nature of magic in Eilune and the need for caution in its use.</p>\n<p><strong>A Delicate Balance</strong></p>\n<p>The existence of reactionary storms underscores the delicate balance between wielding magical power and maintaining harmony with the natural world. It highlights the risks associated with the unregulated use of magic and the importance of understanding the underlying principles of vril to prevent such calamities.</p>","summary":"The Unstable Nature of Magic In the post-Divergence world of Eilune, the manipulation of vril has opened new avenues of magical power. However, this power comes with inherent instability, prompting societies like…","sort":5000,"sourceJournal":"Major Phenomena"},{"name":"Brightglass","category":"Lore","group":"Major Phenomena","type":"text","slug":"brightglass","hero":"assets/Background-Brightglass.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<div><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Background-Brightglass.webp\"/></div><p><strong>Brightglass: A Post-Divergence Marvel</strong></p><p>In the transformed world of Eilune, brightglass emerges as a unique and invaluable crystalline material, discovered beneath the surface of the Bright Plains. Its existence is closely tied to the cataclysmic changes brought about by the Divergence, highlighting the emergence of new resources and possibilities in this reshaped reality.</p><p><strong>Characteristics and Properties</strong></p><p>Brightglass is noted for its remarkable density and weight, distinguishing it from ordinary crystals or glass. However, its most extraordinary feature lies in its capacity to contain vril—specifically, vril that has been woven into complex syllabic structures, effectively allowing it to store spells. This ability to encapsulate magical energy without the risk of dissipating the vril back into the environment positions brightglass as a groundbreaking material in the study and application of magic.</p><p><strong>Implications for Magic and Technology</strong></p><p>The utilization of brightglass to store spells without triggering the layering of unwoven vril significantly reduces the risk of generating reactionary storms, a common hazard associated with the overuse of magic in Eilune. This property has not only made brightglass a valuable commodity in the magical community but has also spurred interest in its potential to bridge the realms of magic and technology. The Coskoreia Republic, in particular, invests heavily in the mining and experimentation with brightglass, seeking ways to integrate its magical containment capabilities with technological advancements.</p><p><strong>Brightglass in Commerce and Conflict</strong></p><p>The high value and utility of brightglass have led to its occasional smuggling out of the Bright Plains, where it enters illegitimate markets and fuels a trade that spans beyond the republic's borders. This illicit commerce underscores the material's desirability and the lengths to which individuals will go to acquire it, hinting at the broader implications for Eilune's economic and political landscapes.</p>","summary":"Brightglass: A Post-Divergence Marvel In the transformed world of Eilune, brightglass emerges as a unique and invaluable crystalline material, discovered beneath the surface of the Bright Plains. Its existence is…","sort":6000,"sourceJournal":"Major Phenomena"},{"name":"Brightcrystal","category":"Lore","group":"Major Phenomena","type":"text","slug":"brightcrystal","hero":"assets/Background-Brightcrystal.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<div><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Background-Brightcrystal.webp\"/></div><p>Brightcrystals, with their ability to store spells, indeed play a pivotal role in the practice of magic across Eilune. Their compact size and portability make them convenient tools for spellcasters, allowing them to carry a diverse array of magical abilities with them wherever they go. However, the process of creating and using brightcrystals is not without its challenges and risks, as the concentration and precision required can pose significant obstacles for all but the most skilled practitioners.</p><p>The stringent regulation of brightcrystals in Runvegr reflects the nation's cautious approach to magic and its potential consequences. By restricting access to these powerful artifacts to only the highest echelons of society, Runvegr seeks to maintain control over the dissemination and use of magic within its borders. However, such measures also breed resentment and fuel the illicit trade of brightcrystals on the black market, where they can fetch exorbitant prices among those willing to skirt the law for access to their power.</p><p>In contrast, the more relaxed attitude towards brightcrystals in Ushana and Coskoreia reflects the differing cultural perspectives on magic and its role in society. In Ushana, where trade and commerce are paramount, the use of brightcrystals may be seen as a valuable commodity to be bought and sold like any other. Similarly, in Coskoreia, where magic and technology are often intertwined, the regulation of brightcrystals may be viewed as less of a priority compared to other concerns.</p><p>Overall, the use and regulation of brightcrystals serve as a microcosm of the broader dynamics at play within Eilune, where the interplay between magic, society, and governance continues to shape the world in profound and unexpected ways.</p>","summary":"Brightcrystals, with their ability to store spells, indeed play a pivotal role in the practice of magic across Eilune. Their compact size and portability make them convenient tools for spellcasters, allowing them to…","sort":7000,"sourceJournal":"Major Phenomena"},{"name":"Mirrorstone","category":"Lore","group":"Major Phenomena","type":"text","slug":"mirrorstone","hero":"","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Among the many subtle tools of the Tesseris, Mirrorstones are among the most trusted.</p><p>A Mirrorstone is a small, smooth disc of polished obsidian or dark glass, easily concealed in the palm or worn as jewelry. Each Mirrorstone is paired to a single network of other stones, allowing messages to appear across all connected stones simultaneously.</p><p>When a Tesseris agent speaks a command word and touches the stone, they can imprint a brief message — no longer than a few sentences — into its surface. The obsidian ripples like disturbed water, then freezes, displaying the message in ghostly, faint silver script.</p><p>Recipients with bonded Mirrorstones will feel a subtle cold pulse when a message arrives. They can simply gaze into the stone to read the missive. After being read, the message lingers for an hour before fading into the stone's depths, erasing all record unless preserved by magic.</p><p>Mirrorstones have a radius of approximately 10 to 15 miles, making them only good for use in a single city. </p>","summary":"Among the many subtle tools of the Tesseris, Mirrorstones are among the most trusted. A Mirrorstone is a small, smooth disc of polished obsidian or dark glass, easily concealed in the palm or worn as jewelry. Each…","sort":8000,"sourceJournal":"Major Phenomena"},{"name":"The Whisperer","category":"Lore","group":"Major Phenomena","type":"text","slug":"the-whisperer","hero":"assets/Deities-WhispererMark.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<div><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Deities-WhispererMark.webp\"/></div>\n<p>No tome records his birth, and no priest claims him, yet the Whisperer claims to be older than any empire that stands upon Eilune. He speaks of himself as a watcher of possibilities, and a collector of interesting stories, particularly yours.</p>\n<p>He knows of Veylith and Niraskos, speaking of them as titans who cast long shadows, yet he stands apart from them. He claims no allegiance and no intention beyond observation.</p>\n<p>His Marks are chaotic sigils, reminiscent of tangled vril paths, shifting subtly when one looks away, but seemingly invisible to all but the Bearers. They are neither blessing nor curse, but permission, a sign that the Whisperer has taken an interest in the Bearer’s story.</p>","summary":"No tome records his birth, and no priest claims him, yet the Whisperer claims to be older than any empire that stands upon Eilune. He speaks of himself as a watcher of possibilities, and a collector of interesting…","sort":9000,"sourceJournal":"Major Phenomena"},{"name":"Whisperwings","category":"Lore","group":"Major Phenomena","type":"text","slug":"whisperwings","hero":"assets/Background-WhisperWings.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<div><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Background-WhisperWings.webp\"/></div>\n<p> </p>\n<p>In the shadowed strongholds of Runvegr, where secrecy weighs heavier than steel, the Tesseris have crafted a chilling marvel: the Whisperwing.</p>\n<p>At first glance, a Whisperwing seems like a creature of myth — a great owl with feathers as pale as snowfall, silent wings, and piercing, almost humanlike eyes. But a closer look reveals the truth: embedded deep into their brows is a Mirrorstone, black as midnight and fused to bone and flesh through secret rites.</p>\n<p>The Mirrorstone, polished and veined with silver, serves as both a receiver and transmitter of thought. Using vril manipulation, the Tesseris forge a permanent connection between bird and stone, binding the creature’s life and mind to its function.</p>\n<p>When tasked with a message, a Tesseris agent simply speaks into a paired stone — and across any distance, the Whisperwing is compelled to deliver the memory. Upon reaching its intended target, the owl locks its gaze onto the recipient, and the Mirrorstone pulses, transferring the stored thought or image directly into their mind.</p>\n<p>Whisperwings are utterly loyal, incapable of betraying their purpose. They do not hunt. They do not speak. They exist only to serve the will of their masters.</p>\n<p>Among commonfolk, Whisperwings are viewed with a mixture of awe and dread. In the wild, one does not simply approach a Whisperwing; it approaches you, and you must hope you were the intended target.</p>\n<p>It is said that some Whisperwings, especially those who outlive their handlers, become twisted echoes of their former selves — roaming the mountains like ghost-laden harbingers, still seeking to deliver messages long since forgotten.</p>","summary":"In the shadowed strongholds of Runvegr, where secrecy weighs heavier than steel, the Tesseris have crafted a chilling marvel: the Whisperwing. At first glance, a Whisperwing seems like a creature of myth — a great owl…","sort":9000,"sourceJournal":"Major Phenomena"},{"name":"The Withering Veil","category":"Lore","group":"Major Phenomena","type":"text","slug":"the-withering-veil","hero":"","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>A strange and unsettling affliction has begun to surface within the borders of Wisivashu, an illness unlike any seen before. Dubbed <em>The Withering Veil</em> by scholars of the Coliseum, its symptoms begin subtly—those afflicted report a growing sense of disconnection, as though the world around them becomes distant or muted. Over time, shadows fade, voices become strangely thin, and in some cases, individuals flicker in and out of perception. As the disease progresses, those suffering from it grow weaker, their presence less tangible, until, at its most dire stages, some simply vanish without a trace.</p><p>Despite the Coliseum’s best efforts, no known cure has been found. Conventional magic, alchemy, and healing techniques have proven ineffective, and the cause remains elusive. Strangely, the illness does not appear to affect everyone equally—while some suffer rapid deterioration, others seem entirely immune. Concerned that answers may lie beyond Wisivashu’s borders, the Coliseum has begun sending healers and scholars to research alternative healing methods, hoping to uncover a solution before the Withering Veil spreads further.</p>","summary":"A strange and unsettling affliction has begun to surface within the borders of Wisivashu, an illness unlike any seen before. Dubbed The Withering Veil by scholars of the Coliseum, its symptoms begin subtly—those…","sort":11000,"sourceJournal":"Major Phenomena"},{"name":"The Traders","category":"Lore","group":"Major Divinity","type":"text","slug":"the-traders","hero":"assets/Deities-Twins.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Ever since the Divergence, the gods and goddesses of the Forgotten Realms have not answered any prayers nor made their presence known. For all intents and purposes, the people of Eilune live as if the divine presences that are now only inscribed in historical context never existed to begin with.</p><p>The divine in a majority of Eilune's existence is almost entirely based on faith . There are no proven instances of the patron deities of the nation-states actually intervening (although there are an inordinate number of myths collected over the course of a thousand years), nor is there evidence of them providing power directly to mortals.</p><hr/><div><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Deities-Twins.webp\"/></div><hr/><p>The patron deities of the Ushana Dynasty, the twin gods Kekha and Amheh are the Keepers of the Living and the Dead, respectively.</p><p><strong>O twin gods bless this land</strong></p><p><strong>To us treasure bestow</strong></p><p><strong>City of Desert Sands</strong></p><p><strong>Water and Gold Below</strong></p><hr/><p><strong>Kekha, the Provider</strong></p><p>Typically worshipped by the Ushanan upper class due to his association with precious metals, bountiful harvests, and good fortune.</p><p><em>May we want for naught coin can buy</em></p><p><em>Never see wealth's river run dry</em></p><p><em>May we find fortune after life</em></p><p><em>For this we pray, we pray twinfold</em></p><hr/><p><strong>Amheh, the Devourer</strong></p><p>Often worshipped by the lower castes of Ushana, Amheh is the final arbiter and judge of the dead, weighing their souls when they pass from this to the next life. Those who are found wanting are consumed by Amheh.</p><p><em>May we all as true equals die</em></p><p><em>Never fear unjust favor's bite</em></p><p><em>May we be judged by what is right</em></p><p><em>For this we pray, we pray twinfold</em></p><hr/>","summary":"Ever since the Divergence, the gods and goddesses of the Forgotten Realms have not answered any prayers nor made their presence known. For all intents and purposes, the people of Eilune live as if the divine presences…","sort":0,"sourceJournal":"Major Divinity"},{"name":"The Maiden","category":"Lore","group":"Major Divinity","type":"text","slug":"the-maiden","hero":"assets/Deities-TheMaiden.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Ever since the Divergence, the gods and goddesses of the Forgotten Realms have not answered any prayers nor made their presence known. For all intents and purposes, the people of Eilune live as if the divine presences that are now only inscribed in historical context never existed to begin with.</p>\n<p>The divine in a majority of Eilune's existence is almost entirely based on faith . There are no proven instances of the patron deities of the nation-states actually intervening (although there are an inordinate number of myths collected over the course of a thousand years), nor is there evidence of them providing power directly to mortals.</p>\n<hr/>\n<div><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Deities-TheMaiden.webp\"/></div>\n<hr/>\n<p>The patron deity of Runvegr, Erov is the maiden goddess of winter and the moon. She is worshipped as both a mother and sister figure to the Tesseris.</p>\n<p><strong>With your light, our hearts take flight,</strong></p>\n<p><strong>In silver dreams and sacred rite.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Solace, shelter, love unbound—</strong></p>\n<p><strong>In Erov’s song, we all are found.</strong></p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>Erov, the Maiden</strong></p>\n<p>Erov is depicted in Runvegr astrology as the largest moon in Eilune's sky. The two smaller moons are worshipped as Erov's pet hounds, Slaine and Bran.</p>\n<p><em>She will hear my song tonight,</em></p>\n<p><em>Maiden bright, full moonlight.</em></p>\n<p><em>See me now, a woman whole,</em></p>\n<p><em>Born of winter, song, and soul.</em></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><em>Secrets held and truths made clear,</em></p>\n<p><em>With your grace, I shed my fear.</em></p>\n<p><em>Guide me, goddess, through the snow,</em></p>\n<p><em>Where only daring daughters go.</em></p>\n<hr/>","summary":"Ever since the Divergence, the gods and goddesses of the Forgotten Realms have not answered any prayers nor made their presence known. For all intents and purposes, the people of Eilune live as if the divine presences…","sort":1000,"sourceJournal":"Major Divinity"},{"name":"The Artificer","category":"Lore","group":"Major Divinity","type":"text","slug":"the-artificer","hero":"assets/Deities-TheArtificer.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Ever since the Divergence, the gods and goddesses of the Forgotten Realms have not answered any prayers nor made their presence known. For all intents and purposes, the people of Eilune live as if the divine presences that are now only inscribed in historical context never existed to begin with.</p><p>The divine in a majority of Eilune's existence is almost entirely based on faith . There are no proven instances of the patron deities of the nation-states actually intervening (although there are an inordinate number of myths collected over the course of a thousand years), nor is there evidence of them providing power directly to mortals.</p><hr/><div><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Deities-TheArtificer.webp\"/></div><hr/><p>The patron deity of Coskoreia Republic, Auran is the goddess of invention and progress.</p><p><em>O Divine and Celestial Innovator, hear our plea,</em></p><p><em>Guide us with your light, grant us clarity to see.</em></p><p><em>In the Republic's name, we sing to thee,</em></p><p><em>Innovate our hearts to set our spirits free.</em></p><hr/><p><strong>Auran, the Artificer</strong></p><p>Auran is a cloaked woman, wearing a clockwork mask and a crown of lightning, symbolizing the mastery of magical and technological convergence. Her temples are grand structures filled with intricate clockwork mechanisms.</p><p><em>Auran, Celestial Artisan, we call upon your grace,</em></p><p><em>Inventor of the cosmos, in you we find our place.</em></p><p><em>Your hands crafted the stars, set the planets to dance,</em></p><p><em>In your light, we find purpose, in your design, we advance.</em></p><p><em>Grant us the skill to create, the vision to innovate,</em></p><p><em>In your image, we strive, in your wisdom, we navigate.</em></p><p><em>Guide our hands as we work, our minds as we dream,</em></p><p><em>In your divine inspiration, our world we redeem.</em></p><hr/>","summary":"Ever since the Divergence, the gods and goddesses of the Forgotten Realms have not answered any prayers nor made their presence known. For all intents and purposes, the people of Eilune live as if the divine presences…","sort":2000,"sourceJournal":"Major Divinity"},{"name":"The Veiled Sage","category":"Lore","group":"Major Divinity","type":"text","slug":"the-veiled-sage","hero":"assets/Deities-TheSage.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Ever since the Divergence, the gods and goddesses of the Forgotten Realms have not answered any prayers nor made their presence known. For all intents and purposes, the people of Eilune live as if the divine presences that are now only inscribed in historical context never existed to begin with.</p><p>The divine in a majority of Eilune's existence is almost entirely based on faith . There are no proven instances of the patron deities of the nation-states actually intervening (although there are an inordinate number of myths collected over the course of a thousand years), nor is there evidence of them providing power directly to mortals.</p><hr/><div><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Deities-TheSage.webp\"/></div><hr/><p>The patron deity of Wisivashu, Esivar is the god of knowledge and mysteries.</p><p><em>Veiled Sage, grant us sight,</em></p><p><em>To see beyond the shadows of the night.</em></p><p><em>In your wisdom, we find our way,</em></p><p><em>Guide us through the mysteries, day by day.</em></p><hr/><p><strong>Esivar, the Veiled Sage</strong></p><p>Esivar is depicted as a figure cloaked in swirling mists, their face hidden by a veil. They are often shown holding a book or a scroll, symbolizing hidden knowledge.</p><p><em>In whispers soft, your teachings flow,</em></p><p><em>In every leaf, in every snow,</em></p><p><em>The unseen threads that bind us all,</em></p><p><em>In your embrace, we stand tall.</em></p><hr/>","summary":"Ever since the Divergence, the gods and goddesses of the Forgotten Realms have not answered any prayers nor made their presence known. For all intents and purposes, the people of Eilune live as if the divine presences…","sort":3000,"sourceJournal":"Major Divinity"},{"name":"Calendar","category":"Lore","group":"Calendars and Festivals","type":"text","slug":"calendar","hero":"","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>The Eilunian calendar is based on the cycles of its three moons, each corresponding to a lunar cycle of one of the moons. Most of Eilune has adopted the Runvegr names for the moons: Erov for the largest moon, and Slaine and Bran as the two smaller moons.</p>\n<p>The calendar consists of 12 months, each with a varying number of days based on the lunar cycle of its corresponding moon.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Frostfall</strong> (28 days, Slaine): The first month of the year, characterized by the arrival of frost and the beginning of winter.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Snowpeak</strong> (30 days, Erov): As Erov reaches its peak brightness, snowfall becomes heavy, covering the land in a blanket of white.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Thawrise</strong> (32 days, Bran): The month of thawing, when the first signs of spring begin to appear, and the ice starts to melt.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Blossomtide</strong> (28 days, Slaine): Flowers bloom across the land, marking the arrival of spring in full force.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Suncrest</strong> (30 days, Erov): Erov shines brightly in the sky, heralding longer days and warmer temperatures.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Glowheat</strong> (32 days, Bran): The peak of summer, characterized by intense heat and long, sunny days.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Skyblaze</strong> (28 days, Slaine): The hottest month of the year, when the sun seems to set the sky ablaze with its fiery colors.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Harvestwatch</strong> (30 days, Erov): The month of harvest, when crops are gathered and stored for the coming winter.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Leafsong</strong> (32 days, Bran): Trees turn golden and red as their leaves begin to fall, signaling the approach of autumn.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Mistveil</strong> (28 days, Slaine): The month of mists, when fog rolls in from the sea and blankets the land.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Mournfall</strong> (30 days, Erov): A somber month, marked by shorter days and colder temperatures as winter approaches.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Deepnight</strong> (32 days, Bran): The longest nights of the year, when the land is covered in darkness and the cold of winter sets in.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<hr/>\n<p>The Eilunian calendar reflects the cyclical nature of life and the seasons, with each month corresponding to a different aspect of the natural world.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p>Each week is seven days long, with the 7th day being a typical day of rest:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Moonday</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Starday</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Lunaday</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Moondown</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Starfall</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Sunspark</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Sunrest</p>\n</li>\n</ol>","summary":"The Eilunian calendar is based on the cycles of its three moons, each corresponding to a lunar cycle of one of the moons. Most of Eilune has adopted the Runvegr names for the moons: Erov for the largest moon, and Slaine…","sort":0,"sourceJournal":"Calendars and Festivals"},{"name":"The Celestial Revelry","category":"Lore","group":"Calendars and Festivals","type":"text","slug":"the-celestial-revelry","hero":"assets/Calendar-CelestialRevelry.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p>The Celestial Revelry is a vibrant and joyful celebration of creativity, innovation, and the wonders of the cosmos, held in honor of Auran, the Celestial Innovator. It is a time for artists, inventors, and dreamers to come together to share their creations and inspire each other to new heights of creativity. The festival lasts for three full days.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>Activities</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Artistic Showcases</strong>: The festival features exhibitions of art, sculpture, and craftsmanship, showcasing the creativity and skill of Coskoreia's artisans. Artists from across the republic display their works in galleries and outdoor installations, and there are competitions and awards for the most innovative creations.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>Inventor's Bazaar</strong>: A bustling marketplace is set up where inventors and tinkerers can showcase their latest inventions and innovations. Visitors can see demonstrations of new technologies and gadgets, and even purchase some of these marvels to take home.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>Musical Performances</strong>: Music is a universal language that transcends boundaries, and the festival features performances by musicians and composers from diverse backgrounds. Concerts are held in outdoor amphitheaters, showcasing a variety of musical styles and genres.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>Interactive Workshops</strong>: Throughout the festival, there are interactive workshops where attendees can learn new skills and techniques from master craftsmen, artists, and inventors. These hands-on experiences allow people to unleash their own creativity and take home something they have made themselves.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>Symbolism</strong></p>\n<p>The Celestial Revelry symbolizes the endless potential of the human spirit to create and innovate, mirroring Auran's role as the Celestial Innovator. It is a time to celebrate the ingenuity and creativity of humanity and to be inspired by the beauty and complexity of the world around us.</p>\n</td>\n<td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Calendar-CelestialRevelry.webp\"/>\n<article>\n<p><strong>When</strong></p>\n<p>Skyblaze 14</p>\n<p><strong>Where</strong></p>\n<p>Coskoreia Republic</p>\n</article>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","summary":"The Celestial Revelry is a vibrant and joyful celebration of creativity, innovation, and the wonders of the cosmos, held in honor of Auran, the Celestial Innovator. It is a time for artists, inventors, and dreamers to…","sort":1000,"sourceJournal":"Calendars and Festivals"},{"name":"The Dragoon's Vigil","category":"Lore","group":"Calendars and Festivals","type":"text","slug":"the-dragoon-s-vigil","hero":"assets/Calendar-DragoonVigil.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table><tbody><tr><td><p>The Dragoon's Vigil is a festival filled with martial displays and celebrations, honoring the elite warriors who protect the realm. The city is adorned with banners and flags bearing the Dragoon's insignia, and the streets are bustling with activity. The sound of drums and trumpets fills the air, adding to the festive atmosphere. The festival culminates in a grand fireworks display, lighting up the night sky in honor of the Dragoons' bravery and dedication.</p><hr/><p><strong>Activities</strong></p><p><strong>Grand Parade</strong>: A procession through the city streets showcasing the Dragoons' skills and military prowess, featuring displays of horsemanship, archery, and swordsmanship.</p><hr/><p><strong>Recruitment Drive</strong>: An opportunity for young men and women to sign up for training with the Dragoons, with demonstrations and trials to test their skills.</p><hr/><p><strong>Combat Tournaments</strong>: Friendly competitions among the Dragoons and aspiring recruits to demonstrate their combat abilities.</p><hr/><p><strong>Drill Demonstrations</strong>: Displays of precision and discipline as the Dragoons perform their signature drills and formations.</p><hr/><p><strong>Memorial Service</strong>: A solemn ceremony to honor fallen Dragoons, with speeches, prayers, and the lighting of candles.</p><hr/><p><strong>Feast and Merriment</strong>: A grand feast where Dragoons, recruits, and citizens come together to celebrate, with music, dancing, and storytelling.</p><hr/><p><strong>Weapon and Armor Displays</strong>: Exhibits showcasing the weaponry, armor, and equipment used by the Dragoons, allowing the public to learn more about their tools and techniques.</p><hr/><p><strong>Symbolism</strong></p><p>The festival serves to honor the Dragoons for their service and sacrifice, as well as to inspire pride and patriotism in the citizens. It also serves as a recruitment drive, attracting young men and women who wish to join the prestigious ranks of the Dragoons. The festival reinforces the importance of military strength and preparedness in protecting the realm and upholding its values.</p></td><td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Calendar-DragoonVigil.webp\"/><article><p><strong>When</strong></p><p>Skyblaze 15</p><p><strong>Where</strong></p><p>Runvegr</p></article></td></tr></tbody></table>","summary":"The Dragoon's Vigil is a festival filled with martial displays and celebrations, honoring the elite warriors who protect the realm. The city is adorned with banners and flags bearing the Dragoon's insignia, and the…","sort":2000,"sourceJournal":"Calendars and Festivals"},{"name":"Festival of Innovation","category":"Lore","group":"Calendars and Festivals","type":"text","slug":"festival-of-innovation","hero":"assets/Calendar-Innovation.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table><tbody><tr><td><p>The Festival of Innovation is a celebration of Coskoreia's ingenuity and technological prowess. The city is transformed into a showcase of the latest advancements in science, magic, and technology, with displays and exhibits that amaze and inspire. The festival draws inventors, engineers, and enthusiasts from far and wide, creating a vibrant atmosphere of creativity and discovery.</p><hr/><p><strong>Activities</strong></p><p><strong>Inventors' Showcase</strong>: Inventors and innovators from across the Coskoreia Republic display their latest creations and technological marvels.</p><hr/><p><strong>Technology</strong> <strong>Fair</strong>: A fair showcasing the latest advancements in technology, including steam-powered machinery, clockwork devices, and magical inventions.</p><hr/><p><strong>Magitech</strong> <strong>Demonstrations</strong>: Displays of magical technology and devices that combine magic with machinery, highlighting Coskoreia's mastery of both.</p><hr/><p><strong>Workshops and Seminars</strong>: Educational sessions where experts share their knowledge and insights into the latest technological trends and developments.</p><hr/><p><strong>Interactive Exhibits</strong>: Hands-on exhibits where festival-goers can interact with and experience cutting-edge technology firsthand.</p><hr/><p><strong>Cosplay Contest</strong>: A contest where participants dress up as their favorite technological or magical characters from fiction or history.</p><hr/><p><strong>Symbolism</strong></p><p>The festival celebrates Coskoreia's commitment to innovation and progress, highlighting the importance of technology and science in shaping the future of the republic. It serves as a platform for showcasing Coskoreia's advancements to the world, attracting investment and collaboration opportunities. The festival also fosters a culture of innovation and curiosity among Coskoreia's citizens, inspiring them to push the boundaries of what is possible.</p></td><td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Calendar-Innovation.webp\"/><article><p><strong>When</strong></p><p>Thawrise 16</p><p><strong>Where</strong></p><p>Coskoreia Republic</p></article></td></tr></tbody></table>","summary":"The Festival of Innovation is a celebration of Coskoreia's ingenuity and technological prowess. The city is transformed into a showcase of the latest advancements in science, magic, and technology, with displays and…","sort":3000,"sourceJournal":"Calendars and Festivals"},{"name":"Festival of the Twin Traders","category":"Lore","group":"Calendars and Festivals","type":"text","slug":"festival-of-the-twin-traders","hero":"assets/Calendar-TwinTraders.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table><tbody><tr><td><p>The Festival of the Twin Traders is a vibrant and lively celebration that highlights Ushana's role as a hub of trade and commerce. The city is decorated with colorful banners and streamers, and the streets are filled with the sounds of music and laughter. The festival creates a sense of unity and community among Ushana's inhabitants, fostering a spirit of generosity and goodwill.</p><hr/><p><strong>Activities</strong></p><p><strong>Market Fair</strong>: A bustling marketplace filled with traders selling goods from across Ushana, including exotic spices, fine textiles, and precious metals.</p><hr/><p><strong>Ceremonial Offerings</strong>: Devotees offer prayers and offerings to Kekha and Amheh at temples and shrines throughout the city.</p><hr/><p><strong>Feast of Plenty</strong>: A communal feast where the rich and poor alike come together to share food and celebrate the blessings of the Twin Traders.</p><hr/><p><strong>The Great Trade</strong>: A reenactment of ancient trade routes and caravans, showcasing Ushana's history as a center of commerce.</p><hr/><p><strong>Artisan</strong> <strong>Exhibitions</strong>: Displays of craftsmanship and artistry, featuring pottery, jewelry, and other goods created by Ushana's skilled artisans.</p><hr/><p><strong>Processions</strong>: Colorful processions through the streets, with participants dressed in traditional costumes and carrying banners and flags.</p><hr/><p><strong>Music and Dance</strong>: Performances of traditional Ushanan music and dance, celebrating the cultural heritage of the region.</p><hr/><p><strong>Symbolism</strong></p><p>The festival honors Kekha and Amheh, the Twin Traders, who are revered as the gods of prosperity and abundance. It serves as a reminder of the importance of trade and commerce in Ushana's history and culture, as well as a celebration of the wealth and prosperity that the Twin Traders bring to the region. The festival also promotes unity and solidarity among Ushana's diverse population, fostering a sense of pride in their shared heritage.</p></td><td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Calendar-TwinTraders.webp\"/><article><p><strong>When</strong></p><p>Harvestwatch 1</p><p><strong>Where</strong></p><p>Ushana</p></article></td></tr></tbody></table>","summary":"The Festival of the Twin Traders is a vibrant and lively celebration that highlights Ushana's role as a hub of trade and commerce. The city is decorated with colorful banners and streamers, and the streets are filled…","sort":4000,"sourceJournal":"Calendars and Festivals"},{"name":"Festival of Silver Moons","category":"Lore","group":"Calendars and Festivals","type":"text","slug":"festival-of-silver-moons","hero":"assets/Calendar-SilverMoons.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table><tbody><tr><td><p>The Festival of Silver Moons is a magical event that transforms the city of Runvegr into a shimmering wonderland. Lanterns and torches cast a soft, silver light over the streets, creating an ethereal atmosphere. The air is filled with the sound of music and laughter, as people come together to celebrate the beauty and mystery of the moons. The festival lasts two weeks.</p><hr/><p><strong>Activities</strong></p><p><strong>Opening</strong> <strong>Ceremony</strong>: The festival begins with a solemn ceremony led by the Tesseris, where prayers are offered to Erov for her guidance and protection.</p><hr/><p><strong>Musical</strong> <strong>Performances</strong>: Musicians play haunting melodies that echo through the streets, creating a magical atmosphere.</p><hr/><p><strong>Dance</strong> <strong>Performances</strong>: Dancers perform graceful routines under the silver light of the moons, captivating the audience with their skill and beauty.</p><hr/><p><strong>Storytelling</strong>: Storytellers share tales of Erov's adventures and wisdom, keeping alive the traditions and legends of the goddess.</p><hr/><p><strong>Moonlight</strong> <strong>Parade</strong>: Participants dress in shimmering costumes and carry lanterns adorned with silver ribbons, parading through the city streets accompanied by music and laughter.</p><hr/><p><strong>Feasting</strong>: The festival is a time of feasting and celebration, with people enjoying traditional foods and drinks in honor of Erov.</p><hr/><p><strong>Crafts</strong> <strong>and</strong> <strong>Artisans</strong>: Local artisans showcase their crafts, with many creating special items inspired by Erov and the moons.</p><hr/><p><strong>Prayer and</strong> <strong>Reflection</strong>: Throughout the festival, there are opportunities for prayer and reflection, as people express their gratitude to Erov and seek her blessings for the future.</p><hr/><p><strong>Symbolism</strong></p><p>The festival holds great significance for the people of Runvegr, as it is a time to honor Erov, the maiden goddess of winter and the moon. It is believed that by celebrating the festival with joy and reverence, the people can invoke Erov's blessing for the coming year, ensuring prosperity and protection for their city and its inhabitants.</p></td><td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Calendar-SilverMoons.webp\"/><article><p><strong>When</strong></p><p>Frostfall 1</p><p><strong>Where</strong></p><p>Runvegr</p></article></td></tr></tbody></table>","summary":"The Festival of Silver Moons is a magical event that transforms the city of Runvegr into a shimmering wonderland. Lanterns and torches cast a soft, silver light over the streets, creating an ethereal atmosphere. The air…","sort":5000,"sourceJournal":"Calendars and Festivals"},{"name":"Festival of Veiled Wisdom","category":"Lore","group":"Calendars and Festivals","type":"text","slug":"festival-of-veiled-wisdom","hero":"assets/Calendar-VeiledWisdom.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table><tbody><tr><td><p>The Festival of Veiled Wisdom is a celebration of knowledge, mystery, and the unseen. It is held in honor of Esivar, the Veiled Sage, patron deity of Wisivashu, and is a time for scholars, mystics, and seekers of wisdom to come together to share knowledge and insights. The festival lasts for seven full days.</p><hr/><p><strong>Activities</strong></p><p><strong>Ritual Offerings</strong>: People make offerings of incense, flowers, and symbolic items representing wisdom and knowledge at temples and shrines dedicated to Esivar.</p><hr/><p><strong>Lectures and Workshops</strong>: Scholars and sages from across Wisivashu and beyond gather to present lectures, workshops, and debates on various topics such as philosophy, metaphysics, magic, and the natural world. These sessions are open to the public and encourage lively discussion and debate.</p><hr/><p><strong>Mystical Performances</strong>: There are performances of music, dance, and theater that explore mystical and philosophical themes, often using symbolism and allegory to convey deeper meanings.</p><hr/><p><strong>Veiled Procession:</strong> A grand procession is held on the final day of the festival, where a statue or representation of Esivar, veiled in mystery, is carried through the streets. This symbolizes the hidden nature of wisdom and the quest to uncover deeper truths.</p><hr/><p><strong>Feasting and Merrymaking</strong>: The festival is also a time for feasting and merrymaking, with street vendors selling a variety of foods and drinks, and people gathering in taverns and inns to celebrate late into the night.</p><hr/><p><strong>Symbolism</strong></p><p>The Festival of Veiled Wisdom symbolizes the quest for knowledge and understanding that lies at the heart of Wisivashu's culture. It encourages people to seek wisdom not just in books and teachings, but also in the mysteries of the world around them and the unseen realms beyond. It is a time to reflect on the deeper meanings of life and the universe, and to celebrate the pursuit of knowledge in all its forms.</p></td><td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Calendar-VeiledWisdom.webp\"/><article><p><strong>When</strong></p><p>Deepnight 22</p><p><strong>Where</strong></p><p>Wisivashu</p></article></td></tr></tbody></table>","summary":"The Festival of Veiled Wisdom is a celebration of knowledge, mystery, and the unseen. It is held in honor of Esivar, the Veiled Sage, patron deity of Wisivashu, and is a time for scholars, mystics, and seekers of wisdom…","sort":6000,"sourceJournal":"Calendars and Festivals"},{"name":"Golden Harvest Festival","category":"Lore","group":"Calendars and Festivals","type":"text","slug":"golden-harvest-festival","hero":"assets/Background-UshanaMarket.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table><tbody><tr><td><p>The Golden Harvest Festival celebrates the abundance of the land and the blessings of Kekha, the Provider. It is a time of gratitude for the bountiful harvests, prosperity in trade, and general wealth and well-being that Kekha is believed to bestow upon his followers.</p><hr/><p><strong>Activities</strong></p><p><strong>Market Fair</strong>: The festival kicks off with a bustling market fair where merchants from far and wide gather to showcase their goods. It's a time for buying, selling, and trading, with a focus on luxury items, precious metals, and fine craftsmanship.</p><hr/><p><strong>Feast of Plenty</strong>: A grand feast is held, featuring dishes made from the finest ingredients and delicacies that symbolize prosperity and abundance. It's a time for indulgence and enjoyment of the fruits of the land.</p><hr/><p><strong>Treasure Hunt</strong>: A popular activity during the festival is a treasure hunt, where participants search for hidden treasures and valuable artifacts. It's a playful way to honor Kekha's blessings of wealth and fortune.</p><hr/><p><strong>Gift Giving</strong>: People exchange gifts, particularly items that represent prosperity and good fortune, such as gold coins, jewelry, or beautifully crafted items. It's a gesture of goodwill and a way to share Kekha's blessings with others.</p><hr/><p><strong>Charity and Generosity</strong>: In addition to celebrating wealth, the festival also emphasizes the importance of generosity and giving back to the community. People are encouraged to donate to the less fortunate and support charitable causes.</p><hr/><p><strong>Symbolism</strong></p><p>The Golden Harvest Festival symbolizes the importance of wealth and material prosperity in society, as well as the obligation to share that wealth with others. It reinforces the idea of abundance and generosity as key values upheld by Kekha and his followers.</p></td><td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Background-UshanaMarket.webp\"/><article><p><strong>When</strong></p><p>Harvestwatch 15</p><p><strong>Where</strong></p><p>Ushana Dynasty</p></article></td></tr></tbody></table>","summary":"The Golden Harvest Festival celebrates the abundance of the land and the blessings of Kekha, the Provider. It is a time of gratitude for the bountiful harvests, prosperity in trade, and general wealth and well-being…","sort":7000,"sourceJournal":"Calendars and Festivals"},{"name":"The Masks of Runvegr","category":"Lore","group":"Calendars and Festivals","type":"text","slug":"the-masks-of-runvegr","hero":"assets/Background-RunvegrMasks.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<div><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Background-RunvegrMasks.webp\"/></div>\n<p>In Runvegr, the mask is more than ornament or disguise, it is identity made manifest.</p>\n<p>Among the nobility, masks are worn at all times in public, a tradition rooted deep in Runvegr’s fractured past. Every mask tells a story. The curve of the brow, the material of the inlay, the shimmer of vril-reactive dye, all speak to lineage, allegiance, rank, and intent. To look upon a noble’s unmasked face is rarer than to see their blood spilled. It is an intimacy few are ever granted, and a disgrace few survive.</p>\n<p>Some wear masks of glass-thread and lacquered bone, others of hammered gold veiled in silk. Each is crafted with painstaking care, passed from parent to child or commissioned anew to mark a rise in status. The nobility's masks are not merely symbolic, they are tools of court and war alike. A half-lowered mask can spark scandal. A mask turned slightly left during a greeting can signal rivalry. To appear without one, even in the most informal of gatherings, is to declare something grave: dissent, grief, defiance, or madness.</p>\n<p>Half-masks are common among merchants, travelers, and servants. Full masks are worn by diplomats, councilors, and Tesseris agents. A mask with no eye holes is a symbol of penitence or punishment. Half-masks with fangs shaped among the bottom are common among Dragoon knights within Kvamaknottr. </p>\n<p>In Kvamaknottr, the custom has spread far beyond noble halls. There, even commoners wear linen masks, simple and pale, as a gesture of respect and order. The origin is debated amongst scholars, but whatever it may be, the mask endures. In Runvegr, what you show is never all you are. And what you hide may one day save your life.</p>","summary":"In Runvegr, the mask is more than ornament or disguise, it is identity made manifest. Among the nobility, masks are worn at all times in public, a tradition rooted deep in Runvegr’s fractured past. Every mask tells a…","sort":7500,"sourceJournal":"Calendars and Festivals"},{"name":"Passage of Souls Festival","category":"Lore","group":"Calendars and Festivals","type":"text","slug":"passage-of-souls-festival","hero":"assets/Calendar-PassageofSouls.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table><tbody><tr><td><p>The Passage of Souls Festival is a solemn and reflective occasion held to honor the departed and seek the guidance and blessings of Amheh the Devourer. It is observed annually during the time when the veil between the living and the dead is believed to be thinnest, allowing for easier communication with the spirits.</p><hr/><p><strong>Activities</strong></p><p><strong>Ritual Offerings</strong>: Families prepare offerings of food, drink, and incense to be placed on altars or gravesites dedicated to their ancestors. These offerings are believed to nourish the spirits and provide them with comfort on their journey to the afterlife.</p><hr/><p><strong>Ceremonial Processions</strong>: Priests and worshippers of Amheh lead processions through the streets, carrying lanterns and chanting prayers for the souls of the departed. The procession leads out of the city and culminates at a desert shrine dedicated to Amheh.</p><hr/><p><strong>Candlelight Vigil</strong>: As night falls, candles are lit in memory of the dead. The soft glow of candlelight illuminates the darkness and is said to guide the spirits of the departed on their journey to the afterlife.</p><hr/><p><strong>Remembering the Departed</strong>: Families gather to share stories and memories of their loved ones who have passed away. It is a time of reflection and honoring the lives and legacies of those who have gone before.</p><hr/><p><strong>Theatre of Shadows</strong>: Performances and plays depicting stories of the afterlife and the journey of the soul are staged. These performances serve as both entertainment and a reminder of the cycle of life and death.</p><hr/><p><strong>Symbolism</strong></p><p>The Passage of Souls Festival symbolizes the belief in the continuity of life beyond death and the importance of honoring and remembering the departed. It is a time to reflect on mortality, the legacy we leave behind, and the interconnectedness of past, present, and future generations.</p></td><td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Calendar-PassageofSouls.webp\"/><article><p><strong>When</strong></p><p>Mournfall 28</p><p><strong>Where</strong></p><p>Ushana Dynasty</p></article></td></tr></tbody></table>","summary":"The Passage of Souls Festival is a solemn and reflective occasion held to honor the departed and seek the guidance and blessings of Amheh the Devourer. It is observed annually during the time when the veil between the…","sort":8000,"sourceJournal":"Calendars and Festivals"},{"name":"Twin Traders' Balance","category":"Lore","group":"Calendars and Festivals","type":"text","slug":"twin-traders-balance","hero":"assets/Calendar-Balance.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table><tbody><tr><td><p>The Twin Traders' Balance is a solemn yet celebratory holiday that honors both Kekha the Provider, and Amheh the Keeper of the Dead. It is a time to reflect on the balance between material wealth and spiritual well-being, and to seek harmony between the two aspects of life.</p><hr/><p><strong>Activities</strong></p><p><strong>Offerings and Prayers</strong>: People make offerings of food, drink, and precious items to both Kekha and Amheh, thanking them for their blessings and seeking their favor for the future. Prayers are offered for abundance in life and a peaceful passage into the afterlife.</p><hr/><p><strong>Feast of Remembrance</strong>: A communal feast is held to remember and honor the ancestors and loved ones who have passed away. It is a time to share stories, memories, and favorite foods of the departed, keeping their spirits alive in the hearts of the living.</p><hr/><p><strong>Judgment Ceremony</strong>: A symbolic reenactment of Amheh's judgment is performed, where individuals confess their wrongdoings and seek forgiveness. It is believed that by acknowledging one's faults and seeking redemption, they can find peace in the afterlife.</p><hr/><p><strong>Charity and Almsgiving</strong>: People are encouraged to give to those in need, reflecting the generosity and compassion of both Kekha and Amheh. This act of charity is seen as a way to balance one's material wealth with spiritual fulfillment.</p><hr/><p><strong>Candle Lighting</strong>: At dusk, candles are lit in honor of the Twin Traders, symbolizing the light of guidance and protection they provide to their followers. It is a time for quiet reflection and meditation on the dual nature of life and death.</p><hr/><p><strong>Symbolism</strong></p><p>The Twin Traders' Balance festival symbolizes the interconnectedness of life and death, wealth and poverty, and material and spiritual well-being. It teaches the importance of finding harmony and balance in all aspects of life, and the need to honor both the material and spiritual aspects of existence.</p></td><td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Calendar-Balance.webp\"/><article><p><strong>When</strong></p><p>Glowheat 14</p><p><strong>Where</strong></p><p>Ushana Dynasty</p></article></td></tr></tbody></table>","summary":"The Twin Traders' Balance is a solemn yet celebratory holiday that honors both Kekha the Provider, and Amheh the Keeper of the Dead. It is a time to reflect on the balance between material wealth and spiritual…","sort":9000,"sourceJournal":"Calendars and Festivals"},{"name":"The Celestial Dragon","category":"Lore","group":"Tales and Lore","type":"simple-quest.lore","slug":"the-celestial-dragon","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Lore-CelestialDragon.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Once, when the world was still young enough to sing clearly, there lived a dragon beyond the highest clouds.</p><p>He was not the largest dragon. He was not the fiercest. He did not hoard gold beneath the mountains, nor did he scorch villages, nor did he demand tribute from kings.</p><p>His scales were pale as moonlit snow, and his wings shimmered like starlight on still water. His eyes were kind, and very, very old.</p><p>His name was Mournamir.</p><p>But children knew him by another name.</p><p>They called him the Last Listener.</p><p>For Mournamir had a gift no other creature possessed. He could hear the heart of every living thing.</p><p>He could hear the joy of fox kits tumbling in the snow. He could hear the dreams of seeds sleeping beneath winter earth. He could hear the laughter hidden inside bells, and the lonely songs whales sang beneath frozen seas.</p><p>When a child cried in the night, Mournamir heard.</p><p>When a soldier wished to go home, Mournamir heard.</p><p>When an old woman whispered goodbye to the stars, Mournamir heard.</p><p>And because he heard so much, he loved the world more than any creature ever had.</p><p>Now, in those days, there was also a woman of silver light and sorrowful eyes. Some called her saint. Some called her witch. Some called her mother.</p><p>But Mournamir simply called her friend.</p><p>The Silver Lady often climbed the tallest mountain to speak with him. There, above the clouds, she would sit between his great silver claws and tell him of the troubles of the world below.</p><p>\"The people are afraid,\" she would say.</p><p>\"I hear them,\" Mournamir would answer.</p><p>\"The earth is wounded.\"</p><p>\"I hear it.\"</p><p>\"The stars themselves tremble.\"</p><p>\"I hear them too.\"</p><p>And each time, the Silver Lady would ask, \"What should I do?\"</p><p>Mournamir never gave easy answers. Dragons rarely do, in the better stories.</p><p>Instead, he would lower his great head beside her and say, \"Listen longer.\"</p><p>So the Silver Lady listened. She listened to rivers. She listened to mountains. She listened to the spaces between breaths. She listened until she could hear what Mournamir heard: that the world was full of grief, yes, but also love. And sometimes love was only grief that had refused to die.</p><p>Then came the night when the sky broke.</p><p>The stars bent like reeds in a storm. The seas rose up in terror. Forests screamed as they froze. Mountains cracked open and spilled fire into the snow. The world began to tear, thread by thread, as if some cruel hand were pulling it apart.</p><p>People prayed. People ran. People held one another and wept.</p><p>And high above it all, Mournamir heard every voice, every cry, every goodbye.</p><p>The Lady stood beneath the broken heavens, silver light pouring from her hands, trying to hold the world together or was she making the wound?</p><p>She looked to the heavens and called, \"Mournamir! I must save them all!\"</p><p>The celestial dragon descended through the storm.</p><p>His wings blotted out the broken stars. His roar shook the valleys. But it was not a roar of anger. It was a roar of mourning.</p><p>He landed beside the Silver Lady, and even then, even at the end of all things, he bowed his head to her.</p><p>\"You have listened,\" he said.</p><p>\"I have,\" the Lady answered, and her tears shone like glass.</p><p>\"Then you know. Not all things can be saved.\"</p><p>The Silver Lady shook her head. \"There must be another way.\"</p><p>\"There is always another way,\" said Mournamir. \"But not always one that leaves us whole.\"</p><p>Then the great dragon turned his gaze upon the breaking world. He heard mothers singing to frightened children. He heard brothers calling through the snow. He heard the last prayers of the lost, the brave, the wicked, the innocent. He heard Eilune and he loved it, so Mournamir did the thing only he could do.</p><p>He reached into his own breast with claws of starlight and drew out his heart. It was silver, it was crystal, it was bright and terrible and beautiful. Inside it lived every sorrow he had ever heard, and every love that had made that sorrow matter.</p><p>The Silver Lady cried out, \"No!\"</p><p>But Mournamir only smiled. \"Take it,\" he said. \"Let grief become an anchor. Let love become a chain. Let what has been lost hold fast what yet remains.\"</p><p>The Silver Lady took the heart in both hands, all life in Eilune was connected and so they all remained. Eilune remained. But, the sky was changed forever after that. The old stars were gone, or hidden, or watching from somewhere too far to reach. The world was colder. Stranger. Full of wounds that would never truly close.</p><p>And Mournamir, the Last Listener, was gone.</p><p>But his heart remained.</p>","summary":"Once, when the world was still young enough to sing clearly, there lived a dragon beyond the highest clouds. He was not the largest dragon. He was not the fiercest. He did not hoard gold beneath the mountains, nor did…","sort":0,"sourceJournal":"Tales and Lore"},{"name":"Along the Ember Road","category":"Lore","group":"The Traveler’s Hymnal","type":"text","slug":"along-the-ember-road","hero":"","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<div><audio controls=\"controls\"><source src=\"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/music/Along%20the%20Ember%20Road.mp3\" type=\"audio/mpeg\"/></audio></div>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>🗺️ Region:</strong> Ember Hinterlands (now sung across the continent)<br/><strong>🕯️ Type:</strong> Wandering Ballad of Long Roads and Quiet Companionship<br/><strong>📜 Traditionally Sung By:</strong> Caravaners, desert guides, lone travelers, and tavern bards along trade routes.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>📖 Lore</strong></p>\n<p data-end=\"741\" data-start=\"345\">Born from the endless ochre trails and wind-scoured plateaus of the Ember Hinterlands, <em data-end=\"454\" data-start=\"432\">Along the Ember Road</em> is a traveler’s hymn, part map, part memory, part prayer. Its origins are unclear, but caravan leaders claim it was first sung by spice traders making the long haul between Altar and the Ushana Dynasty, where days were marked only by the sun’s angle and the slow sway of packbeasts.</p>\n<p data-end=\"1092\" data-start=\"743\">The “Ember Road” itself refers to the winding trails that glow with red-gold light at dawn and dusk, their dust and stone catching the fire of the low sun. For many who walk it, the song is a compass as much as a comfort — verses often change to reflect the singer’s own journey, slipping in local landmarks, scents, or blessings for safe passage.</p>\n<p data-end=\"1861\" data-start=\"1504\">Though born in the Hinterlands, the song has wandered far beyond them. In Runvegrian border towns, it shifts to speak of frost and stone rather than dust and heat; in Ushana, it carries the scent of spice markets and desert winds. No matter the form, the heart of the ballad remains the same: that every road, no matter how harsh, can still lead you home.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>🎼 Lyrics</strong></p>\n<p><em>Through the dust, where the wind wears the stone,</em><br/><em>Past the hills where the wild seeds are sown,</em><br/><em>Carry my heart on the road that I roam,</em><br/><em>Never so far that I can’t find home.</em></p>\n<p><em>Stars spill silver on rivers below,</em><br/><em>Fires fade warm as the night starts to grow,</em><br/><em>Every mile sings the name that I know,</em><br/><em>Bound to the path where the wanderers go.</em></p>\n<p><em>Oh, the road, it winds through the amber and grey,</em><br/><em>Every step steals a piece, yet it shows me the way,</em><br/><em>If the moon’s still kind, and the dawn still burns gold,</em><br/><em>I’ll keep walking my story, along the Ember Road.</em></p>\n<p><em>Hear the bell in the far market square,</em><br/><em>Smell the spice in the cold mountain air,</em><br/><em>I am rich with the worlds that I share,</em><br/><em>With the dust in my hair, and no weight to bear.</em></p>\n<p><em>Oh, the road, it winds through the amber and grey,</em><br/><em>Every step steals a piece, yet it shows me the way,</em><br/><em>If the moon’s still kind, and the dawn still burns gold,</em><br/><em>I’ll keep walking my story, along the Ember Road.</em></p>\n<p> </p>","summary":"🗺️ Region: Ember Hinterlands (now sung across the continent) 🕯️ Type: Wandering Ballad of Long Roads and Quiet Companionship 📜 Traditionally Sung By: Caravaners, desert guides, lone travelers, and tavern bards along…","sort":0,"sourceJournal":"The Traveler’s Hymnal"},{"name":"Daughters of Frost and Song","category":"Lore","group":"The Traveler’s Hymnal","type":"text","slug":"daughters-of-frost-and-song","hero":"","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<div><audio controls=\"controls\"><source src=\"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/music/Daughters%20of%20Frost%20and%20Song.mp3\" type=\"audio/mpeg\"/></audio></div>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>🗺️ Region:</strong> Runvegr<br/><strong>🕯️ Type:</strong> Devotional Hymn of Erov<br/><strong>📜 Traditionally Sung By:</strong> Tesseris mages — most often young women completing their first moonlit vigil, but also senior sisters leading rites during the full moon.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>📖 Lore</strong></p>\n<p><em data-end=\"493\" data-start=\"464\">Daughters of Frost and Song</em> is among the most intimate hymns in the Tesseris’ sacred canon, sung during a mage’s first vigil in service to <strong data-end=\"613\" data-start=\"605\">Erov</strong>, the patron deity of Runvegr. It marks the moment a woman comes fully into her vril-born strength, swearing her voice and will to the sisterhood.</p>\n<p>The hymn is said to have begun in the high valleys, where moonlight falls clear and cold upon the snow. The lyrics speak to a lineage of women bound by frost, silver, and song, drawing strength from those who came before and pledging to guide those yet to come.</p>\n<p>Beyond the Tesseris, the hymn has quietly found its way into Runvegrian villages as a song for daughters leaving home for the first time, mothers gifting their blessing beneath the moon, and winter gatherings where women speak their truths aloud.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>🎼 Lyrics</strong></p>\n<p><em>Oh when the fair moon climbs the sky,</em><br/><em>Through silver woods I wander by,</em><br/><em>My breath a mist, my heart alight,</em><br/><em>I walk her path this winter night.</em></p>\n<p><em>The stars are cold, the winds are still,</em><br/><em>But in her gaze I find my will.</em><br/><em>She watches close, she walks so near,</em><br/><em>The Maiden moon, I feel her here.</em></p>\n<p><em>Erov, fair light, O sister divine,</em><br/><em>Guide us through shadow with hands intertwined.</em><br/><em>Daughters of frost, of silver and song,</em><br/><em>We carry your music, we carry it strong.</em></p>\n<p><em>My mother walked this trail before,</em><br/><em>Her voice a hush, a sacred lore.</em><br/><em>She told me, “Child, when you have grown,</em><br/><em>Let Erov’s moon make your truth known.”</em></p>\n<p><em>So now I stand with open throat,</em><br/><em>Each whispered prayer a trembling note,</em><br/><em>I sing not just for what may be,</em><br/><em>But all the women born from me.</em></p>\n<p><em>She will hear my song tonight,</em><br/><em>Maiden bright, full moonlight.</em><br/><em>See me now, a woman whole,</em><br/><em>Born of winter, song, and soul.</em></p>\n<p><em>Secrets held and truths made clear,</em><br/><em>With your grace, I shed my fear.</em><br/><em>Guide me, goddess, through the snow,</em><br/><em>Where only daring daughters go.</em></p>\n<p><em>Erov, O moon, our winter flame,</em><br/><em>In your name we cast no shame.</em><br/><em>Sister of snow, and mother of might,</em><br/><em>Shine through the veil, rekindle the night.</em></p>\n<p><em>With your light, our hearts take flight,</em><br/><em>In silver dreams and sacred rite.</em><br/><em>Solace, shelter, love unbound—</em><br/><em>In Erov’s song, we all are found.</em></p>\n<p><em>O moon above, soft and white,</em><br/><em>Keep our voices through the night</em></p>","summary":"🗺️ Region: Runvegr 🕯️ Type: Devotional Hymn of Erov 📜 Traditionally Sung By: Tesseris mages — most often young women completing their first moonlit vigil, but also senior sisters leading rites during the full moon. 📖…","sort":1000,"sourceJournal":"The Traveler’s Hymnal"},{"name":"The Coward Stag (Fuck The Elves!)","category":"Lore","group":"The Traveler’s Hymnal","type":"text","slug":"the-coward-stag-fuck-the-elves","hero":"","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<div><audio controls=\"controls\"><source src=\"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/music/The%20Coward%20Stag.mp3\" type=\"audio/mpeg\"/></audio></div><hr/><p><strong>🗺️ Region:</strong> Runvegr<br/><strong>🕯️ Type:</strong> Tavern / Drinking Song<br/><strong>📜 Traditionally Sung By:</strong> Dragoons, dockworkers, fishers, hunters, caravan guards, off-duty soldiers, and very drunk commonfolk, especially in northern taverns, winter festivals, barracks halls, and inns where Efra Dorei is spoken of with contempt.</p><hr/><p><strong>📖 Lore</strong></p><p><em data-end=\"493\" data-start=\"464\">The Coward Stag</em> is one of Runvegr’s most infamous tavern songs: loud, crude, patriotic, and gleefully hostile toward Efra Dorei. Where the sacred hymns of Erov speak of moonlight, sisterhood, and winter truth, this song takes those same devotional symbols and drags them through spilled ale, stomping boots, and shouted curses.</p><p>The song centers on Bran and Slaine, the twin moon-hounds of Erov, imagined as celestial hunters chasing down the emerald stag, a mocking symbol for Efra Dorei and its elven peoples. In older Runvegrian folklore, the stag was said to represent the pride, beauty, and evasiveness of the deep forests. In this song, however, that image is deliberately twisted into cowardice: the stag runs, the hounds pursue, and Runvegr cheers the chase.</p><p>Many Runvegrians insist the song began among Dragoons stationed near contested borders, while others claim it was first sung by fishers in Pagallvolr after an Efra Dorei trade vessel was driven from the Norvbay. Whatever its origin, it spread quickly. Its chorus is simple enough for any drunk to remember, and its howled refrain often turns an entire tavern into a pack of baying hounds.</p><p>The Tesseris officially regard the song as vulgar and unbecoming of sacred imagery, though many sisters privately tolerate it as an expression of Runvegrian unity. In poorer villages, it is less a political statement than a ritual of belonging: cups raised, boots stomping, voices cracking, everyone shouting the parts they know and laughing through the rest.</p><p>In Efra Dorei, the song is despised.</p><p>In Runvegr, that only makes it more popular.</p><hr/><p><strong>🎼 Lyrics</strong></p><p><em>In the sky where the night wind howls,</em></p><p><em>Two fierce hounds begin their prowl,</em></p><p><em>Bran and Slaine, with eyes of fire,</em></p><p><em>Chase the stag of Elvish ire.</em></p><p></p><p><em>Run, run, the hounds draw near (awoooo!)</em></p><p><em>Bran and Slaine, they know no fear.</em></p><p><em>The emerald stag flees the night (so long!)</em></p><p><em>Our Maiden's moons hunt with might!</em></p><p></p><p><em>(Fuck the elves!)</em></p><p></p><p><em>From Erov's gaze, no elf can hide,</em></p><p><em>For Bran and Slaine run side by side,</em></p><p><em>Their fangs are sharp, their pace is swift,</em></p><p><em>Through realms of night, they tear and lift.</em></p><p></p><p><em>Run, run, the hounds draw near, (awoooo!)</em></p><p><em>Bran and Slaine, they know no fear.</em></p><p><em>The emerald stag flees the night, (so long!)</em></p><p><em>Our Maiden's moons hunt with might!</em></p><p></p><p><em>(Fuck the elves! Fuck the elves!)</em></p><p></p><p><em>The elves may dream of forest deep,</em></p><p><em>But Bran and Slaine give no reprieve,</em></p><p><em>Across the sky, through every land,</em></p><p><em>They chase the stag by Erov's hand.</em></p><p></p><p><em>Run, run, the hounds draw near, (awoooo!)</em></p><p><em>Bran and Slaine, they know no fear.</em></p><p><em>The emerald stag flees the night, (so long!)</em></p><p><em>Our Maiden's moons hunt with might!</em></p><p></p><p><em>In taverns warm, with hearts of steel,</em></p><p><em>We sing of moons that never yield,</em></p><p><em>Bran and Slaine, they lead the way,</em></p><p><em>To break the stag at break of day.</em></p><p></p><p><em>So raise your cups and sing with pride,</em></p><p><em>For Bran and Slaine, who never hide,</em></p><p><em>The coward stag, they'll bring to heel,</em></p><p><em>With every turn of winter's wheel.</em></p><p></p><p><em>Run, run, the hounds draw near, (awoooo!)</em></p><p><em>Bran and Slaine, they know no fear.</em></p><p><em>The emerald stag flees the night, (so long!)</em></p><p><em>Our Maiden's moons hunt with might!</em></p><p></p><p><em>(Fuck the elves!)</em></p><p><em>(Fuck the elves!)</em></p><p><em>(Fuck the elves!)</em></p><p><em>(Fuck the elves!)</em></p>","summary":"🗺️ Region: Runvegr 🕯️ Type: Tavern / Drinking Song 📜 Traditionally Sung By: Dragoons, dockworkers, fishers, hunters, caravan guards, off-duty soldiers, and very drunk commonfolk, especially in northern taverns, winter…","sort":1000,"sourceJournal":"The Traveler’s Hymnal"},{"name":"In the Balance","category":"Lore","group":"The Traveler’s Hymnal","type":"text","slug":"in-the-balance","hero":"","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<div><audio controls=\"\"><source src=\"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/music/In%20the%20Balance.mp3\" type=\"audio/mpeg\"/></audio></div><hr/><p><strong>🗺️ Region:</strong> Ushana<br/><strong>🕯️ Type:</strong> Dance Ritual Hymn of Devotion and Passage<br/><strong>📜 Traditionally Sung By:</strong> Temple choirs during dawn and dusk offerings completed with ritual dances.</p><hr/><p><strong>📖 Lore</strong></p><p>This hymn is dedicated to the twin patron deities of the Ushana Dynasty: <strong>Kekha</strong> and <strong>Amheh</strong>, the Keepers of the Living and the Dead.</p><p>It is believed that the hymn must be sung in full, with both verses to Kekha and Amheh, or the blessings of balance will be withheld. The phrase <em>“we pray twinfold”</em> is sacred, often echoed by the chorus in rising, mirrored voices—one half bright, the other low and solemn.</p><hr/><p><strong>🎼 Lyrics</strong></p><p><em>O twin gods bless this land, to us treasure bestow<br/>City of desert sands, water and gold below<br/>Lifeblood and rubies red, precious coins cast aglow<br/>Four hands our fortunes mend, that want we may not know<br/>And when we reach our ends, to scales we gladly go<br/>Our fates are yours to bend, to hells and heavens flow</em></p><p><em>Under arid sky, with silk veils we weave a rainbow<br/>Voices lifted high, dreams upon our backs we carry<br/>When day beckons night (day and night dancing)<br/>As does restless time we never slow<br/>Trusting hand in hand, life death will follow</em></p><p><em>Stoke now nascent flame, brighter burn, dance with souls afire<br/>May ember catch and red-gold spark rise to new heights<br/>May we want for naught coin can buy<br/>Never see wealth’s river run dry<br/>May we find fortune after life<br/>For this we pray, we pray, we pray, we pray twinfold</em></p><p><em>O twin gods bless this land, to us treasure bestow<br/>City of desert sands, water and gold below<br/>Lifeblood and rubies red, precious coins cast aglow<br/>Four hands our fortunes mend, that want we may not know<br/>And when we reach our ends, to scales we gladly go<br/>Our fates are yours to bend, to hells and heavens flow</em></p><p><em>Under arid sky, with silk veils we weave a rainbow<br/>Voices lifted high, dreams upon our backs we carry<br/>When day beckons night (day and night dancing)<br/>As does restless time we never slow<br/>Trusting hand in hand, life death will follow</em></p><p><em>Stoke now kindled flame, hotter burn, sing till breath expires<br/>May those who wander paths in the dark find firelight<br/>May we all as true equals die<br/>Never fear unjust favor's bite<br/>May we be judged by what is right<br/>For this we pray, we pray, we pray, we pray twinfold</em></p><p><em>May we want for naught coin can buy (as true equals die)<br/>Never see wealth’s river run dry (unjust favor's bite)<br/>May we find fortune after life (by what is right)<br/>For this we pray, we pray, we pray, we pray twinfold</em></p>","summary":"🗺️ Region: Ushana 🕯️ Type: Dance Ritual Hymn of Devotion and Passage 📜 Traditionally Sung By: Temple choirs during dawn and dusk offerings completed with ritual dances. 📖 Lore This hymn is dedicated to the twin patron…","sort":2000,"sourceJournal":"The Traveler’s Hymnal"},{"name":"Night of Divergence","category":"Lore","group":"The Traveler’s Hymnal","type":"text","slug":"night-of-divergence","hero":"","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<div><audio controls=\"controls\"><source src=\"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/music/The%20Night%20of%20Divergence.mp3\" type=\"audio/mpeg\"/></audio></div>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>🗺️ Region:</strong> Eilune (Runvegr origin, now sung across the continent)<br/><strong>🕯️ Type:</strong> Epic Lament of Remembrance and Defiance<br/><strong>📜 Traditionally Sung By:</strong> Massed voices at remembrance gatherings, warrior vigils, and great halls on the winter anniversary of the Divergence.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>📖 Lore</strong></p>\n<p><em>The Night of Divergence</em> is not a song whispered, it is roared. In its oldest form, the verses were delivered as a slow dirge, but over centuries the ballad grew into a towering hymn of communal grief and defiance, performed with the force of a hundred voices and the pounding of deep frame drums.The sound is meant to be overwhelming, a living echo of the chaos it recalls.</p>\n<p>Originating in Runvegr, the song recounts the night the sky split, the Ribbon’s wrath swept across the land, and the bonds of the old world were severed forever. It names Pagallvolr’s desolation, the Drekka’s hunger, and the countless heroes who fell beneath a fractured sky.</p>\n<p>The song is as much a vow as it is a memorial. It is said that the ancient words and pounding drums were first used to rally survivors in the aftermath, binding them together in the will to endure. Today, it is performed to remind Eilune that though the Divergence broke the world, the people of the present still carry the fire forward.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>🎼 Lyrics</strong></p>\n<p><em>In the shadows of the evening, when the stars began to wane,</em><br/><em>A whisper filled the air, a chill that brought the pain.</em><br/><em>The sky it split asunder, the heavens cracked and cried,</em><br/><em>On the night of Divergence, when the world was cast aside.</em></p>\n<p><em>Oh, dark night of Divergence, where shadows claimed the day,</em><br/><em>The world was torn asunder as hope was led astray.</em><br/><em>The Ribbon's wrath upon us, in chaos we were lost,</em><br/><em>In the night of Divergence, we paid a heavy cost.</em></p>\n<p><em>The mountains groaned in sorrow, the rivers turned to ice,</em><br/><em>The lands we knew were shattered, beneath the moon's cold light.</em><br/><em>Ancient bonds were broken, the magic ran wild and free,</em><br/><em>On the night of Divergence, we lost our unity.</em></p>\n<p><em>Oh, dark night of Divergence, where shadows claimed the day,</em><br/><em>The world was torn asunder, as hope was led astray.</em><br/><em>The Ribbon's wrath upon us, in chaos we were lost,</em><br/><em>In the night of Divergence, we paid a heavy cost.</em></p>\n<p><em>In Pagallvolr's desolation, the echoes of despair,</em><br/><em>The Drekka's gaping maw, a scar beyond repair.</em><br/><em>Heroes fell to darkness, their light consumed by dread,</em><br/><em>On the night of Divergence, the living mourned the dead.</em></p>\n<p><em>Now we walk in twilight beneath a fractured sky,</em><br/><em>Haunted by the memories of those who said goodbye.</em><br/><em>Their voices in the wind, a mournful, ghostly choir,</em><br/><em>On the night of Divergence, we faced the storm's full ire.</em></p>\n<p><em>Oh, dark night of Divergence, where shadows claimed the day,</em><br/><em>The world was torn asunder as hope was led astray.</em><br/><em>The Ribbon's wrath upon us, in chaos we were lost,</em><br/><em>In the night of Divergence, we paid a heavy cost.</em></p>\n<p><em>So raise a glass to silence and to the ones we've lost,</em><br/><em>In the night of Divergence, we remember what it cost.</em><br/><em>For in the darkest moments, we find a spark of light,</em><br/><em>To guide us through the shadows and bring us through the night.</em></p>\n<p><em>Oh, dark night of Divergence, where shadows claimed the day,</em><br/><em>The world was torn asunder as hope was led astray.</em><br/><em>The Ribbon's wrath upon us, in chaos we were lost,</em><br/><em>In the night of Divergence, the living mourn the dead. </em></p>\n<p> </p>","summary":"🗺️ Region: Eilune (Runvegr origin, now sung across the continent) 🕯️ Type: Epic Lament of Remembrance and Defiance 📜 Traditionally Sung By: Massed voices at remembrance gatherings, warrior vigils, and great halls on the…","sort":3000,"sourceJournal":"The Traveler’s Hymnal"},{"name":"Shadewalker's Lament","category":"Lore","group":"The Traveler’s Hymnal","type":"text","slug":"shadewalker-s-lament","hero":"","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<div><audio controls=\"\"><source src=\"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/music/Shadewalker%27s%20Lament%20(Remastered).mp3\" type=\"audio/mpeg\"/></audio></div><hr/><p><strong>🗺️ Region:</strong> The Outlands<br/><strong>🕯️ Type:</strong> Elegy of Mourning and Remembrance<br/><strong>📜 Traditionally Sung By:</strong> Traveling bards and Shadewalkers in solitude, when mourning those lost to the Ribbon. Sometimes performed as a quiet rite when returning alone from a failed crossing.</p><hr/><p><strong>📖 Lore</strong></p><p>This mournful song, passed quietly among Shadewalkers, tells the tale of an unnamed guide who lost her charges to a violent attack during a Ribbon crossing. Sung quietly by traveling bards, it is often sung quietly with little musical accompaniment.</p><p>Though no record remains of where the crossing occurred, the lyrics reference a glowing lake, indicating the crossing likely began in Shade. The song has no known author, but its verses have remained unchanged for generations. Many believe it is a true story, passed down from one Shadewalker to the next, as a reminder of the risks they bear and the lives they carry.</p><hr/><p><strong>🎼 Lyrics</strong></p><p><em>In the depths of Shade where shadows lie,<br/>A Shadewalker roamed, with watchful eye.<br/>Through the labyrinthine paths she led,<br/>Protecting souls from darkness and dread.</em></p><p><em>Oh, Ribbon winds, so cold and wild,<br/>You took the laughter of a child.<br/>Now silence fills the empty night,<br/>Where once their voices brought delight.</em></p><p><em>Underneath the gleaming lake's soft glow,<br/>She guided them, through light and shadow.<br/>But the Ribbon's wrath, a storm so fierce,<br/>Brought forth a sorrow that time won't pierce.</em></p><p><em>Oh, Ribbon winds, so cold and wild,<br/>You took the laughter of a child.<br/>Now silence fills the empty night,<br/>Where once their voices brought delight.</em></p><p><em>She wanders now with tear-streaked face,<br/>A ghostly wraith in a desolate place.<br/>The memories haunt her every step,<br/>Of the little ones she couldn't protect.</em></p><p><em>Oh, Ribbon winds, so cold and wild,<br/>You took the laughter of a child.<br/>Now silence fills the empty night,<br/>Where once their voices brought delight.</em></p><p><em>In the echo of her mournful song,<br/>The shadows weep for those long gone.<br/>A mother's heart forever torn,<br/>By the Ribbon's rage, her soul was worn.</em></p><p><em>Oh, Ribbon winds, so cold and wild,<br/>You took the laughter of a child.<br/>Now silence fills the empty night,<br/>Where once their voices brought delight.</em></p><p><em>So, in the depths where shadows lie,<br/>A Shadewalker roams, with a tearful sigh.<br/>Her charges lost to the Ribbon's might,<br/>She guards their memory in the night.</em></p>","summary":"🗺️ Region: The Outlands 🕯️ Type: Elegy of Mourning and Remembrance 📜 Traditionally Sung By: Traveling bards and Shadewalkers in solitude, when mourning those lost to the Ribbon. Sometimes performed as a quiet rite when…","sort":4000,"sourceJournal":"The Traveler’s Hymnal"},{"name":"Stone and Snow","category":"Lore","group":"The Traveler’s Hymnal","type":"text","slug":"stone-and-snow","hero":"","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<div><audio controls=\"\"><source src=\"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/music/Stone%20and%20Snow.mp3\" type=\"audio/mpeg\"/></audio></div><hr/><p><strong>🗺️ Region:</strong> Runvegr<br/><strong>🕯️ Type:</strong> Ritual Folk Song of Endurance and Ancestral Memory<br/><strong>📜 Traditionally Sung By:</strong> Tesseris initiates during oath-taking rites, village elders during winter solstice gatherings, and whispered by soldiers on the eve of battle, among many Runvegr natives.</p><hr/><p><strong>📖 Lore</strong></p><p>“Stone and Snow” is a traditional Runvegrian ritual song, older than written record. Its origins are uncertain, but it is often attributed to early settlers who survived the first long winters in the Medalvegr mountain range. The song has since become a cultural touchstone—used in rites of passage, funerals, and moments of collective resolve.</p><p>The lyrics invoke the harshness of the land—stone beneath, snow above—and the solitary nature of survival in Runvegr. Each verse speaks to endurance, sacrifice, and memory. The chorus is often sung in deep, resonant unison, layered with harmonies that seem to echo through the bones of the mountains themselves.</p><p>To many, the phrase <em>“Call the stars to know our name”</em> is not metaphor. It’s believed that the stars remember the names of the lost, and that to sing this song is to ensure those names are not forgotten. When sung during solstice festivals, the entire village may join, lighting torches as the final chorus echoes through the snow-laden streets.</p><hr/><p><strong>🎼 Lyrics</strong></p><p><em>Old is the road where the blood runs thin<br/>Silent the hall where the song begins<br/>Wind through the pines bears the names we lost<br/>Bind them in frost, in flame, in cost</em></p><p><em>Stone and snow, we walk alone<br/>Shadow-bound and far from home<br/>Breathe the oath, and light the flame<br/>Call the stars to know our name</em></p><p><em>Brands on the skin, and fire in the breath<br/>We dance with fate, we drink with death<br/>Words unspoken, yet understood<br/>In root and ash, in bone and wood</em></p><p><em>Stone and snow, we walk alone<br/>Shadow-bound and far from home<br/>Breathe the oath, and light the flame<br/>Call the stars to know our name</em></p><p><em>Echoes in the black of stone<br/>Hands that reach but find no home<br/>If I fall, remember me<br/>By the mountain, by the sea</em></p><p><em>Stone and snow, we walk alone<br/>Shadow-bound and far from home<br/>Breathe the oath, and light the flame<br/>Call the stars to know our name</em></p>","summary":"🗺️ Region: Runvegr 🕯️ Type: Ritual Folk Song of Endurance and Ancestral Memory 📜 Traditionally Sung By: Tesseris initiates during oath-taking rites, village elders during winter solstice gatherings, and whispered by…","sort":5000,"sourceJournal":"The Traveler’s Hymnal"},{"name":"Where the Frost Roads Go","category":"Lore","group":"The Traveler’s Hymnal","type":"text","slug":"where-the-frost-roads-go","hero":"","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<div><audio controls=\"controls\"><source src=\"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/music/Where%20The%20Frost%20Roads%20Go.mp3\" type=\"audio/mpeg\"/></audio></div>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>🗺️ Region:</strong> Runvegr<br/><strong>🕯️ Type:</strong> Folk Marching Song of Kinship and Resilience<br/><strong>📜 Traditionally Sung By:</strong> Caravaners, pilgrims, and mountain guides traversing the ley-bound paths across Runvegr—especially during the final leg of long journeys.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>📖 Lore</strong></p>\n<p>This rustic but reverent folk song is often heard echoing through Runvegr’s highland passes and ley-touched crags. Known for its brisk tempo and communal refrain, “Where the Frost Roads Go” is passed down by those who live and die on the move—guides, wanderers, Tesseris envoys, and families who brave the wilds together.</p>\n<p>The phrase <em>“frost roads”</em> refers to ancient ley-lines that twist invisibly through the land, marking old pilgrim paths and Tesseris routes. They are said to shimmer under moonlight, though few claim to have seen them. The song speaks to hardship, camaraderie, and the strange comfort of knowing your steps join countless others from generations before.</p>\n<p>Some say the chorus is echoed not just by travelers, but by the land itself—that voices long gone whisper along the ley-lines to those who still carry the fire. To sing it is to remember that even in solitude, you walk with those who came before.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>🎼 Lyrics</strong></p>\n<p><em>Boots in the drift, sky turning red<br/>Carry the fire, the words we said<br/>Sling the pack, the song, the steel<br/>Leave behind what time can’t heal</em></p>\n<p><em>Hey-la, hey-lo, the wind won’t wait<br/>Stone knows hunger, snow bears weight</em></p>\n<p><em>Where the frost roads go, we follow<br/>Over crag and through the hollow<br/>Echoed steps on ice and bone<br/>We are never quite alone</em></p>\n<p><em>Eyes on the ridge, heart in the hand<br/>Singing the name of the waking land<br/>Feel the pull where the ley-lines hum<br/>Not all who run are meant to run</em></p>\n<p><em>Hey-la, hey-lo, the cold won’t bend<br/>But we are fire, we are end</em></p>\n<p><em>Where the frost roads go, we follow<br/>Over crag and through the hollow<br/>Echoed steps on ice and bone<br/>We are never quite alone</em></p>\n<p><em>Hands to the stone, to the sky, to the flame<br/>Carry the story, carry the name<br/>Forward we go, with ash in our breath<br/>Chasing the sun, and outpacing death</em></p>\n<p><em>Where the frost roads go, we follow<br/>Bright with hope and dark with shadow<br/>Echoed steps on ice and bone<br/>We are never quite alone</em></p>","summary":"🗺️ Region: Runvegr 🕯️ Type: Folk Marching Song of Kinship and Resilience 📜 Traditionally Sung By: Caravaners, pilgrims, and mountain guides traversing the ley-bound paths across Runvegr—especially during the final leg…","sort":6000,"sourceJournal":"The Traveler’s Hymnal"},{"name":"Without You","category":"Lore","group":"The Traveler’s Hymnal","type":"text","slug":"without-you","hero":"","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<div><audio controls=\"controls\"><source src=\"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/music/Without%20You%20(Remastered).mp3\" type=\"audio/mpeg\"/></audio></div>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>🗺️ Region:</strong> Runvegr<br/><strong>🕯️ Type:</strong> Folk Ballad of Grief and Devotion<br/><strong>📜 Traditionally Sung By:</strong> Tavern singers, festival performers, and grieving Tesseris mages—often late into the night, when the fire has dimmed and the past feels near.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>📖 Lore</strong></p>\n<p>“Without You” is a mournful ballad said to have originated with a Tesseris mage who lost her beloved—a Dragoon slain during a clash with the Wild Hunt near the Grarfold Mounts. Though the original author remains anonymous, the song spread quickly across Runvegr, finding its way into both rural taverns and city festivals.</p>\n<p>Its melody is simple and haunting, sung slowly and with aching sincerity. The refrain, <em>“Your armor gleamed in the twilight...”</em> is often joined by others in the room, especially among Dragoons, who are known to weep openly during its final verse.</p>\n<p>It’s said that if the song is sung alone beneath a blood moon, the ghost of the fallen Dragoon may appear beside the singer, though whether in comfort or sorrow, no one knows. The Tesseris, who rarely speak of such superstitions, do not discourage this belief.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>🎼 Lyrics</strong></p>\n<p><em>In the silence of the evening, where shadows whisper low,<br/>I hear the echoes of your laughter in the places we used to go.<br/>The wind carries your name softly through the fields where we once roamed,<br/>Now I walk alone, with memories of you, in a world so cold.</em></p>\n<p><em>Your armor gleamed in the twilight, a dragoon’s pride, so fierce and true,<br/>But the battle called, and took you away, leaving me without you.</em></p>\n<p><em>The stars above seem dimmer now without your guiding light,<br/>I trace the constellations, wishing you were here tonight.<br/>The moon casts a silver glow on the path we used to tread,<br/>Now I linger in the stillness with the tears I’ve yet to shed.</em></p>\n<p><em>Your armor gleamed in the twilight, a dragoon’s pride, so fierce and true,<br/>But the battle called, and took you away, leaving me without you.</em></p>\n<p><em>I remember the vows we whispered beneath the ancient tree,<br/>The promises of forever now lost in history.<br/>Your voice a distant murmur in the breeze that passes by,<br/>I reach for you in dreams but wake to an empty sky.</em></p>\n<p><em>The fields where we danced are barren, the flowers wilt and fade,<br/>I wander through the memories in the places we once stayed.<br/>Your touch, a phantom feeling, that lingers on my skin,<br/>A love that burned so brightly now a whisper in the wind.</em></p>\n<p><em>Your armor gleamed in the twilight, a dragoon’s pride, so fierce and true,<br/>But the battle called, and took you away, leaving me without you.</em></p>\n<p><em>In the quiet of the night where the world fades to grey,<br/>I hold on to the pieces of a love that slipped away.<br/>Your spirit walks beside me in the shadows of the dawn,<br/>A dragoon’s heart, forever mine, though your body’s gone.</em></p>\n<p><em>Your armor gleamed in the twilight, a dragoon’s pride, so fierce and true,<br/>But the battle called, and took you away, leaving me without you.</em></p>","summary":"🗺️ Region: Runvegr 🕯️ Type: Folk Ballad of Grief and Devotion 📜 Traditionally Sung By: Tavern singers, festival performers, and grieving Tesseris mages—often late into the night, when the fire has dimmed and the past…","sort":7000,"sourceJournal":"The Traveler’s Hymnal"},{"name":"The Acolyte","category":"Lore","group":"Alliants","type":"text","slug":"the-acolyte","hero":"assets/Alliant-Runa.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table><tbody><tr><td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Alliant-Runa.webp\"/></td><td><p><strong>Name: </strong>Runa Vilhjalmsdottir</p><p><strong>Title: </strong>Tesseris White Mage</p><p><strong>Race: </strong>Hyur</p><p><strong>Age: </strong>Early 20s</p><p></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><span><strong>\"I want to help people. Not just command them, or silence them, or — I want to heal them.\"</strong></span></p></td></tr></tbody></table>","summary":"Name: Runa Vilhjalmsdottir Title: Tesseris White Mage Race: Hyur Age: Early 20s \"I want to help people. Not just command them, or silence them, or — I want to heal them.\"","sort":0,"sourceJournal":"Alliants"},{"name":"The Empress","category":"Characters","group":"Major Players","type":"text","slug":"the-empress","hero":"assets/Players-EmpressEira.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table><tbody><tr><td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Players-EmpressEira.webp\"/></td><td><p><strong>Name: </strong>Eira Thrymsdottir</p><p><strong>Title: </strong>Empress of Runvegr</p><p><strong>Race: </strong>Hyur</p><p><strong>Age: </strong>Mid-30s</p><p></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><span><strong>\"In the heart of winter's fury, we find our strength.\"</strong></span></p><p><strong>Appearance:</strong></p><p>Eira is a striking figure, tall and commanding with long, silver hair that flows like a waterfall of moonlight, often adorned with intricate braids and silver ornaments. Her eyes are a piercing ice-blue, reflecting both the harsh winters of her land and the depth of her wisdom. Her skin is fair, with a slight hint of the cold, and she carries herself with a regal bearing that exudes authority and grace. She is usually seen wearing elegant, fur-lined robes and a crown crafted from Brightglass, glowing faintly in the dark.</p><p><strong>Background:</strong></p><p>Eira was born into the royal family of Runvegr, a direct descendant of the revered warrior queen Brynhildr. From a young age, she was trained in the ways of leadership, combat, and the intricate politics of her realm. Her childhood was marked by rigorous training and education, preparing her for the burdens and responsibilities of the throne.</p><p><strong>Personality:</strong></p><p>Eira is known for her wisdom, compassion, and unyielding determination. She is deeply connected to her people and values their well-being above all else. Her rule is marked by fairness, and she often seeks counsel from the Tesseris and other advisors to ensure she makes balanced decisions. She is a strategic thinker, able to navigate the complex political landscape of Runvegr with skill and finesse.</p><p><strong>Personal Life:</strong></p><p>Eira is a widow, having lost her husband, a valiant Dragoon, to a fierce battle against the Wild Hunt. She has one daughter, Sigrid, who is being groomed to one day take over the throne. Eira's relationship with her daughter is a mix of stern discipline and deep affection, ensuring that Sigrid is well-prepared for the responsibilities of leadership.</p><p><strong>Emblem:</strong></p><p>The emblem of Eira's reign is a silver wolf howling at a crescent moon, symbolizing both her fierce protection of her people and her connection to the moon goddess, Erov.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>","summary":"Name: Eira Thrymsdottir Title: Empress of Runvegr Race: Hyur Age: Mid-30s \"In the heart of winter's fury, we find our strength.\" Appearance: Eira is a striking figure, tall and commanding with long, silver hair that…","sort":0,"sourceJournal":"Major Players"},{"name":"The Most High","category":"Characters","group":"Major Players","type":"text","slug":"the-most-high","hero":"assets/Players-MostHighAlarice.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Players-MostHighAlarice.webp\"/></td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Name:</strong> Alarice Thrandulsdottir</p>\n<p><strong>Title: </strong>Most High of the Tesseris</p>\n<p><strong>Race: </strong>Hyur</p>\n<p><strong>Age: </strong>Mid-50s</p>\n<p> </p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span><strong>\"Defy the Tesseris, and you will learn that even the coldest winter is a gentle caress compared to my wrath.\"</strong></span></p>\n<p><strong>Appearance:</strong></p>\n<p>Alarice is an imposing figure with a commanding presence, standing tall with a muscular build. Her hair is a dark, stormy gray, often kept in an intricate braid adorned with silver runes. Her eyes are a deep, penetrating green, reflecting both the power and wisdom she wields. Her face is lined with the marks of age and experience, yet she exudes a sense of vitality and strength. She is usually clad in the ceremonial garb of the Tesseris, which includes a dark, flowing cloak adorned with intricate silver runes and a staff made of ancient, twisted wood with a Brightglass core.</p>\n<p><strong>Background:</strong></p>\n<p>Born into a prominent family whose women were all members of the Tesseris, Alarice showed great promise from an early age. Her affinity for vril and her exceptional strategic mind set her apart from her peers. She quickly rose through the ranks, proving herself in both magical prowess and council. Alarice was one of the few mages who showed great skills in multiple shades of magic, ultimately choosing to take the black. Alarice's dedication to the Tesseris and her unwavering sense of duty eventually led to her appointment as the Most High, a position she has held for the past two decades. As the Most High, Alarice is served by her Left and Right Hands.</p>\n<p><strong>Personality:</strong></p>\n<p>Alarice is known for her stern and disciplined demeanor. She is a woman of few words, but when she speaks, her words carry great weight. She is highly intelligent and strategic, often thinking several steps ahead. Alarice is also deeply compassionate, though she rarely shows it openly, believing that a leader must remain strong and composed. Her leadership style is one of respect and trust, but she is not above manipulation to ensure the Tesseris remain in power.</p>\n<p><strong>Personal Life:</strong></p>\n<p>Alarice is a widow, having lost her wife many years ago to a Sorrow Storm. She has two daughters, both of whom are rising stars within the Tesseris. Despite her demanding role, Alarice is a dedicated mother and ensures her daughters receive the training and guidance they need to succeed.</p>\n<p><strong>Emblem:</strong></p>\n<p>The emblem of Alarice's leadership is a silver wolf entwined with vril threads, symbolizing the strength and unity of the Tesseris under her guidance.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","summary":"Name: Alarice Thrandulsdottir Title: Most High of the Tesseris Race: Hyur Age: Mid-50s \"Defy the Tesseris, and you will learn that even the coldest winter is a gentle caress compared to my wrath.\" Appearance: Alarice is…","sort":1000,"sourceJournal":"Major Players"},{"name":"The Right Hand","category":"Characters","group":"Major Players","type":"text","slug":"the-right-hand","hero":"assets/Players-RightHand.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Players-RightHand.webp\"/></td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Name:</strong> Astrid Skarsdottir</p>\n<p><strong>Title: </strong>The Right Hand of Most High</p>\n<p><strong>Race: </strong>Hyur</p>\n<p><strong>Age: </strong>Late-30s</p>\n<p> </p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<p><span><strong>\"Loyalty to the Tesseris is loyalty to our future; we stand united, or we fall divided.\"</strong></span></p>\n<p><strong>Appearance:</strong></p>\n<p>Astrid is an imposing and formidable figure, standing tall with a lean, muscular build honed from years of rigorous training and battle. She has long, auburn hair, often tied back in a practical yet elegant braid that keeps it out of her face during combat. Her eyes are a striking shade of amber, burning with intensity and determination. Astrid's fair skin is marked with a few scars, each a testament to her many battles. She wears the traditional garb of a Red Mage, a blend of practical combat gear and intricate scarlet robes, adorned with symbols of her rank and prowess.</p>\n<p><strong>Background:</strong></p>\n<p>Born into a prestigious family with a storied history in the Tesseris, Astrid was destined for greatness from a young age. She showed an early aptitude for both martial and magical disciplines, excelling in the unique blend of combat and spellcasting that defines Red Magic. Her rise through the ranks was marked by her exceptional skill and unwavering dedication to the Tesseris. She has served in numerous campaigns beyond the empire's borders, earning a fearsome reputation. Her loyalty and effectiveness eventually earned her the position of Right Hand to the Most High, Alarice Thrandulsdottir.</p>\n<p><strong>Personality:</strong></p>\n<p>Astrid is known for her fierce loyalty and uncompromising determination. She is a natural leader, with a commanding presence that inspires both fear and respect. Her leadership style is direct and assertive, demanding excellence from those she commands. Despite her tough exterior, Astrid is deeply loyal to the Tesseris and the Most High, willing to go to great lengths to protect and serve her order. She is strategic and pragmatic, valuing results and efficiency above all else.</p>\n<p><strong>Personal Life:</strong></p>\n<p>Astrid is single, having dedicated her life to her duties and the Tesseris. Her focus on her role leaves little time for personal relationships, but she is deeply connected to her comrades, viewing them as her family. She mentors several young Red Mages, taking a personal interest in their development and success.</p>\n<p><strong>Emblem:</strong></p>\n<p>The emblem of Astrid's position is a red phoenix entwined with a sword, symbolizing her mastery of Red Magic, her fierce spirit, and her role as the enforcer of the Most High's will.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","summary":"Name: Astrid Skarsdottir Title: The Right Hand of Most High Race: Hyur Age: Late-30s \"Loyalty to the Tesseris is loyalty to our future; we stand united, or we fall divided.\" Appearance: Astrid is an imposing and…","sort":2000,"sourceJournal":"Major Players"},{"name":"The Left Hand","category":"Characters","group":"Major Players","type":"text","slug":"the-left-hand","hero":"assets/Players-LeftHand.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Players-LeftHand.webp\"/></td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Name:</strong> Morgana Elfridsdottir</p>\n<p><strong>Title: </strong>The Left Hand of Most High</p>\n<p><strong>Race: </strong>Hyur</p>\n<p><strong>Age: </strong>Early-30s</p>\n<p> </p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","summary":"Name: Morgana Elfridsdottir Title: The Left Hand of Most High Race: Hyur Age: Early-30s","sort":3000,"sourceJournal":"Major Players"},{"name":"The First Elder","category":"Characters","group":"Major Players","type":"text","slug":"the-first-elder","hero":"assets/Players-ElderBrynjar.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table><tbody><tr><td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Players-ElderBrynjar.webp\"/></td><td><p><strong>Name:</strong> Brynjar Haldorsson</p><p><strong>Title: </strong>First Elder of the Dragoons</p><p><strong>Race: </strong>Hyur</p><p><strong>Age: </strong>Early-60s</p><p></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><span><strong>\"Strength and honor are the pillars upon which we stand; without them, we are nothing.\"</strong></span></p><p><strong>Appearance:</strong></p><p>Elder Brynjar is a formidable and imposing figure, standing tall with a broad, muscular build that speaks of a lifetime of rigorous training and combat. His hair is a stark white, worn long and tied back, with a well-trimmed beard that adds to his authoritative presence. His eyes are a piercing blue, sharp and watchful, always assessing the surroundings. His weathered face is marked with scars, each telling a story of battles fought and won. He is often seen wearing the traditional Dragoon armor, a mix of practical leather and shining steel, adorned with the insignia of his order.</p><p><strong>Background:</strong></p><p>Brynjar was born into a family with a long history of serving in the Dragoons. From a young age, he was trained in the ways of combat, discipline, and leadership. His prowess on the battlefield and his strategic mind quickly set him apart from his peers. Over the years, he rose through the ranks, earning respect and admiration from his fellow Dragoons. His appointment as an Elder came after a particularly fierce battle where his leadership was instrumental in securing victory against overwhelming odds.</p><p><strong>Personality:</strong></p><p>Brynjar is known for his stoic and stern demeanor. He is a man of few words, preferring to let his actions speak for him. His leadership style is firm but fair, and he demands the best from those under his command. Despite his tough exterior, he cares deeply for his comrades and would go to great lengths to ensure their safety and success. He is highly disciplined and expects the same from others, believing that order and discipline are the cornerstones of a strong fighting force.</p><p><strong>Personal Life:</strong></p><p>Brynjar is a widower, having lost his wife many years ago to illness. He has one son, Leif, who is also a member of the Dragoons and is being trained under Brynjar's watchful eye. Despite his demanding role, Brynjar is a dedicated father, ensuring that Leif is well-prepared for the responsibilities and challenges of being a Dragoon.</p><p><strong>Emblem:</strong></p><p>The emblem of Brynjar's leadership is a silver dragon entwined with a sword, symbolizing the strength and honor of the Dragoons under his guidance.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>","summary":"Name: Brynjar Haldorsson Title: First Elder of the Dragoons Race: Hyur Age: Early-60s \"Strength and honor are the pillars upon which we stand; without them, we are nothing.\" Appearance: Elder Brynjar is a formidable and…","sort":4000,"sourceJournal":"Major Players"},{"name":"The Second Elder","category":"Characters","group":"Major Players","type":"text","slug":"the-second-elder","hero":"assets/Players-ElderThalric.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table><tbody><tr><td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Players-ElderThalric.webp\"/></td><td><p><strong>Name:</strong> Thalric Windstrider</p><p><strong>Title: </strong>Second Elder of the Dragoons</p><p><strong>Race: </strong>Air Genasi</p><p><strong>Age: </strong>Late-40s</p><p></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><span><strong>\"True strength lies not in rigidity, but in the ability to bend and change with the currents of life.\"</strong></span></p><p><strong>Appearance:</strong></p><p>Elder Thalric is a striking figure, his Air Genasi heritage evident in his ethereal appearance. He has light blue skin with a faint, swirling pattern that seems to shift with the breeze. His hair is a silvery-white, always gently billowing as if caught in an unseen wind. His eyes are a clear, sky blue, filled with a calm and focused intensity. Thalric's build is lean and athletic, with an agility that reflects his elemental nature. He often wears the traditional Dragoon armor, modified to allow for greater mobility, and his cloak is adorned with feathers and light materials that catch the wind.</p><p><strong>Background:</strong></p><p>Thalric was born to a nomadic tribe of Air Genasi, known for their deep connection to the winds and skies. His tribe frequently interacted with the Dragoons, and from a young age, Thalric was fascinated by their discipline and combat prowess. He joined the Dragoons as soon as he was able, quickly rising through the ranks due to his natural agility and keen strategic mind. His unique abilities as an Air Genasi and his dedication to the order led to his appointment as an Elder, where he has served with distinction.</p><p><strong>Personality:</strong></p><p>Thalric is known for his calm and composed demeanor. He is thoughtful and introspective, often contemplating the larger picture before making decisions. His leadership style is one of quiet confidence, inspiring those around him through his unwavering dedication and insight. Thalric is deeply connected to nature and the elements, often seeking solitude in high places to meditate and gain clarity. He values freedom and flexibility, both in thought and action, and encourages his comrades to think creatively in their approaches.</p><p><strong>Personal Life:</strong></p><p>Thalric is unmarried and has no children, dedicating his life to the Dragoons and his connection to the elements. He finds solace in nature, often retreating to high places to meditate and gain perspective. Thalric mentors several young Dragoons, imparting his wisdom and encouraging them to embrace their unique strengths.</p><p><strong>Emblem:</strong></p><p>The emblem of Thalric's leadership is a silver eagle with outstretched wings, surrounded by swirling winds, symbolizing freedom, vision, and the power of the air.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>","summary":"Name: Thalric Windstrider Title: Second Elder of the Dragoons Race: Air Genasi Age: Late-40s \"True strength lies not in rigidity, but in the ability to bend and change with the currents of life.\" Appearance: Elder…","sort":5000,"sourceJournal":"Major Players"},{"name":"The Third Elder","category":"Characters","group":"Major Players","type":"text","slug":"the-third-elder","hero":"assets/Players-ElderVarian.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Players-ElderVarian.webp\"/></td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Name:</strong> Varian Stormcloak</p>\n<p><strong>Title:</strong> Third Elder of the Dragoons</p>\n<p><strong>Race:</strong> Hyur</p>\n<p><strong>Age:</strong> Late-20s</p>\n<p> </p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","summary":"Name: Varian Stormcloak Title: Third Elder of the Dragoons Race: Hyur Age: Late-20s","sort":6000,"sourceJournal":"Major Players"},{"name":"The Fourth Elder","category":"Characters","group":"Major Players","type":"text","slug":"the-fourth-elder","hero":"assets/Players-ElderHrothgar.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Players-ElderHrothgar.webp\"/></td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Name:</strong> Hrothgar Thulgarsson</p>\n<p><strong>Title:</strong> Fourth Elder of the Dragoons</p>\n<p><strong>Race:</strong> Half-Orc</p>\n<p><strong>Age:</strong> Early-40s</p>\n<p> </p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","summary":"Name: Hrothgar Thulgarsson Title: Fourth Elder of the Dragoons Race: Half-Orc Age: Early-40s","sort":7000,"sourceJournal":"Major Players"},{"name":"The Fifth Elder","category":"Characters","group":"Major Players","type":"text","slug":"the-fifth-elder","hero":"assets/Players-ElderRagnar.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table><tbody><tr><td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Players-ElderRagnar.webp\"/></td><td><p><strong>Name:</strong> Ragnar Valtason</p><p><strong>Title:</strong> Fifth Elder of the Dragoons</p><p><strong>Race:</strong> Hyur</p><p><strong>Age:</strong> Early-30s</p><p></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><span><strong>\"Those who underestimate the power of influence are destined to be led.\"</strong></span></p><p><strong>Appearance:</strong></p><p>Elder Ragnar is a striking and charismatic figure, with a presence that commands attention and respect. He has long, fiery red hair that he often wears in a loose, flowing style or in a warrior's braid. His eyes are a vivid emerald green, full of intensity and cunning. His fair skin is marked with a few battle scars, each a testament to his experience and resilience. Ragnar's build is athletic and agile, with a grace that belies his strength. He wears the traditional Dragoon armor, customized with intricate designs that reflect his personal style and status within the order.</p><p><strong>Background:</strong></p><p>Ragnar was born into a noble family with a long history of service to Runvegr. From a young age, he showed exceptional skill in combat and a keen strategic mind. His family’s influence helped him gain entry into the Dragoons, but it was his own abilities and determination that propelled him through the ranks. Ragnar's rise to the position of Elder was marked by his leadership in several key battles, where his tactics and bravery earned him widespread recognition and respect. His charisma and ability to influence others played a significant role in his rapid ascent.</p><p><strong>Personality:</strong></p><p>Ragnar is known for his charismatic and manipulative nature. He is a master of persuasion, able to inspire loyalty and devotion in those around him while subtly manipulating situations to his advantage. His leadership style is dynamic and inspirational, often motivating those around him to push beyond their limits. Ragnar values honor and integrity above all else and expects the same from those he leads. While he can be intense and demanding, he also shows a deep compassion and commitment to the well-being of his comrades.</p><p><strong>Personal Life:</strong></p><p>Ragnar is married to a fellow Dragoon, a man named Erik, who shares his dedication to the order. They have one adopted son, Bjorn, who is training to follow in their footsteps. Ragnar’s family is his anchor, providing him with strength and motivation. He is also a mentor to several young Dragoons, taking a personal interest in their development and success.</p><p><strong>Emblem:</strong></p><p>The emblem of Ragnar’s leadership is a red dragon entwined with a flaming sword, symbolizing his fiery spirit, courage, and the honor he upholds within the Dragoons.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>","summary":"Name: Ragnar Valtason Title: Fifth Elder of the Dragoons Race: Hyur Age: Early-30s \"Those who underestimate the power of influence are destined to be led.\" Appearance: Elder Ragnar is a striking and charismatic figure,…","sort":8000,"sourceJournal":"Major Players"},{"name":"The Sultana","category":"Characters","group":"Major Players","type":"text","slug":"the-sultana","hero":"assets/Players-SultanaNyla.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table><tbody><tr><td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Players-SultanaNyla.webp\"/></td><td><p><strong>Name: </strong>Nyla Aramvek</p><p><strong>Title: </strong>Sultana of Ushana</p><p><strong>Race: </strong>Earth Genasi</p><p><strong>Age: </strong>Early-30s</p><p></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><span><strong>\"A powerful ruler must be as unyielding as the desert sun and as adaptable as the shifting sands.\"</strong></span></p><p><strong>Appearance:</strong></p><p>Sultana Nyla is an enchanting figure, radiating an aura of regal elegance and authority. As an Earth Genasi, her skin has a slight metallic sheen, resembling polished bronze, and her hair, a rich, dark brown, has subtle streaks of shimmering gold. Her eyes are a striking amber, with a faint inner glow that reflects her elemental nature. Her features are finely chiseled, giving her an almost statuesque appearance. She carries herself with a graceful poise, often wearing luxurious, flowing robes in vibrant colors, embroidered with intricate patterns and adorned with jewelry that reflects her status. A distinctive mark of her reign is the golden diadem she wears, set with a large, flawless ruby.</p><p><strong>Background:</strong></p><p>Born into the royal family of Ushana, Nyla was groomed from a young age to assume the mantle of leadership. Her Earth Genasi heritage is a symbol of strength and resilience among her people. She received an extensive education in politics, economics, and the arts of diplomacy and statecraft. Her ascension to the throne came after the sudden death of her father, the previous Sultan, and she has attempted to rule Ushana with determination ever since.</p><p><strong>Personality:</strong></p><p>Nyla is known for her charisma, intelligence, and diplomatic prowess. She is a natural leader, able to inspire loyalty and respect from her subjects and allies. Beneath her charming exterior lies a shrewd and strategic mind, capable of navigating the complex political landscape of Ushana and beyond. While she is compassionate and cares deeply for her people, she is also capable of being ruthless when necessary to protect her kingdom and maintain her power.</p><p><strong>Personal Life:</strong></p><p>Nyla is married to Prince Kasim, a skilled diplomat and advisor who supports her in her rule. They have one young daughter, Princess Layla, who is being raised to understand the responsibilities and privileges of their royal lineage. Nyla's family is her greatest source of strength and motivation.</p><p><strong>Emblem:</strong></p><p>The emblem of Nyla's reign is a golden falcon with outstretched wings, clutching a pair of scales in its talons, symbolizing both justice and the balance of trade that sustains Ushana's prosperity.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>","summary":"Name: Nyla Aramvek Title: Sultana of Ushana Race: Earth Genasi Age: Early-30s \"A powerful ruler must be as unyielding as the desert sun and as adaptable as the shifting sands.\" Appearance: Sultana Nyla is an enchanting…","sort":9000,"sourceJournal":"Major Players"},{"name":"The Regent","category":"Characters","group":"Major Players","type":"text","slug":"the-regent","hero":"assets/Players-RegentSeraphine.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table><tbody><tr><td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Players-RegentSeraphine.webp\"/></td><td><p><span><strong>Name: </strong>Seraphine Nereidal</span></p><p><span><strong>Title: </strong>Regent of Westernesse</span></p><p><span><strong>Race: </strong>Water Genasi</span></p><p><span><strong>Age: </strong>Mid-40s</span></p><p></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><span><strong>\"In the stillness of the water, we find clarity and strength.\"</strong></span></p><p><strong>Appearance:</strong></p><p>Regent Seraphine is an ethereal and graceful figure, embodying the fluid elegance of her Water Genasi heritage. Her skin has a dark blue tint, with a shimmering quality that resembles the surface of a tranquil sea. Her hair flows like liquid silver, often styled in intricate waves and adorned with delicate aquatic-themed accessories. Her eyes are a deep, oceanic blue, filled with a calm and wise intensity. Seraphine's attire is both regal and practical, designed to allow freedom of movement while reflecting her high status, often featuring shades of blue and silver with intricate embroidery.</p><p><strong>Background:</strong></p><p>Born into a prominent family in Easternesse, Seraphine was groomed from a young age for leadership. Her Water Genasi heritage marked her as special, and she received extensive training in diplomacy, governance, and the magical arts. When the Sultana decided to rebuild her influence in Westernesse, Seraphine was appointed as the new Regent, tasked with ruling in the Sultana's stead. Her wisdom, grace, and diplomatic skills have made her a respected and effective leader in Westernesse, bridging the cultural and political differences between the two regions.</p><p><strong>Personality:</strong></p><p>Seraphine is known for her calm and composed demeanor. She is a patient and empathetic leader, able to navigate complex political landscapes with ease. Her leadership style is inclusive and diplomatic, valuing the input and perspectives of those around her. Despite her gentle exterior, Seraphine is firm and decisive when necessary, unafraid to make difficult decisions to protect and advance the interests of Westernesse and the Sultana's rule.</p><p><strong>Personal Life:</strong></p><p>Seraphine is married to a prominent scholar and mage, Callum, who supports her in her duties and shares her dedication to the well-being of Westernesse. They have two children, twins named Marina and Caspian, who are being groomed for leadership roles. Seraphine's family is her anchor, providing her with strength and motivation. She is also a mentor to several young Water Genasi, guiding them in the use of their abilities and the responsibilities of leadership.</p><p><strong>Emblem:</strong></p><p>The emblem of Nyla's reign is a golden falcon with outstretched wings, clutching a pair of scales in its talons, symbolizing both justice and the balance of trade that sustains Ushana's prosperity.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>","summary":"Name: Seraphine Nereidal Title: Regent of Westernesse Race: Water Genasi Age: Mid-40s \"In the stillness of the water, we find clarity and strength.\" Appearance: Regent Seraphine is an ethereal and graceful figure,…","sort":10000,"sourceJournal":"Major Players"},{"name":"The Secessionist","category":"Characters","group":"Major Players","type":"text","slug":"the-secessionist","hero":"assets/Players-RegentTorvald.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table><tbody><tr><td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Players-RegentTorvald.webp\"/></td><td><p><span><strong>Name: </strong>Torvald Kaltsson</span></p><p><span><strong>Title: </strong>Regent of Bern</span></p><p><span><strong>Race: </strong>Hyur</span></p><p><span><strong>Age: </strong>Late-30s</span></p><p></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><span><strong>\"Independence is our right, and I will not rest until Bern stands tall and unbowed.\"</strong></span></p><p><strong>Appearance:</strong></p><p>Regent Torvald is a towering and robust figure, his presence commanding and intimidating. He has rugged, sun-kissed skin, with a broad, muscular build that reflects his hands-on approach to leadership. His hair is a wild mane of dark brown, often tousled and unkempt, and his eyes are a piercing blue, filled with determination and fervor. Torvald's face is marked with a few battle scars, each a testament to his fierce nature and history of conflict. He typically wears practical, sturdy clothing suited for both governance and combat, adorned with symbols of Bern's independence and strength.</p><p><strong>Background:</strong></p><p>Torvald was born and raised in Bern, a city known for its rugged independence and resourcefulness. His family has deep roots in the city, with a history of leadership and defiance against external control. From a young age, Torvald was taught the value of self-reliance and the importance of standing up for one's beliefs. He quickly rose to prominence in Bern, his brash and fearless nature earning him both respect and controversy. His eagerness to see Bern secede from Ushana and chart its own course led to his appointment as Regent, where he now works tirelessly to achieve his vision of independence.</p><p><strong>Personality:</strong></p><p>Torvald is known for his brash and outspoken demeanor. He is a passionate and fiery leader, unafraid to challenge authority and push for what he believes is best for Bern. His leadership style is direct and forceful, often rallying his followers with stirring speeches and bold actions. Torvald values independence and self-determination above all else, believing that Bern should control its own destiny without interference from Easternesse or Westernesse. While his approach can be divisive, he is deeply committed to the welfare of his city and its people.</p><p><strong>Personal Life:</strong></p><p>Torvald is unmarried, dedicating his life to his cause and the welfare of Bern. His personal relationships are often secondary to his political ambitions, though he maintains a close circle of loyal advisors and comrades. He is deeply connected to his family and the history of Bern, drawing strength and inspiration from their legacy of resilience and independence.</p><p><strong>Emblem:</strong></p><p>The emblem of Torvald's regency is a fierce bear standing on its hind legs, roaring, symbolizing Bern's strength, independence, and determination to stand on its own.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>","summary":"Name: Torvald Kaltsson Title: Regent of Bern Race: Hyur Age: Late-30s \"Independence is our right, and I will not rest until Bern stands tall and unbowed.\" Appearance: Regent Torvald is a towering and robust figure, his…","sort":11000,"sourceJournal":"Major Players"},{"name":"The Councilor","category":"Characters","group":"Major Players","type":"text","slug":"the-councilor","hero":"assets/Players-CouncilorMaren.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table><tbody><tr><td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Players-CouncilorMaren.webp\"/></td><td><p><span><strong>Name: </strong>Maren Leifdottir</span></p><p><span><strong>Title: </strong>Councilor of Altar</span></p><p><span><strong>Race: </strong>Tiefling</span></p><p><span><strong>Age: </strong>Late-40s</span></p><p></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><span><strong>\"Our city's independence is our greatest asset; we must protect it with wisdom, courage, and unity.\"</strong></span></p><p><strong>Appearance:</strong></p><p>Councilor Maren is a commanding and striking figure, her Tiefling heritage giving her an otherworldly presence. Her skin is a deep crimson, with a smooth, almost metallic sheen that reflects the light. She has long, black hair that cascades down her back in waves, often partially pulled back to keep it out of her face. Her eyes are a piercing gold, glowing faintly in the dark, adding to her intimidating yet captivating appearance. Small, curved horns protrude from her forehead, and her tail, often wrapped around her waist or legs, moves with a mind of its own. Maren's attire is both practical and subtly elegant, featuring durable fabrics suitable for the harsh environment, adorned with symbols of her office and the city of Altar.</p><p><strong>Background:</strong></p><p>Born and raised in Altar, Maren comes from a family with a long history of service to the city. Her parents were influential figures in Altar's governance, instilling in her a deep sense of duty and commitment to the community. From a young age, Maren was involved in the city's affairs, learning the intricacies of leadership and diplomacy. Her rise to the position of Councilor was a natural progression, driven by her dedication, intelligence, and ability to unite and inspire the people of Altar.</p><p><strong>Personality:</strong></p><p>Maren is known for her calm and composed demeanor, paired with a strong sense of justice and fairness. She is a strategic thinker, able to navigate the complex political landscape of Eilune with ease. Her leadership style is inclusive and collaborative, valuing the input and perspectives of those around her. Maren is deeply committed to the well-being of Altar and its people, often putting their needs above her own. Despite the challenges she faces, she remains optimistic and resilient, always looking for solutions and opportunities to improve the city.</p><p><strong>Personal Life:</strong></p><p>Maren is married to a renowned healer, Kael, who supports her in her duties and shares her commitment to the well-being of Altar. They have one daughter, Lina, who is being raised with a strong sense of community and service. Maren's family is her greatest source of strength and motivation, providing her with the support and perspective needed to lead effectively. She also mentors several young leaders in Altar, guiding them in the responsibilities and challenges of governance.</p><p><strong>Emblem:</strong></p><p>The emblem of Maren's leadership is a silver phoenix rising from flames, symbolizing Altar's resilience, independence, and the rebirth and renewal that come from overcoming adversity.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>","summary":"Name: Maren Leifdottir Title: Councilor of Altar Race: Tiefling Age: Late-40s \"Our city's independence is our greatest asset; we must protect it with wisdom, courage, and unity.\" Appearance: Councilor Maren is a…","sort":12000,"sourceJournal":"Major Players"},{"name":"The Serpent","category":"Characters","group":"Major Players","type":"text","slug":"the-serpent","hero":"assets/Players-Velara.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table><tbody><tr><td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Players-Velara.webp\"/></td><td><p><strong>Name: </strong>Velara</p><p><strong>Title: </strong>Leader of the Gilded Claws</p><p><strong>Race: </strong>Fire Genasi</p><p><strong>Age: </strong>Mid-30s</p><p></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><span><strong>\"I am the serpent that watches from the shadows, striking only when the time is right.\"</strong></span></p><p><strong>Appearance:</strong></p><p>Velara the Serpent is an alluring and formidable figure, her Fire Genasi heritage lending her an otherworldly, almost mesmerizing presence. Her skin has a warm, coppery hue that glows subtly, especially in dim light, and her hair is a cascade of fiery red, often kept loose to emphasize her wild and untamed nature. Her eyes are a molten gold, burning with intensity and intelligence. Velara's most distinctive feature is the intricate golden snake tattoo that coils around her arm, a symbol of her power and control over the Gilded Claws. She typically wears elegant yet practical clothing, favoring dark, rich colors that accentuate her striking appearance.</p><p><strong>Background:</strong></p><p>Born into a life of hardship, Velara learned early on the power of manipulation and cunning to survive. Her Fire Genasi abilities set her apart, allowing her to rise quickly through the ranks of the criminal underworld. Velara's intelligence and ruthlessness helped her eliminate rivals and consolidate power, eventually taking control of the Gilded Claws. Under her leadership, the syndicate has thrived, expanding its influence and operations throughout Easternesse and beyond. Her reputation as both charming and deadly has cemented her status as one of the most feared and respected figures in the criminal underworld.</p><p><strong>Personality:</strong></p><p>Velara is known for her charm and charisma, able to captivate and manipulate those around her with ease. She is a master strategist, always thinking several steps ahead and using her extensive network of spies and informants to stay ahead of her enemies. Velara's leadership style is ruthless and efficient; she demands loyalty and competence from her subordinates, rewarding those who succeed and dealing harshly with those who fail or betray her. Despite her ruthless nature, she is deeply loyal to those who have proven themselves trustworthy and valuable to her operations.</p><p><strong>Personal Life:</strong></p><p>Velara keeps her personal life largely separate from her criminal activities, though she maintains a luxurious residence in a secluded part of Easternesse where she can retreat and relax. She is fiercely private and trusts very few people with personal details about her life. Despite her ruthless nature, Velara is known to have a soft spot for the underdogs and those who show genuine loyalty and potential, often mentoring promising individuals within the syndicate.</p><p><strong>Emblem:</strong></p><p>The emblem of Velara's leadership is a golden snake coiled around a dagger, symbolizing her cunning, her deadly nature, and her iron grip on the Gilded Claws.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>","summary":"Name: Velara Title: Leader of the Gilded Claws Race: Fire Genasi Age: Mid-30s \"I am the serpent that watches from the shadows, striking only when the time is right.\" Appearance: Velara the Serpent is an alluring and…","sort":13000,"sourceJournal":"Major Players"},{"name":"Guilded Claws","category":"Factions","group":"Factions","type":"simple-quest.faction","slug":"guilded-claws","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Groups-GildedClaws.webp","tags":["Ushana"],"mainTag":"Guilded Claws","subtitle":"Snakes in the Shadows","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>The Gilded Claws are a notorious criminal syndicate that operates in the capital city of Easternesse. They are heavily involved in the entertainment district, particularly within the Sandshine Quarter, which is famous for its fighting rings and coliseum shows. This syndicate has its claws deeply embedded in the city's underworld, controlling various illegal activities, from gambling and smuggling to extortion and black market trades.</p><p><strong>Leadership</strong></p><p>The leader of the Gilded Claws is known as <em><strong>Velara the Serpent</strong></em>, a cunning and ruthless woman with a reputation for being both charming and deadly. Velara is a master manipulator who uses her network of spies and informants to maintain control over the syndicate's operations. She is known for her distinctive golden snake tattoo that coils around her arm and symbolizes her iron grip on the organization.</p><p><strong>Structure</strong></p><p>The Gilded Claws are organized into several divisions, each overseen by a lieutenant who reports directly to Velara. These divisions include:</p><ul><li><p><strong>The Rings</strong>: This division manages the fighting rings and coliseum shows. They recruit fighters, fix matches, and ensure that the betting odds favor the syndicate. They also run illegal betting operations, making huge profits from both legitimate and rigged fights.</p></li><li><p><strong>The Shadows</strong>: This group is responsible for espionage, gathering information, and blackmail. They allegedly have agents placed in key positions throughout the city, including in the government, other guilds, and even the Tesseris.</p></li><li><p><strong>The Fangs</strong>: The muscle of the syndicate, the Fangs are enforcers who deal with anyone who opposes the Gilded Claws. They handle extortion, protection rackets, and violent disputes within the criminal underworld.</p></li><li><p><strong>The Silk</strong>: This division manages the more subtle operations, including smuggling rare and illegal goods, running high-stakes gambling dens, and overseeing brothels. They ensure that the syndicate's more discreet activities remain profitable and hidden from the authorities.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Operations</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Fighting Rings and Coliseum Shows</strong>: The Gilded Claws are deeply involved in the organization and management of fighting rings and coliseum events. They recruit and train fighters, often coercing those with debts or personal issues into participating. The syndicate ensures that the events are thrilling and deadly, drawing large crowds and substantial betting.</p></li><li><p><strong>Gambling</strong>: The Gilded Claws run numerous illegal gambling operations, from dice games in back alleys to high-stakes card games in hidden clubs. They also control the betting on coliseum fights, often rigging outcomes to maximize their profits.</p></li><li><p><strong>Smuggling and Black Market</strong>: They smuggle rare and illicit goods into Easternesse, including exotic animals, illegal drugs, and forbidden artifacts. The black market they operate is the go-to place for anyone looking for hard-to-find items.</p></li><li><p><strong>Extortion and Protection Rackets</strong>: The syndicate offers \"protection\" to businesses and individuals in the Sandshine Quarter, ensuring their safety in exchange for regular payments. Those who refuse to pay often find themselves the victims of unfortunate accidents or targeted thefts.</p></li><li><p><strong>Espionage and Blackmail</strong>: With a network of spies and informants, the Gilded Claws gather sensitive information on influential figures and rival organizations. They use this information for blackmail or to manipulate events to their advantage.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Alliance and Rivalries:</strong></p><p>The Gilded Claws have tenuous alliances with other criminal groups and corrupt officials who benefit from their operations. These alliances are often based on mutual interest and can change quickly if circumstances shift.</p><p>The Claws face constant threats from rival gangs looking to take over their territories and from law enforcement agencies aiming to dismantle their operations. The most significant threat comes from the Crimson Justicars, who are determined to bring Runvegr-flavored justice and order to Easternesse.</p><p><strong>Public Perception</strong></p><p>To the average citizen, the Gilded Claws are a shadowy presence that operates behind the scenes of the city's vibrant entertainment district. While many fear them, others see them as a necessary evil, providing excitement and employment in a city where opportunities can be scarce.</p><p>By day, Easternesse's Sandshine Quarter is a bustling hub of legitimate entertainment, but by night, it transforms into the Gilded Claws' playground, where fortunes are made and lost, and lives can change in an instant.</p>","summary":"The Gilded Claws are a notorious criminal syndicate that operates in the capital city of Easternesse. They are heavily involved in the entertainment district, particularly within the Sandshine Quarter, which is famous…","sort":0,"sourceJournal":"Factions Journal"},{"name":"Most Holy Order of Dragon Killers and Dragoons","category":"Factions","group":"Factions","type":"simple-quest.faction","slug":"most-holy-order-of-dragon-killers-and-dragoons","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Groups-Dragoons.webp","tags":["Runvegr"],"mainTag":"Dragoons","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>In the rugged and mystical landscape of Eilune, where magic and might collide, stands the Most Holy Order of Dragon Killers and Dragoons. This esteemed order, rooted deeply in the traditions and defense of the Holy Empire of Runvegr, holds a place of honor and authority second only to the Tesseris, the empire's elite mages.</p><p><strong>Origins and Evolution</strong></p><p>Initially formed to combat the dragons that roamed Eilune's northern territories, the Dragoons were fearsome warriors trained specifically for this purpose. However, the world-altering event known as the Divergence shifted the dragons' presence to the eastern Wastes, past the mysterious Ribbon. In response, the Dragoons' role expanded, transforming them into a versatile military and security force tasked with safeguarding the empire against a variety of threats. Esteemed for their prowess and discipline, Dragoons are highly respected, enjoying a status within Runvegr that is surpassed only by the Tesseris.</p><p><strong>Recruitment and Training</strong></p><p>Entry into this elite Order is fiercely competitive, with candidates—often as young as seven or eight—subjected to rigorous tests conducted by a council of Tesseris Voyants and Elder Dragoons. These trials remain shrouded in secrecy, emphasizing qualities beyond mere physical strength or noble lineage. These tests, whose nature remains a closely guarded secret, seek qualities beyond mere physical prowess, ensuring that only the most capable and resilient candidates are admitted. Upon acceptance, novitiates relinquish all previous ties to status and wealth, dedicating themselves wholly to the decade-long training regimen that awaits them. This intensive preparation covers survival, tracking, combat, and weapons mastery, culminating in the enigmatic final trial known as The Sharpening.</p><p><strong>The Sharpening</strong></p><p>This ritual, marking the transition from trainee to full Dragoon, is a profound and transformative experience. Lasting five days, it bestows upon the participants preternatural abilities, making them among the few men in Runvegr sanctioned to wield such powers. However, the specifics of The Sharpening, including the nature of these abilities, are obscured from the Dragoons' memories, adding an air of mystery to their already formidable reputation.</p><p><strong>The Order's Structure</strong></p><p>The Dragoons are overseen by five Elders, whose dictates are absolute. This leadership ensures the Order remains a cohesive and formidable force within Runvegr and beyond, maintaining the Order's formidable reputation both within and beyond Runvegr's borders.</p><p><strong>Influence and Authority</strong></p><p>Dragoons are revered across Runvegr, their status affording them significant influence and command. Their unparalleled martial skills and the mystical powers conferred upon them during The Sharpening position them as key players in Runvegr's defense and in the broader geopolitical landscape of Eilune. Their ability to rise through the ranks irrespective of their origins is a testament to Runvegr's meritocratic ideals, at least within the confines of this most holy order.</p><p><strong>Relationship with the Tesseris</strong></p><p>Although independent, many Dragoons often find themselves allied with Voyants of the Tesseris, especially when operations extend beyond the national borders. This collaboration underscores the deep interconnection between Runvegr's two most powerful orders, combining might and magic to serve the empire's interests.</p><p>The Most Holy Order of Dragon Killers and Dragoons is not merely a military entity but a pillar of Runvegr's society and a symbol of its values. In the ever-dangerous world of Eilune, they stand as guardians against the dark, wielding their extraordinary abilities to protect and preserve the empire's way of life.</p>","summary":"In the rugged and mystical landscape of Eilune, where magic and might collide, stands the Most Holy Order of Dragon Killers and Dragoons. This esteemed order, rooted deeply in the traditions and defense of the Holy…","sort":0,"sourceJournal":"Factions Journal"},{"name":"Shadewalkers","category":"Factions","group":"Factions","type":"simple-quest.faction","slug":"shadewalkers","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Groups-Shadewalker.webp","tags":["Ribbon"],"mainTag":"","subtitle":"The Ribbon's Pathfinders","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Shadewalkers, the enigmatic guides of the Ribbon, occupy a unique and perilous niche in a world reshaped by cataclysmic events. Skilled in navigating the dangers that lie within and around the Ribbon, these individuals offer their services to those needing to cross the volatile divide, their expertise and experience determining the price of passage. The profession of a Shadewalker is not for the faint of heart; it demands a deep understanding of the Ribbon's ever-changing dangers, as well as the ability to navigate its unpredictable terrain and protect their charges from the myriad threats that dwell within.</p><p><strong>A Clanless Clan</strong></p><p>The lack of formal organization among Shadewalkers speaks to the solitary nature of their work. While some may form temporary alliances, the majority operate alone, guided by their personal code and driven by the rewards their perilous crossings afford. This individualistic approach fosters a diverse range of philosophies and methods among Shadewalkers; some prioritize the safety and success of their entire group, while others adopt a more self-centered view of what constitutes a successful crossing. The diversity among Shadewalkers ensures that those seeking to cross the Ribbon can find a guide suited to their needs and means, though it also introduces an element of unpredictability into the already dangerous journey.</p><p><strong>Bases of Operation</strong></p><p>The city of Shade, nestled in the shadows of the Wastes, serves as a primary haven for Shadewalkers. Its subterranean seclusion offers a respite from the dangers of the Ribbon and the harsh conditions of the Wastes, making it an ideal place for Shadewalkers to rest, resupply, and seek out new clients. Daybreak, positioned on the edge of the Caaddoret Wilds, serves a similar function, providing a point of departure or arrival for those journeys that begin or end in the wilds rather than the Wastes.</p><p><strong>Success Is Marked</strong></p><p>Shadewalkers are marked by distinctive tattoos, a visual testament to their experience and success. The initial tattoo, placed on the neck, signifies at least one successful crossing of the Ribbon, with additional markings adorning the arms or chest for further crossings. These tattoos serve as both a badge of honor and a practical means of establishing credibility among potential clients. However, the definition of \"success\" varies widely among Shadewalkers, from ensuring the safe passage of all members of a group to the mere survival of the Shadewalker themselves.</p><p><strong>Danger In The Dark</strong></p><p>The life of a Shadewalker is fraught with danger, and many meet an early end on the treacherous paths of the Ribbon. Tales of Shadewalkers abandoning their clients at the first sign of trouble are not uncommon, adding an element of risk for those who seek to employ their services. Despite this, the allure of crossing the Ribbon, with its promise of adventure, discovery, or escape, ensures a steady demand for Shadewalkers' unique skills.</p><p>In a world defined by division and danger, Shadewalkers occupy a crucial role, bridging the gap between realms and guiding those brave or desperate enough to traverse the Ribbon. Their existence is a testament to the indomitable will of mortality to overcome the barriers that separate them, forging paths through the unknown in pursuit of their goals.</p>","summary":"Shadewalkers, the enigmatic guides of the Ribbon, occupy a unique and perilous niche in a world reshaped by cataclysmic events. Skilled in navigating the dangers that lie within and around the Ribbon, these individuals…","sort":0,"sourceJournal":"Factions Journal"},{"name":"The Tesseris","category":"Factions","group":"Factions","type":"simple-quest.faction","slug":"the-tesseris","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Groups-TesserisMages.webp","tags":["Runvegr"],"mainTag":"Tesseris","subtitle":"The Witch Queens of Eilune","meta":[],"lists":[{"label":"Influence","items":[{"name":"Runvegr","value":"Extreme"},{"name":"Ember Hinterlands","value":"Strong"},{"name":"Ushana","value":"Medium"},{"name":"Wisivashu","value":"Low"},{"name":"Coskoreia","value":"Low"},{"name":"Efra Dorei","value":"Non-Existent"}]}],"content":"<p>The Tesseris are a venerable and powerful order of mages within the Holy Empire of Runvegr, holding sway over not just the nation’s military and governance but extending their influence across the world. Born in the aftermath of the cataclysmic Divergence, they were the pioneers in understanding and harnessing the new forms of magic that emerged.</p><p>The Tesseris are revered and feared in equal measure, seen as protectors of Runvegr's heritage and as formidable wielders of magic. Their presence ensures the empire's place as a dominant force in the post-Divergence world, with their actions and decisions influencing the fate of nations.</p><p><strong>The Four Shades of Magic</strong></p><p>Central to the Tesseris' power are the four shades of magic—black, white, blue, and red—each embodying different aspects and powers. The Tesseris guard the knowledge of these magics jealously, though inevitably, whispers of their power spread beyond Runvegr's borders. Those outside the Tesseris who attempt to wield these powers are derogatorily termed \"glamour witches\" or \"glams\" and are often pursued by the Tesseris for fear of misuse or dilution of their sacred arts. Glams are hunted down for forced enlistment or elimination.</p><p><strong>Membership and Structure</strong></p><p>The Tesseris is an all-female order, with members known as Voyants. Potential members undergo rigorous training, initially at Kappknottr, where they are introduced to the basics of magic. They must then choose to align with one of the four shades, a decision that dictates their path and specialization within the order. The final rite of passage is a perilous trial testing their magical aptitude, knowledge, and survival skills. Those who emerge successful are assigned roles either within Runvegr or across the globe.</p><p><strong>Governance</strong></p><p>At the helm of the Tesseris is the Most High, elected to lead the order. Her authority is absolute, aided by the Twelve Hands—three master mages for each shade of magic—who oversee the order's operations and ensure the purity and potency of their respective magics. The Most High is supported directly by her Left and Right Hands, who act as her closest advisors and enforcers, executing her will both within and beyond the empire's borders.</p><p>If the Right Hand of the Most High is her blade in hand, then the Left Hand is the one concealed in her sleeve.</p><p><strong>Laws and Customs</strong></p><p>The Voyants of the Tesseris are bound by strict laws that dictate their conduct and appearance. Within Runvegr, they must wear cloaks corresponding to their chosen shade of magic, ensuring their recognition and respect. Their word is law, with any disobedience met with severe penalties, reinforcing the Tesseris' authority and the seriousness with which their commands are to be taken. Due to the potential dangers of their role, many Voyants are accompanied by Runvegr Dragoons when operating outside the nation, providing additional protection and companionship.</p><p><strong>The Inquisitors</strong></p><p>The Crimson Justicars serve as the vigilant guardians of spiritual and magical justice within the Tesseris. Known simply as \"Justicars\" by those they protect and judge, these formidable enforcers embody the duality of divine wrath and balanced judgment.</p><p>Each Justicar is a master of both Red and White magic, a rare and revered combination that grants them unparalleled versatility in the field. Clad in cloaks and heavy armor that reflect both their associated magical shade, their presence is further distinguished by a unique symbol embroidered on their attire: a sword entwined with scales, rendered in shades of red and white. This emblem is a stark reminder of their dual mandate to wield the sword in defense of order and to balance the scales of justice.</p><p>The Justicars are more than mere warriors; they are inquisitors of the highest order. When violations and disturbances threaten the peace of Runvegr and beyond, the Justicars are dispatched to seek out the perpetrators. With the might of their sword and the righteousness of their magic, they ensure that the law is upheld with unwavering resolve.</p><p>Answering directly to the Right Hand of the Tesseris, the Justicars operate with a level of autonomy and authority that is unparalleled. Their decisions are guided by a deep sense of duty and an unshakeable moral compass, instilled in them through rigorous training and the sacred oaths they swear upon initiation.</p>","summary":"The Tesseris are a venerable and powerful order of mages within the Holy Empire of Runvegr, holding sway over not just the nation’s military and governance but extending their influence across the world. Born in the…","sort":0,"sourceJournal":"Factions Journal"},{"name":"Holy Empire of Runvegr","category":"Places","group":"Holy Empire of Runvegr","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"holy-empire-of-runvegr","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/StainedGlass-Runvegr.webp","tags":["Nation","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Runvegr","subtitle":"A vast imperial realm of ice, faith, and military discipline, ruled through the intertwined power of the throne, the Tesseris, and the Dragoons.","meta":[{"label":"Population","value":"~2.3 million"},{"label":"Area","value":"100,000 square miles"},{"label":"Government","value":"Imperial Theocracy"},{"label":"Demonym","value":"Runvegrian"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"Empress Eira Thrymsdottir"},{"label":"Founded","value":"c. 1 PD (Modern Empire)"}],"lists":[],"content":"<p>The Holy Empire of Runvegr, the icy bastion of theocracy in Eilune, stands as a realm where the lines between magic, religion, and governance blur into a singular force of power and control. This northern empire, once known for its temperate climes that graciously yielded to the touch of warmth during the fleeting summer months, has been transformed by the cataclysmic events of the Divergence into a land eternally shrouded in frost and snow. The landscape, a sprawling expanse of white, mirrors the rigidity and coldness of its ruling order, presenting a stark testament to the resilience and tenacity of its people.</p><p>At the heart of Runvegr's vast tundra lies Horgrknottr, the empire's sacred capital. Here, the Empress, a figure of divine authority and secular power, presides over her frozen dominion. Her rule is supported and enforced by the Tesseris, an elite cadre of mages who are not only masters of the arcane arts but also the empire's military commanders, enforcers of its stringent laws, and guardians of its cultural legacy. The Tesseris wield an influence that permeates every facet of Runvegrian society, their presence a constant reminder of the empire's might and the peril of dissent.</p><p>In Runvegr, the intertwining of religion and magic dictates the rhythm of daily life. Worship of Erov, the Goddess of Winter, Magic, and the Moon, is not merely a matter of faith but a codified mandate, her doctrines shaping the laws that govern the land. Magic, while revered as a divine gift, is subject to strict regulation, its practice a privilege reserved exclusively for women. This gendered control over the arcane is enforced with ruthless efficiency, with men found to possess magical talents or daring to dabble in the arts swiftly apprehended by the Tesseris. The fate of these men remains a closely guarded secret, shrouded in whispers and fear; their disappearance serving as a grim warning to others who might challenge the ordained order.</p><p>Runvegr's isolation, both geographically and ideologically, is deepened by its antagonism towards Efra Dorei and, by extension, all those of elvish lineage. The blame for the Divergence, cast upon the elves with scant evidence, has sown seeds of suspicion and hostility that have taken deep root in the national psyche. Elves and their kin are regarded with a mix of wariness and outright animosity, their presence within the empire's borders a source of unease and contention.</p><p>Despite its harsh climate and the severity of its rulers, Runvegr is not devoid of beauty or culture. The empire's architecture, with its soaring spires and intricate ice sculptures, reflects the elegance and complexity of its beliefs. Runvegrian art and literature are suffused with themes of endurance, the mystical beauty of winter, and the solemn reverence for the moon and magic. Festivals dedicated to Erov illuminate the perpetual twilight of the tundra, their celebrations a rare but fervent defiance of the cold that grips the land.</p><p>Runvegr stands as a formidable power in Eilune, its influence extending far beyond its icy borders. The empire's unwavering devotion to its theocratic principles and the unparalleled control over magic wielded by the Tesseris make it a respected and feared force on the continent. Yet, beneath the veneer of unity and strength lie the complexities of a society grappling with the legacies of its past and the realities of a world forever altered by the Divergence.</p>","summary":"The Holy Empire of Runvegr, the icy bastion of theocracy in Eilune, stands as a realm where the lines between magic, religion, and governance blur into a singular force of power and control. This northern empire, once…","sort":100000,"sourceJournal":"Holy Empire of Runvegr"},{"name":"Horgrknotter","category":"Places","group":"Holy Empire of Runvegr","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"horgrknotter","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Horgrknottr.webp","tags":["City","Capital","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Runvegr","subtitle":"","meta":[{"label":"Population","value":"~180,000"},{"label":"Area","value":"65 square miles"},{"label":"Government","value":"Imperial Theocratic Capital"},{"label":"Demonym","value":"Horgrknottrian"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"Empress Eira Thrymsdottir"},{"label":"Founded","value":"c. 1 PD (Modern Empire)"}],"lists":[{"label":"Notable Locations","items":[{"name":"The Empress’s Palace","description":"Fortified imperial residence and administrative heart of the empire."},{"name":"Temple of Erov","description":"Spiritual center of Runvegr; a colossal temple of white marble, blue-veined ice, silver, and sapphires."},{"name":"The Fourfold Spire","description":"The Tesseris Capital Tower, a citadel of magic, libraries, arcane workshops, wards, and mage training.","icon":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Groups-Tesseris.webp"},{"name":"Citadel of the Spear","description":"Dragoon Capital Headquarters, consisting of barracks, armouries, libraries, and training grounds.","icon":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/packs/classes/class-dragoon.png"},{"name":"The Imperial Gardens","description":"Snowbound palace gardens that thrive despite the cold, maintained through sacred craft and magic."}]}],"content":"<p>Horgrknottr, the sacred heart of Runvegr, rises from the icy expanse like a vision from a frost-bound dream, its grandeur a testament to the empire’s might and devotion. This holy capital, ensconced within the embrace of the perpetual tundra, mirrors the fierce beauty and indomitable spirit of its people. Its architecture, inspired by the ancient Nordic styles of Eilune's distant past, showcases towering spires that reach towards the heavens, vast halls carved from ice and stone, and elaborate runic carvings that weave tales of gods, magic, and the valor of ancestors.</p><p>The city is built to withstand the relentless embrace of winter, its structures sprawling yet interconnected, creating a labyrinth of wind-sheltered walkways and enclosed bridges. The buildings, with their steeply pitched roofs and heavy timbers, are designed not just for beauty but also for practicality, shedding snow and ice with ease. Stone and ice blend seamlessly in Horgrknottr’s construction, with the latter not merely as a building material but as a medium for artistry. Ice sculptures, luminescent and intricate, line the public squares and the exteriors of temples, glowing ethereally under the auroras that dance across the sky.</p><p>At the city's center stands the Temple of Erov, a marvel of Runvegrian architecture and faith. This colossal structure, built from white marble and blue-veined ice, houses the empire's most sacred relic and serves as the focal point for the worship of Erov. The temple’s dome, adorned with silver and sapphires, reflects the moonlight, casting a serene glow over the city. Its interior is a vast, echoing space filled with statues of the Goddess in her many aspects, and the walls are inscribed with runes that tell of her dominion over winter, magic, and the moon.</p><p>The Empress’s palace, another architectural masterpiece, dominates the skyline with its imposing fortifications and elegant gardens that somehow thrive amidst the snow. The palace, a fortress of solitude and power, serves as both the residence of the Empress and the administrative heart of the empire. Its halls are decorated with tapestries and paintings that capture the history and mythology of Runvegr, while its windows, framed by intricate stonework, offer views of the stark, breathtaking landscape beyond.</p><p>Horgrknottr is also home to the Tesseris’ stronghold, a citadel of knowledge and magic. This formidable complex, with its library towers and arcane workshops, is where the empire’s mages study the mysteries of the arcane and train in the arts of war and peace. The stronghold is a hive of activity, with apprentices and masters alike working to harness the powers bestowed by Erov, their efforts safeguarded by wards and spells woven into the very fabric of the buildings.</p><p>Despite its icy veneer, Horgrknottr is a city alive with color and light. The markets bustle with traders selling furs, jewels, and enchanted items, their stalls arranged around warm hearths. Festivals, marked by the lighting of great bonfires and the telling of epic sagas, bring warmth and joy to the city’s inhabitants, their laughter and songs a defiant echo against the cold.</p><p>Horgrknottr, with its grandeur and Nordic-inspired architecture, stands as a beacon of Runvegr’s enduring strength and its reverence for tradition and the divine. It is a city carved from the ice, a symbol of an empire’s will to not just survive but to thrive in a world forever changed, its beauty and majesty a testament to the indomitable spirit of its people.</p>","summary":"Horgrknottr, the sacred heart of Runvegr, rises from the icy expanse like a vision from a frost-bound dream, its grandeur a testament to the empire’s might and devotion. This holy capital, ensconced within the embrace…","sort":200000,"sourceJournal":"Holy Empire of Runvegr"},{"name":"The Drekka","category":"Places","group":"Holy Empire of Runvegr","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"the-drekka","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-TheDrekka.webp","tags":["Wilderness","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Runvegr","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>The Drekka is a massive caved-in hole located near Norvbay in Runvegr, measuring dozens of miles across and so deep that its bottom cannot be seen. Its edges are jagged and uneven, suggesting a sudden and violent collapse rather than a gradual erosion. The walls of the Drekka are dark and forbidding, with strange symbols and markings etched into the rock, hinting at mystical or arcane significance.</p><p>The area around the Drekka is barren and desolate, with no signs of life or vegetation. The air is cold and still, adding to the eerie atmosphere of the place. Some say that strange whispers can be heard emanating from the depths of the Drekka, while others claim to have seen ghostly figures moving along its rim at night.</p><p>Despite its ominous appearance, the Drekka is a place of fascination for many scholars and adventurers, who are drawn to its mysteries and the possibility of uncovering ancient secrets buried within its depths. However, few who venture into the Drekka ever return, adding to its reputation as a place of danger and dread.</p>","summary":"The Drekka is a massive caved-in hole located near Norvbay in Runvegr, measuring dozens of miles across and so deep that its bottom cannot be seen. Its edges are jagged and uneven, suggesting a sudden and violent…","sort":212500,"sourceJournal":"Holy Empire of Runvegr"},{"name":"Drekkjaheimr","category":"Places","group":"Holy Empire of Runvegr","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"drekkjaheimr","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Drekkjaheimr.webp","tags":["City","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Runvegr","subtitle":"A resilient Runvegrian city of stone, ice, hearthlight, and skilled hands, built along a vast frozen lake whose beauty sustains and threatens its people in equal measure.","meta":[{"label":"Population","value":"~31,000"},{"label":"Area","value":"14 square miles"},{"label":"Government","value":"Communal Hall Council under Imperial Oversight"},{"label":"Demonym","value":"Drekkjaheimrian"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"The Hallwarden of Drekkjaheimr"},{"label":"Founded","value":"Early Post-Divergence Era"}],"lists":[{"label":"Notable Locations","items":[{"name":"The Great Hall","description":"Central meeting place, feasting hall, and seat of local governance."},{"name":"Drekksjo","description":"Vast icebound lake that provides fresh water, defense, festivals, and danger."},{"name":"The Lake Holes","description":"Carefully maintained openings in the ice used to draw fresh water."},{"name":"Artisans’ Row","description":"Workshops producing jewelry, weapons, carvings, tools, and enchanted craftwork."},{"name":"The Stonecarvers' Facades","description":"District of carved buildings depicting dragons, heroes, gods, and Runvegrian myths."},{"name":"Drekksjo Market","description":"Bustling trade district where locals and travelers gather for craft goods and northern wares."},{"name":"The Gray Quays","description":"Lakeside docks, sled platforms, and storage houses used when the ice roads are passable."}]}],"content":"<p>Drekkjaheimr, a city sculpted from the ice and stone of Runvegr's unforgiving landscape, stands as a testament to the resilience and ingenuity of its people. Positioned along the edge of a vast frozen lake, this medium-sized city combines the stark beauty of its natural surroundings with the architectural elegance born of necessity and tradition. The city serves as a vibrant community for some who call the icy expanse of Runvegr home.</p><p>The heart of Drekkjaheimr beats in rhythm with the frozen lake beside which it has been built. This massive body of ice, ever-present and unyielding, is not merely a backdrop to the city but an integral part of its identity. The lake provides a source of fresh water, accessed through carefully maintained holes that pierce its thick surface, and serves as a natural defense against potential invaders. During the long winter nights, the ice plays host to festivals and gatherings, its surface illuminated by torches and magical lights, creating a spectacle of dancing shadows and gleaming reflections.</p><p>The architecture of Drekkjaheimr reflects the dual demands of beauty and survival. Buildings are constructed from the gray stone of the surrounding mountains, their walls thick and insulating, designed to hold back the chill of the perpetual winter. Roofs are steeply pitched, allowing snow to slide off rather than accumulate. But it is not just in its practicality that the city's architecture shines; intricate carvings and statues adorn the facades of buildings, telling stories of Runvegr's history and mythology, of dragons and heroes, of gods and the elements.</p><p>The city is known for its skilled artisans and craftsmen, who draw inspiration from the landscape and the legends of Runvegr. Their workshops produce goods that are both functional and beautiful, from intricately wrought jewelry that captures the glimmer of ice to weapons forged in the likeness of the creatures that roam the wilds. The marketplaces of Drekkjaheimr are a bustling hive of activity, where locals and visitors alike come to trade, share news, and seek the unique wares for which the city is renowned.</p><p>Community life in Drekkjaheimr revolves around the Great Hall, a magnificent structure that serves as a meeting place, feasting hall, and center of governance. Here, the city's leaders gather to discuss matters of state, and citizens come together to celebrate achievements, mark the changing seasons, and strengthen the bonds of kinship and friendship that sustain them through the darkest days.</p><p>Despite its beauty and the strength of its community, Drekkjaheimr is not without its challenges. The frozen lake, while a source of life, can also be a harbinger of danger, with creatures from the deep occasionally breaking through the ice to threaten the city. The ever-present cold demands constant vigilance and effort to ensure survival. Yet, the people of Drekkjaheimr face these challenges with a resilience born of generations living in harmony with the ice and snow.</p><p>Drekkjaheimr, with its frozen lake and stone edifices, stands as a symbol of Runvegr's enduring spirit. It is a city that has carved out a place of warmth and light in the midst of the ice, a beacon for those who navigate the frozen wilds of the north.</p>","summary":"Drekkjaheimr, a city sculpted from the ice and stone of Runvegr's unforgiving landscape, stands as a testament to the resilience and ingenuity of its people. Positioned along the edge of a vast frozen lake, this…","sort":225000,"sourceJournal":"Holy Empire of Runvegr"},{"name":"Drekksjo","category":"Places","group":"Holy Empire of Runvegr","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"drekksjo","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Drekksjo.webp","tags":["Drekkjaheimr","Lake","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Runvegr","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Drekksjo, a vast frozen lake at the heart of Runvegr, is as much a symbol of the region's harsh beauty as it is a source of life and legend. Spanning approximately 40-45 miles in diameter, its irregular circular shape is encased by towering ice shelves and jagged cliffs, natural barriers that reflect the rugged resilience of the land and its people.</p><p>For centuries, the lake has been a cornerstone of Runvegr's identity, sustaining its inhabitants while inspiring awe and reverence through its enigmatic presence.</p><p>Drekksjo’s icy surface forms a glimmering mirror under the moonlight, reflecting the celestial dance of Erov and her hounds, Slaine and Bran. During the harshest winters, the ice solidifies into a thick, unbroken expanse, strong enough to support the weight of caravans and gatherings. Beneath this frozen veneer, the lake conceals mysteries both natural and mythical.</p><p>Legends speak of <em>Vetrarsongr</em>, the Winter’s Song, an ethereal glow that illuminates the ice from below, caused by the movement of luminescent creatures in the frigid depths. These elusive beings are said to embody the lake’s spirit, their presence a symbol of life persisting in the most inhospitable conditions.</p><p>Despite its size and importance, the true depth of Drekksjo remains unknown. Tales of submerged ruins and ancient relics stir the imaginations of explorers, yet few dare to test the lake’s icy grip.</p><p>Drekksjo’s significance goes beyond its physical form; it is a lifeline for the city of Drekkjaheimr, which stands proudly on its shores. The lake provides fresh water, drawn through carefully maintained holes in the ice, and its depths are home to the prized <em>hrafnsilfr</em> fish. These creatures, known for their shimmering, silver-like scales, are not only a vital source of food but also a symbol of Runvegr’s craftsmanship. Jewelry and artifacts fashioned from the scales of <em>hrafnsilfr</em> are renowned for their beauty and rarity.</p><p>The lake also serves as a central stage for community gatherings and festivals. During the long winter nights, its surface transforms into a bustling arena of light and music. Events such as <em>Erovsveil</em> celebrate the goddess Erov and her hounds with feasting, dancing, and storytelling. The ice reflects flickering torches and magical lights, creating a scene of haunting beauty that reinforces the bond between the people of Runvegr and their land.</p><p>Drekksjo, for all its splendor, is not without its dangers. The ice, though deceptively stable, can crack and shatter without warning, plunging the unwary into its freezing depths. The lake’s depths are also said to harbor <em>issormar</em> - ancient, serpentine creatures of immense size. Though rarely seen, the <em>issormar</em> are spoken of in hushed tones, their movements said to cause ripples and tremors that can shake the ice above.</p><p>To the people of Drekkjaheimr, Drekksjo is more than a lake—it is a symbol of their unyielding spirit. It embodies the delicate balance between life and survival, a balance they strive to maintain against the ever-present challenges of their frozen homeland.</p>","summary":"Drekksjo, a vast frozen lake at the heart of Runvegr, is as much a symbol of the region's harsh beauty as it is a source of life and legend. Spanning approximately 40-45 miles in diameter, its irregular circular shape…","sort":237500,"sourceJournal":"Holy Empire of Runvegr"},{"name":"Giptavollr","category":"Places","group":"Holy Empire of Runvegr","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"giptavollr","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Giptavollr.webp","tags":["City","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Runvegr","subtitle":"Fertile breadbasket city of Runvegr","meta":[{"label":"Population","value":"~74,000"},{"label":"Area","value":"32 square miles"},{"label":"Government","value":"Mayoral Agricultural Governorship under Tesseris Oversight"},{"label":"Demonym","value":"Giptavollrian"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"Mayor of Giptavollr"},{"label":"Founded","value":"Early Post-Divergence Era"}],"lists":[{"label":"Notable Locations","items":[{"name":"The Mayor’s Hall","description":"Civic seat of Giptavollr’s mayor and local agricultural administration."},{"name":"The Harvest Market","description":"Main marketplace for produce, grains, livestock, tools, pottery, clothing, and regional goods."},{"name":"Tesseris Provision House","description":"Tesseris administrative post overseeing law, food security, storage, and distribution."},{"name":"The Granary Wards","description":"Heavily protected storehouses holding grain reserves for the city and broader Runvegr."},{"name":"The Good Luck Fields","description":"Fertile farmlands surrounding the city, source of its name and prosperity."},{"name":"The Millstream District","description":"Mills, bakeries, granaries, and waterworks that process the valley’s harvests."},{"name":"The Feastgrounds","description":"Open communal grounds used for harvest festivals, seasonal feasts, contests, and music."}]}],"content":"<p>Giptavollr, known as the \"Good Luck Field,\" is a sprawling city that began as a humble farming village but has since grown into one of the largest agricultural hubs in Runvegr. Situated in a fertile valley, the city is surrounded by vast farmlands that stretch for miles, providing a significant portion of the nation's food supply.</p><p>The city itself is a bustling center of activity, with markets selling fresh produce, grains, and livestock from the surrounding farms. The streets are lined with shops, inns, and taverns catering to the needs of farmers and travelers alike. Giptavollr is also known for its skilled craftsmen, producing goods such as tools, clothing, and pottery that are traded throughout the region.</p><p>Despite its size and prosperity, Giptavollr maintains a close-knit community feel, with many families having lived in the area for generations. The people of Giptavollr take pride in their work, celebrating the harvest season with elaborate festivals and feasts that draw visitors from far and wide.</p><p>The city is governed by a mayor, but ultimate authority lies with the Tesseris, who have a significant presence in Giptavollr. The Tesseris ensure the city's safety and security, but their influence also extends to the city's laws and governance, with the mayor often deferring to their judgment on important matters.</p><p>Overall, Giptavollr is a vibrant and thriving city, its prosperity built on the hard work and dedication of its inhabitants. It serves as a shining example of Runvegr's agricultural prowess and the resilience of its people.</p>","summary":"Giptavollr, known as the \"Good Luck Field,\" is a sprawling city that began as a humble farming village but has since grown into one of the largest agricultural hubs in Runvegr. Situated in a fertile valley, the city is…","sort":250000,"sourceJournal":"Holy Empire of Runvegr"},{"name":"Kappknottr","category":"Places","group":"Holy Empire of Runvegr","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"kappknottr","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Kappknottr.png","tags":["Tesseris","Dragoons"],"mainTag":"Runvegr","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Kappknottr, the formidable bastion of solitude and discipline, stands amidst the howling winds and perpetual snows of the northern tundras of Runvegr. This stark fortress, far removed from the bustling life of the empire’s heart, serves a singular and sacred purpose: the forging of Runvegr’s most elite protectors and enforcers, the Tesseris mages and the Holy Order of Dragoons. Here, in isolation that is both physical and psychological, recruits are transformed through rigorous training and trials, emerging as paragons of strength, loyalty, and arcane prowess.</p><p>Constructed from stone quarried from the very mountains it stands against, Kappknottr is a monument to endurance. Its walls, thick and impervious, rise like a challenge to the elements, while its towers, sharp and imposing, pierce the sky. The architecture of the fortress is utilitarian, designed not for comfort but for survival and efficiency. The sprawling complex includes extensive training grounds, both indoors and out, where recruits practice combat tactics, magic, and survival skills in conditions that mirror the harshness of the world beyond.</p><p>Beneath the fortress lie the caverns that sustain its occupants. Here, in the dimly lit depths, food is cultivated in a stark reminder of the fortress’s self-sufficiency. Rodent farms and fungal groves provide sustenance, a daily testament to the adaptability and resilience expected of those who train within Kappknottr’s walls. Water, drawn from the glaciers and snowfields that envelop the fortress, is another precious resource, meticulously collected and rationed.</p><p>The interior of Kappknottr is divided into distinct sectors, reflecting the separation of its inhabitants by role and gender. The dormitories and training areas for the Dragoon men and Tesseris women are strategically placed in separate wings of the fortress, fostering a sense of camaraderie and unity within each group while maintaining the traditional divisions of Runvegrian society. Despite this separation, the dining hall and library serve as neutral grounds where the two groups converge, sharing meals and knowledge, their interactions a rare blend of rivalry and mutual respect.</p><p>Romance, though uncommon, does blossom within the cold stone walls of Kappknottr, often seen as either a scandalous defiance of discipline or a testament to the indomitable nature of the human heart. These clandestine relationships, woven into the fabric of daily life, add a touch of warmth to the icy solitude of the fortress, challenging the notions of duty and personal desire.</p><p>Kappknottr is not just a fortress but a crucible, where the future defenders of Runvegr are shaped by the trials of isolation, discipline, and relentless training. It is a place where legends are born, where the might of the Tesseris and the valor of the Dragoons are forged in ice and shadow. The fortress stands as a stark reminder of Runvegr’s commitment to its survival and sovereignty, a beacon of strength in the desolate beauty of the northern tundra.</p>","summary":"Kappknottr, the formidable bastion of solitude and discipline, stands amidst the howling winds and perpetual snows of the northern tundras of Runvegr. This stark fortress, far removed from the bustling life of the…","sort":262500,"sourceJournal":"Holy Empire of Runvegr"},{"name":"Kvammaknottr","category":"Places","group":"Holy Empire of Runvegr","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"kvammaknottr","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Kvamaknottr.webp","tags":["City","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Runvegr","subtitle":"Masked threshold city of southern Runvegr","meta":[{"label":"Population","value":"~52,000"},{"label":"Area","value":"24 square miles"},{"label":"Government","value":"Oligarchic Council under Imperial Oversight"},{"label":"Demonym","value":"Kvamaknottrian"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"Council of the Sphere"},{"label":"Founded","value":"Early Post-Divergence Era"}],"lists":[{"label":"Notable Locations","items":[{"name":"Velkominn Gate","description":"Ancient moonstone-inlaid gate marking the ceremonial threshold into Runvegr."},{"name":"Plaza of Erov","description":"Central plaza and civic-spiritual heart of the city, etched with lunar paths and celestial runes."},{"name":"Statue of Erov","description":"Monumental statue of the moon goddess holding a moonstone orb representing Bran."},{"name":"Council Hall of the Sphere","description":"Formal seat of the rotating Council of the Sphere."},{"name":"Tesseris Tower","description":"The Tesseris Headquarters for the city","icon":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Groups-Tesseris.webp"}]}],"content":"<p></p><p>Kvamaknottr, which translates to “The Arrival Sphere” in the old Runvegrian tongue, serves as the first true threshold into the Holy Empire for those passing through the fortified highland stronghold of Miskunnkvama. Nestled within a wide, glacial valley carved by ancient iceflows, the city acts as both a crossroads and a ceremonial veil—a place where diplomacy, tradition, and silent power converge.</p><p>The architecture of Kvamaknottr reflects its dual nature: both welcoming and watchful. Frost-weathered stone and dark timber rise in tiered concentric rings, each level wrapped like a spiral around the city’s heart: the Plaza of Erov. At its center stands a monumental statue of the moon goddess Erov, cloaked in sculpted winter robes, her porcelain mask turned slightly toward the heavens. In one hand, she cradles a smooth, moonstone orb said to represent Bran, one of Runvegr’s three moons. The plaza’s cobblestones are etched with spiraling lunar paths and celestial runes—a functional calendar to most, a coded ledger to those who know how to read between the stars.</p><p>Kvamaknottr is ruled by a rotating Council of the Sphere, composed of nobles, merchant-princes, and emissaries from the Holy Empire's capital. But beneath the formalities lies the true power structure, the alleged \"Circle Unspoken\", a cabal of mask-bearing families and foreign agents who deal in favors, threats, and blood.</p><p>The Tesseris maintain a curated presence, often intervening only when diplomacy fails or vril-stability is compromised. Their agents here wear masks stitched with red and white thread and are more interested in silencing destabilizing truths than keeping the peace.</p><p>Kvamaknottr is famed for its mask-wearing culture, a tradition that has become local law. Masks here are not merely ceremonial; they are essential social markers. Style, shape, and embellishment reveal lineage, allegiance, rank, and even emotional intent. To walk unmasked is to issue a statement: bold, foolish, or defiant. Even travelers must wear simple linen masks provided at the gates, a custom framed as hospitality but enforced with quiet precision. More ornate masks, those woven with glass thread or inked with vril-reactive dyes, are restricted by law, their use reserved solely for members of the Tesseris.</p><p>Commerce flourishes in Kvamaknottr’s lower rings, where the valley’s milder climate allows for trade routes from Altar, Ushana, and the deeper Runvegrian provinces. Stalls offer preserved fish from Pagallvolr, carved bone tools from Drekkjaheimr, and spices wrapped in vellum from the Ember Hinterlands. But even these markets are carefully surveilled. Every merchant’s arrival is logged in the Arrival Codex, and foreign goods are often subtly inspected for enchantments or contraband runes before being allowed past the outermost ring.</p><p>Festivals in Kvamaknottr are spectacles of cold light and colder meaning. During major holidays and festivals, the city becomes a stage for its infamous silent masquerades—evening gatherings in which no words are spoken, only gestures exchanged beneath flickering lanterns and veiled scrutiny. It is said that entire treaties have been negotiated in silence, entire lives undone with a tilt of a masked head.</p><p>At the city's edge, the Velkominn Gate rises in solemn welcome, its ancient stone carved with celestial symbols and inlaid with faint strands of moonstone. It stands as both threshold and warning. Guard towers loom above it, housing emissaries, wardens, and the ever-present Tesseris observers who ensure that no one enters or leaves Kvamaknottr unnoticed. Hospitality here is not a right but a ritual, and the weight of history hangs heavy on the snow-slicked rooftops.</p><p>Though Kvamaknottr may be the \"first face of Runvegr,\" it is a carefully painted one, layered in tradition, guarded by silence, and watched from behind countless masks. Travelers often leave with awe in their hearts and the uncanny feeling that they’ve been studied more thoroughly than they realize.</p>","summary":"Kvamaknottr, which translates to “The Arrival Sphere” in the old Runvegrian tongue, serves as the first true threshold into the Holy Empire for those passing through the fortified highland stronghold of Miskunnkvama.…","sort":275000,"sourceJournal":"Holy Empire of Runvegr"},{"name":"Medalvegr","category":"Places","group":"Holy Empire of Runvegr","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"medalvegr","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Medalvegr.webp","tags":["City","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Runvegr","subtitle":"Liminal bridge-town between Norvbay and the Northern Empty","meta":[{"label":"Population","value":"~9,500"},{"label":"Area","value":"5 square miles"},{"label":"Government","value":"Imperial Bridgewardenship under Tesseris Observation"},{"label":"Demonym","value":"Medalvegrian"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"The Bridgewarden of Medalvegr"},{"label":"Founded","value":"Pre-Divergence; fortified and resettled in the Early Post-Divergence Era"}],"lists":[{"label":"Notable Locations","items":[{"name":"The Sundered Stones","description":"Memorial markers bearing the names of soldiers who died before the Ribbon ended the Efra Dorei war."},{"name":"The Medalvegr Bridge","description":"Ancient bridge connecting the Norvbay side to the Northern Empty; once nearly destroyed during the Efra Dorei war."},{"name":"The Bridgewarden’s Keep","description":"Fortified administrative seat overseeing the crossing, patrols, bridge maintenance, and restricted travel."},{"name":"The Drekka Watch","description":"Tesseris-monitored towers facing the Drekka and the distant threat of the Ribbon."},{"name":"The Old Efran Camp","description":"Ruins or marked fields where Efra Dorei forces once camped while preparing to use the bridge against Runvegr."},{"name":"The Moot Hall","description":"Old stone hall where Runvegrian leaders debated whether to destroy the bridge and cut themselves off from the world."},{"name":"The Severance Shrine","description":"Shrine commemorating the day the Ribbon appeared and made the old war impossible to continue."},{"name":"The Spanworks","description":"Workshops and storage houses dedicated to maintaining the bridge against ice, wind, and age."},{"name":"The Northern Empty Road","description":"The lonely road leading across the bridge into the barren lands beyond."}]}],"content":"<p>Medalvegr, known in the old Runvegrian tongue as Meðalvegr, \"Between Realms\", is a small but ancient bridge-town built around one of the strangest crossings in northern Runvegr. It stands where the frozen reach of Norvbay gives way toward the Northern Empty, its bridge stretching across a bleak threshold of ice, stone, wind, and memory. To most travelers, Medalvegr feels less like a destination than a pause between worlds.</p><p>Before the Divergence, Medalvegr was a place of immense strategic importance. During the war between Runvegr and Efra Dorei, Efran forces camped near the Drekka, seeking to use the bridge as a route into Runvegrian territory. The bridge became the center of bitter debate within Runvegr itself. Some demanded its destruction, arguing that no span was worth the risk of invasion. Others feared that breaking it would cut Runvegr off from the wider world forever. The argument was never truly resolved; the Ribbon appeared, the world was severed, and the bridge's purpose changed in an instant.</p><p>Now Medalvegr endures as a settlement of bridgekeepers, soldiers, scouts, fishers, pilgrims, and Tesseris observers. Its stone houses crouch against the wind near the bridgehead, their windows narrow and their doors heavy. Old fortifications remain embedded in the town like scars, while newer watchtowers face the Drekka with lenses, signal fires, and quiet wards. The Tesseris maintain a careful presence here, less interested in governing daily life than in watching for disturbances: vril-shear, strange lights, impossible echoes, and anything that might suggest the Ribbon's wound is shifting.</p><p>The Medalvegr Bridge itself dominates the town's identity. It is both road and relic, lifeline and warning. Its stones are older than the current empire, worn smooth by soldiers, merchants, refugees, and pilgrims who once crossed freely between lands now divided by forces no road can overcome. The people of Medalvegr maintain the span with ritual care, replacing cracked stones, scraping away black ice, and leaving small offerings along the rail before storms. Some locals say the bridge remembers every army that crossed it, and every army that never did.</p><p>Life in Medalvegr is quiet but not empty. The Between-Market serves bridge guards, travelers, fisherfolk from Norvbay, salvage crews, and those few bold enough to approach the Northern Empty. The Moot Hall still stands, marking the place where Runvegrian leaders once argued over whether to destroy the bridge. Beyond the town lie the remains of the old Efran encampment, half-buried beneath snow and frost, where rusted stakes and broken stones still emerge from the ground during thaws. The Severance Shrine commemorates the day the Ribbon appeared and rendered the old war meaningless.</p><p>Medalvegr is not grand like Horgrknottr, warm like Pagallvolr, or lively like Giptavollr. It is a place of waiting. A place where history stopped mid-breath. A place where Runvegr did not choose isolation, but inherited it. Travelers who cross the bridge often feel that they are being watched not only by guards and Tesseris lenses, but by the severed shape of the world itself.</p>","summary":"Medalvegr, known in the old Runvegrian tongue as Meðalvegr, \"Between Realms\", is a small but ancient bridge-town built around one of the strangest crossings in northern Runvegr. It stands where the frozen reach of…","sort":287500,"sourceJournal":"Holy Empire of Runvegr"},{"name":"Miskunnkvama","category":"Places","group":"Holy Empire of Runvegr","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"miskunnkvama","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Miskunnkvama.png","tags":["City","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Runvegr","subtitle":"Mountain gate-fortress of southern Runvegr","meta":[{"label":"Population","value":"~38,000"},{"label":"Area","value":"18 square miles"},{"label":"Government","value":"Military-Theocratic Border Governorship"},{"label":"Demonym","value":"Miskunnkvaman"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"Imperial Gatewarden of Miskunnkvama"},{"label":"Founded","value":"Early Post-Divergence Era"}],"lists":[{"label":"Notable Locations","items":[{"name":"The Iron-Stone Gates","description":"Massive gates capable of sealing the mountain pass completely."},{"name":"The Upper Watchtowers","description":"High towers overlooking the Grarfold Mounts, the Ember approach, and the pass roads."},{"name":"The Gatewarden’s Hold","description":"Administrative and military seat of the city’s ruling commander."},{"name":"Dragoon Barracks","description":"Military quarters and training terraces for Dragoon detachments stationed at the border.","icon":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Groups-Dragoons.webp"},{"name":"Tesseris Tower","description":"The Tesseris Headquarters for the border city","icon":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Groups-Tesseris.webp"},{"name":"The Pass Market","description":"A vital trade hub where Runvegrian goods meet wares from the Ember Hinterlands and beyond."},{"name":"The Frosthearth Lodge","description":"A well-known inn in the mid-tier levels near the main market square, popular with travelers, soldiers, guides, and couriers."},{"name":"The Emberward Road","description":"The guarded route leading south toward the Ember Hinterlands."},{"name":"The Grarfold Mounts","description":"The surrounding mountain range, full of hidden valleys, ancient magic, and dangerous legends."}]}],"content":"<p>Miskunnkvama, the gateway to the frozen heart of Runvegr, perches precariously within the imposing Grarfold Mounts, serving as both bastion and bridge between the icy empire and the fiery expanse of the Ember Hinterlands. This border city, carved from the very stone of the mountains it inhabits, is a testament to the architectural prowess and strategic genius of the Runvegrian people. Its location, chosen for both its defensibility and its rarity as a passable route through the treacherous mountain range, underscores its importance as a key to the empire’s seclusion and security.</p><p>The city itself is a marvel of engineering and magical construction, with buildings that cling to the mountain sides and tunnels that burrow deep into the earth. The architecture blends so seamlessly with the natural environment that from a distance, Miskunnkvama appears to be just another part of the mountain range. Its streets and pathways wind tightly up the mountainside, flanked by stone homes with roofs weighted against the heavy snows and fortified structures that house the city's garrison and supplies.</p><p>Miskunnkvama’s strategic significance cannot be overstated. It is here that the Tesseris mages and the Holy Order of Dragoons maintain a vigilant watch, guarding the empire against intrusion from the Ember Hinterlands and beyond. The city’s defenses are formidable, with watchtowers that offer an unobstructed view of the surrounding landscape and magical wards that protect against both physical and arcane threats. The city's gates, massive constructs of iron and stone, are capable of sealing Miskunnkvama off completely, making it an impregnable fortress against would-be invaders.</p><p>Despite its martial focus, Miskunnkvama is not devoid of life or culture. The city serves as a vital trading post, where goods from within the empire are exchanged with those from the Ember Hinterlands and beyond. Markets filled with exotic goods from distant lands nestle alongside taverns and inns where travelers and soldiers share tales over warm hearths. The citizens of Miskunnkvama, though few, are a hardy and resilient folk, accustomed to the harshness of their environment and proud of their role as the guardians of Runvegr’s gateway.</p><p>The Grarfold Mounts themselves add to the city’s mystique, with their towering peaks and hidden valleys teeming with legends of ancient magic and hidden treasures. Adventurers and scholars are drawn to Miskunnkvama not only as a waypoint on their journey but also in search of the mysteries that the mountains hold.</p><p>Yet, life in Miskunnkvama is not without its challenges. The city, with its harsh climate and isolation, requires a level of self-sufficiency that is painstakingly maintained by its inhabitants. Supplies are carefully rationed, and the people must work together to ensure their survival against the elements and the potential threats that lurk beyond their walls.</p><p>Miskunnkvama stands as a symbol of Runvegr’s strength and determination, a city that defies the elements and serves as a steadfast guardian of the empire’s borders. Its presence in the Grarfold Mounts is a constant reminder of the balance between isolation and connection, between the wildness of the untamed lands beyond and the order of the empire it protects.</p>","summary":"Miskunnkvama, the gateway to the frozen heart of Runvegr, perches precariously within the imposing Grarfold Mounts, serving as both bastion and bridge between the icy empire and the fiery expanse of the Ember…","sort":300000,"sourceJournal":"Holy Empire of Runvegr"},{"name":"Norvbay","category":"Places","group":"Holy Empire of Runvegr","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"norvbay","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Norvbay.webp","tags":["Lake","Western Eilune","Pagallvolr"],"mainTag":"Runvegr","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Norvbay is renowned across Eilune for its ethereal beauty, especially during the frigid winter months when the bay freezes over, creating a vast expanse of glittering ice that seems to stretch on forever. The ice itself takes on a bluish hue, reflecting the pale light of the sun that barely rises above the horizon in these northern reaches.</p><p>Legend has it that Norvbay is home to the spirit of an ancient ice giant, whose presence is said to be the reason for the bay's perpetual cold. Some believe that the giant slumbers beneath the ice, and that its dreams are what cause the eerie, haunting melodies that sometimes echo across the frozen expanse. It should be noted there is no evidence behind this myth.</p><p>Despite its otherworldly beauty, Norvbay is also a place of danger. The ice can be treacherous, with hidden crevasses and shifting plates that can trap the unwary traveler. Stories abound of ships that ventured too close to the ice floes and were crushed, their crews lost to the icy depths.</p><p>Despite the risks, Norvbay is also a place of opportunity. The waters beneath the ice are teeming with life, from schools of fish that thrive in the cold depths to the occasional sighting of a massive ice kraken, a legendary creature said to be able to pull entire ships beneath the waves.</p><p>The settlement near Norvbay, Pagallvolr, is a rugged outpost, populated by fishermen, traders, and adventurers drawn by the promise of riches and the allure of the unknown. The people here are hardy and resourceful, accustomed to the harshness of their environment and the mysteries that lurk beneath the ice.</p>","summary":"Norvbay is renowned across Eilune for its ethereal beauty, especially during the frigid winter months when the bay freezes over, creating a vast expanse of glittering ice that seems to stretch on forever. The ice itself…","sort":475000,"sourceJournal":"Holy Empire of Runvegr"},{"name":"Norvdrant Plains","category":"Places","group":"Holy Empire of Runvegr","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"norvdrant-plains","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-NorvdrantPlains.webp","tags":["Wildnerness","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Runvegr","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>The Norvdrant Plains, situated in the northern reaches of Runvegr, are a vast and desolate expanse of ice and snow that stretches from coast to coast. Locked in perpetual winter, the landscape is cloaked in a pristine blanket of white, broken only by jagged outcroppings of rock and the occasional cluster of hardy shrubs and stunted trees.</p><p>Above, the sky dances with the ethereal glow of the aurora borealis, painting ribbons of vibrant color across the horizon in a mesmerizing display of light and motion. The ever-shifting hues of green, blue, and purple cast an otherworldly glow over the icy landscape below, lending an air of magic and mystery to the frozen plains.</p><p>Nestled amidst this frozen wilderness lies the city of Obygoheimr, a bastion of civilization in an otherwise inhospitable land. Located at the southern edge of the Norvdrant Plains, Obygoheimr serves as the last major outpost before the icy expanse consumes the landscape. Despite the harsh conditions, the city thrives, its sturdy buildings and stout walls standing as a testament to the resilience of its inhabitants.</p><p>Further north, along the frozen coastline, lies the remote settlement of Yfirjord, known colloquially as the \"top of the world.\" Perched on the edge of the continent, Yfirjord is battered by frigid winds and buffeted by crashing waves, yet its inhabitants endure, eking out a living amidst the unforgiving landscape.</p><p>The Norvdrant Plains themselves are a land of rugged beauty and treacherous terrain. Glacial valleys and frozen rivers crisscross the landscape, while towering mountains loom in the distance, their peaks perpetually capped with snow. Despite the harshness of the environment, the plains teem with life, from hardy tundra animals to ice and snow-aspected predators and magical creatures that roam the icy wastes.</p><p>For those brave enough to venture into its frozen depths, the Norvdrant Plains offer untold opportunities for exploration and discovery. From ancient ruins buried beneath the ice to hidden caves and caverns waiting to be explored, the frozen wilderness holds secrets that few have dared to uncover.</p><p>But amidst the beauty and danger of the Norvdrant Plains, one thing remains constant: the unyielding spirit of those who call this frozen land home. Whether battling the elements or charting new paths across the ice, the people of Runvegr are bound by a shared determination to thrive in the face of adversity, no matter how cold the world may become.</p>","summary":"The Norvdrant Plains, situated in the northern reaches of Runvegr, are a vast and desolate expanse of ice and snow that stretches from coast to coast. Locked in perpetual winter, the landscape is cloaked in a pristine…","sort":650000,"sourceJournal":"Holy Empire of Runvegr"},{"name":"Obygoheimr","category":"Places","group":"Holy Empire of Runvegr","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"obygoheimr","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Obygoheimr.webp","tags":["City","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Runvegr","subtitle":"Hunter’s city of the Norvdrant wilds","meta":[{"label":"Population","value":"~22,000"},{"label":"Area","value":"11 square miles"},{"label":"Government","value":"Mayoral Settlement under Limited Imperial Oversight"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"Mayor Tobias Jenks"}],"lists":[{"label":"Notable Locations","items":[{"name":"Mountain Ram Inn","description":"The largest structure in town and one of its few wooden buildings, marked by a carved ram’s-head shingle above wide double doors."},{"name":"Benedict’s Baubles","description":"Tall, narrow general store run by Tindra Falusial, stocked with supplies for miners, townsfolk, hunters, and adventurers."},{"name":"Ulfgar’s Smithy","description":"Classic smithy run by Ulfgar Bronzeaxe, serving hunters, miners, guards, and travelers."},{"name":"Obygoheimr Constabulary","description":"Local law office led by Chief Inspector Talli Hammersmith."},{"name":"Mayor’s Hall","description":"Civic seat of Mayor Tobias Jenks and the settlement’s local administration."},{"name":"The Tesseris Outpost","description":"Small imperial-mage presence tolerated more than embraced by the locals, newly formed and growing."},{"name":"The Ravine Edge","description":"Dangerous ice-riven chasmlands where hunters vanish and vril-shards are sometimes found."},{"name":"Norvdrant Plains","description":"The vast wilderness surrounding Obygoheimr, beautiful, cruel, and dangerous."}]}],"content":"<p>Few cities one test the traveler's resolve quite like Obygoheimr: to approach it is to feel the world fall away behind you. The wind grows sharper, the sky grows wider, and the plains of Norvdrant stretch so far and so pale that the horizon seems to dissolve into the very bones of the world.</p><p>Obygoheimr sits on the southern lip of an ancient glacial rise, overlooking ravines carved in ages none now remember. The settlement does not rise proudly as Horgrknottr does, nor does it gleam with carved accuracy like the mountain cities of the south. Instead, it crouches low against the endless cold, built in a manner that speaks not of pride but of survival. Roofs slope steeply beneath heavy shingles, walls are reinforced with stone and packed snow, and smoke escapes in thin, disciplined ribbons from the longhouses, as if reluctant to draw attention to the life below.</p><p>They call it \"Wilderness Land\", and the name is no embellishment.</p><p>Obygoheimr is a hunter's city first and last. Everything here bends to the rhythm of the chase. The air perpetually carries the scent of treated hides, tanned leather, and the sharp tang of northern pine. Pelts hang from doorways like banners. Antlers mark thresholds. Even the children carry carving knives with the quiet familiarity of those raised to respect both the land and its dangers.</p><p>To live here is to accept the plains as your master. The Norvdrant Plains that surround the city are beautiful in their cruelty. The land rolls in long, windswept stretches, interrupted only by the jagged mouths of ice-riven chasms — some wide enough to swallow entire caravans. Travelers speak of these ravines with reverence and fear. Many claim they are haunted, not by spirits but by echoes of the storms that raged here during the old vrilic upheavals. On still nights, it is said one can hear faint murmurs rising from their depths, as though the land itself remembers what transpired.</p><p>Obygoheimr thrives by trading the treasures the plains yield to those bold enough to take them. Pelts, meat, bonecraft, and the rare vril-shards collected from the ravine edges feed the Frostmarket, a bustling square that swells each season with traders from the west and envoys from Horgrknottr. Yet for all its commerce, the city remains humble and wary. Outsiders often remark that the people here wear expressions that read like sharpened flint, not hostile, but honed by necessity.</p><p>It is said that every soul in Obygoheimr, young or old, swears the Hunter's Oath, a vow to respect the creatures of the plains and take only what is needed. The spirits of the land are honored quietly, without pomp: a carved bone charm tucked above a doorway, an offering of meat left on a frozen cliff, a whispered prayer to Erov, Slaine, or Bran before a hunt.</p><p>Though the Tesseris maintain a small outpost here, they hold far less sway than in the southern cities. The wilderness does not bow easily to authority. Their presence is tolerated, perhaps even appreciated during harsh winters, but they remain outsiders in a place that yields its secrets only to those willing to bleed for them.</p><p>Yet Obygoheimr is not defined solely by danger. There is a stark beauty here, a sense of communion between people and land. When the auroras unfurl across the sky like rivers of light, and the snow hushes the world into stillness, one can almost believe the city exists outside the boundaries of time, a place unchanged since the first hunter walked these frozen plains.</p><p>Still, the land whispers its warnings. Hunters vanish in the ravines. Strange frost patterns appear where none should. And in the far north, beyond the reach of even the bravest caravans, nomadic clans report glimmers of blue fire carried on the wind.</p>","summary":"Few cities one test the traveler's resolve quite like Obygoheimr: to approach it is to feel the world fall away behind you. The wind grows sharper, the sky grows wider, and the plains of Norvdrant stretch so far and so…","sort":850000,"sourceJournal":"Holy Empire of Runvegr"},{"name":"Pagallvolr","category":"Places","group":"Holy Empire of Runvegr","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"pagallvolr","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Pagallvolr.webp","tags":["City","Norvbay","Western Eilune","Jaako"],"mainTag":"Runvegr","subtitle":"A hardy coastal settlement between mountain and ice, where fishermen, traders, travelers, and festival-goers gather beside the treacherous blue expanse of Norvbay.","meta":[{"label":"Population","value":"~16,000"},{"label":"Area","value":"7 square miles"},{"label":"Government","value":"Local Harbor Council under Imperial Oversight"},{"label":"Demonym","value":"Pagallvolrian"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"Harbor Warden of Pagallvolr"}],"lists":[{"label":"Notable Locations","items":[{"name":"Jaako’s Homestead","description":"A family home in Pagallvolr, tied to Jaako Jormungandr’s past and return."},{"name":"Norvbay","description":"Vast frozen lake-bay beside the city, beautiful, dangerous, fish-rich, and wrapped in local myth."},{"name":"The Frozen Docks","description":"Icebound lakeside docks, sled platforms, mooring posts, and fish-hauling stations."},{"name":"The Fish Market","description":"Busy market district filled with dried fish, fresh catches, spices, traders, and gossip."},{"name":"The Smokehouses","description":"Long wooden sheds where fish are preserved for winter and trade."},{"name":"The Boatwright Yards","description":"Workshops repairing fishing boats, ice-skiffs, sleds, nets, and bay gear."}]}],"content":"<p>Pagallvolr, nestled between the towering mountains and the frozen bay, presents a rugged and picturesque scene. The settlement is a patchwork of wooden buildings, their roofs laden with snow in the colder months. Despite its humble appearance, Pagallvolr boasts a lively atmosphere, especially during its numerous festivals.</p><p>The people of Pagallvolr are known for their resilience and warmth, traits forged by the harsh environment they call home. They are hardworking and resourceful, making the most of their surroundings. Fishing is a way of life here, and the waters of Norvbay provide an abundance of fish, sustaining the community through the long winters.</p><p>One of the most notable aspects of Pagallvolr is its bustling marketplace. Here, traders from distant lands mingle with locals, exchanging goods and stories. The air is filled with the aroma of dried fish, spices, and the sound of lively chatter.</p><p>The festivals in Pagallvolr are a sight to behold. The Fishing Festival, held at the beginning of the fishing season, is a time of great celebration. Fishermen compete to catch the largest fish, while others showcase their skills in boat races. In the evening, the town square comes alive with music and dancing, as locals and visitors alike join in the revelry.</p><p>Despite its remote location, Pagallvolr is a welcoming place for travelers. The locals are always eager to share their customs and stories with newcomers, making it a memorable stop for anyone journeying through northern Runvegr.</p>","summary":"Pagallvolr, nestled between the towering mountains and the frozen bay, presents a rugged and picturesque scene. The settlement is a patchwork of wooden buildings, their roofs laden with snow in the colder months.…","sort":950000,"sourceJournal":"Holy Empire of Runvegr"},{"name":"Sólhöll","category":"Places","group":"Holy Empire of Runvegr","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"s-lh-ll","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Solholl.webp","tags":["Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Runvegr","subtitle":"Sólhöll, the Summer Palace of the Last Sun","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Once known as the summer palace of northern Runvegr, Solhöll was built in the age before the Divergence, when the Norvdrant Plains were not yet locked beneath ice and snow. In those days, the land was temperate and green during the brief northern summers, with long golden evenings, windswept grasslands, flowering shrubs, and clear rivers running down from the distant mountains.</p><p>The palace served as a seasonal residence for Runvegr’s old rulers and honored guests, a place of retreat far from the pressures of the capital. Its halls were designed to catch the low summer sun, with high windows, open terraces, carved pillars, and sun motifs worked into stone and timber. Feasts, councils, hunts, and royal ceremonies were once held there beneath bright skies.</p><p>When the Divergence came, the northern plains changed almost overnight. Warm earth froze, rivers hardened, and the summer palace became a monument to a season that no longer existed. Solhöll was eventually abandoned, too remote and too costly to maintain in the new frozen world.</p><p>Now it stands alone upon its hill in the Norvdrant Plains, half-buried in snow and watched over by the aurora. Its name remains bitterly ironic: <strong>Sun Hall</strong>, a palace built for warmth, now preserved in endless winter. Beneath its forgotten foundations, darker secrets wait.</p>","summary":"Once known as the summer palace of northern Runvegr, Solhöll was built in the age before the Divergence, when the Norvdrant Plains were not yet locked beneath ice and snow. In those days, the land was temperate and…","sort":1150000,"sourceJournal":"Holy Empire of Runvegr"},{"name":"Stenmark","category":"Places","group":"Holy Empire of Runvegr","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"stenmark","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Stenmark.webp","tags":["City","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Runvegr","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Stenmark is a modest riverside settlement known for its sturdy stone bridges, fishing docks, and the distinctive basalt stones that line the riverbanks. The village primarily supports the capital’s grain and fish markets, with small, water-driven mills that grind flour from grain transported downstream. The villagers celebrate the annual Riverwake Festival, honoring Erov for safe waters and bountiful catches.</p>","summary":"Stenmark is a modest riverside settlement known for its sturdy stone bridges, fishing docks, and the distinctive basalt stones that line the riverbanks. The village primarily supports the capital’s grain and fish…","sort":1250000,"sourceJournal":"Holy Empire of Runvegr"},{"name":"Ushana Dynasty","category":"Places","group":"Ushana Dynasty","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"ushana-dynasty","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/StainedGlass-Ushana.webp","tags":["Nation","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Ushana","subtitle":"Prosperous desert dynasty of trade, spectacle, and sacred law","meta":[{"label":"Population","value":"~4.8 million"},{"label":"Area","value":"85,000 square miles"},{"label":"Government","value":"Dynastic Monarchy"},{"label":"Demonym","value":"Ushanan"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"Sultana Nyla Aramvek"},{"label":"Founded","value":"c. 25–75 PD (Modern Dynasty)"}],"lists":[{"label":"Neighbor Regions","items":[{"tag":"Wisivashu"},{"tag":"Holy Empire of Runvegr"},{"tag":"Ember Hinterlands"}]}],"content":"<p>Ushana, a jewel of wealth and opulence amidst the harshness of sunbaked deserts, stands as a beacon to those drawn by the allure of fortune from across the continents of Eilune. Its capital, Easternesse, a city of splendor and vice, pulses with the lifeblood of commerce, entertainment, and ambition. Here, in the heart of Ushana, the grandeur of fighting arenas, the enchantment of dancer revues, and the thrill of gambling halls beckon visitors into a world where leisure and luxury intertwine.</p><p>The twin Traders, deities of commerce and cunning, are revered above all in Ushana. Their influence permeates every transaction and negotiation, their statues gracing the marketplaces and their symbols etched into the coins that flow like rivers through the hands of the populace. The Dynasty of Ushana, under the guidance of these celestial patrons, has cultivated a society that worships wealth and the pursuit thereof.</p><p>The Sultana of Ushana, a figure of elegance and power, presides over this vast empire from Easternesse, her authority extending across the sands to the distant city of Westernesse. Here, across the vast Sea of Dust, lie the breeding grounds of the dust whales, majestic creatures whose very essence contributes to Ushana's prosperity. The extraction of valuable resources from these gentle giants has bolstered the nation's economy, making Ushana a pivotal trade hub in the region.</p><p>However, the heartbeat of Ushana's wealth lies not only in its mineral riches but also in its renowned clothcrafting industry. Artisans of unparalleled skill weave fabrics that are sought after across the world, their creations a testament to the nation's refined culture and artistic heritage. This industry, alongside the treasures drawn from the earth and sea, cements Ushana's status as the wealthiest of nations.</p><p>Despite its affluence, Ushana faces internal strife and the specter of division. The Sultana's second regent governs the fertile lands of Bern, a vital oasis in a realm otherwise surrendered to the desert. Rumblings of secession from this verdant province threaten the stability of the Dynasty, with fears of resulting starvation and exacerbated water scarcity looming large over the nation's future.</p><p>The transformation of Ushana from a lush marshland to a desolate desert wasteland during the Divergence left deep scars on the land. Tour-of-the-Kings, the once-mighty capital, now lies in ruins, a haunting monument to the past. The surrounding lands are stalked by darkangels, fearsome undead predators that prey upon the living, adding a layer of peril to the already daunting landscape.</p><p>Yet, amidst these challenges, Ushana thrives, a testament to the resilience of its people and the enduring allure of wealth. The Sultana's rule, guided by the wisdom of the twin Traders, seeks to navigate the complexities of power, prosperity, and unity, striving to uphold the glory of Ushana against the backdrop of an ever-changing world. The nation, with its juxtaposition of opulence and adversity, remains a land of endless possibilities, where fortunes are made and destinies are forged under the relentless sun.</p>","summary":"Ushana, a jewel of wealth and opulence amidst the harshness of sunbaked deserts, stands as a beacon to those drawn by the allure of fortune from across the continents of Eilune. Its capital, Easternesse, a city of…","sort":100000,"sourceJournal":"Ushana Dynasty"},{"name":"Bern","category":"Places","group":"Ushana Dynasty","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"bern","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Bern.webp","tags":["City","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Ushana","subtitle":"Verdant breadbasket of the Ushanan Dynasty","meta":[{"label":"Population","value":"~190,000"},{"label":"Area","value":"74 square miles"},{"label":"Government","value":"Sultanic Regency with Autonomist Tensions"},{"label":"Demonym","value":"Bernish"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"Regent Torvald Kaltsson"},{"label":"Founded","value":"Early Post-Divergence Era"}],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Bern, the verdant jewel of Ushana, is a stark contrast to the sprawling deserts and dust seas that define much of the nation. Situated in a rare pocket of fertility, Bern is the only remaining truly fertile ground in Ushana, a vital oasis in a land transformed by the Divergence into an endless expanse of desert. This lush territory, replete with rolling hills, a nearby lake of clean and fresh water, and abundant vegetation, serves as the lifeline for Ushana, providing essential resources that sustain both the population and the economy.</p><p>The city of Bern, at the heart of this fertile land, is a testament to the resilience and adaptability of its people. Here, the ancient and the modern merge seamlessly, with traditional agriculture coexisting with innovative water conservation techniques and crop management practices. The architecture reflects this blend of the old and new, with buildings constructed from local materials designed to maximize natural cooling, surrounded by gardens and orchards that stretch as far as the eye can see.</p><p>Bern's economy thrives on its agricultural output, renowned across Eilune for producing a bounty of grains, fruits, and vegetables, as well as for its livestock. The city's markets are a riot of color and activity, where traders from across the continent come to purchase Bern's produce, ensuring that the city's wealth is not solely based on its agricultural prowess but also on its strategic position as a trade hub.</p><p>Water, in Bern, is more precious than gold. Ingenious systems of aqueducts and water storage ensure that every drop is used to its fullest potential, supporting both the city's needs and its agricultural endeavors. These technologies, developed and refined over generations, are a source of pride for Bern's inhabitants and are guarded jealously against those who would seek to exploit them.</p><p>Despite its prosperity, Bern is a land of contrasts. The city's success and strategic importance have not gone unnoticed, stirring envy and desire among neighboring states and within Ushana itself. Rumblings of secession have begun to disturb the peace, fueled by fears of over-exploitation and the desire for greater autonomy. The city's position as the breadbasket of Ushana places it at the center of political maneuverings, with the Sultana's second regent holding the delicate task of navigating these treacherous waters, balancing the city's needs and contributions against the broader aspirations of the Ushanan Dynasty.</p><p>The cultural life of Bern is as rich and varied as its agriculture. Festivals celebrating the harvest and the changing seasons are major events, drawing visitors from across Ushana and beyond. The people of Bern are known for their warmth and hospitality, with a deep-seated respect for the land that sustains them. Music, dance, and storytelling are integral to Bern's cultural identity, with traditions passed down through generations that speak to the city's history and hopes for the future.</p><p>Yet, beneath its idyllic surface, Bern faces challenges that threaten its very existence. The specter of water scarcity looms large, a constant reminder of the precarious balance between nature and human needs. The threat of secession, driven by fears of resource control and political autonomy, adds to the city's woes, creating a sense of unease that pervades even the most bountiful harvests.</p><p>Bern stands as a symbol of life in the midst of desolation, a reminder of what was lost in the Divergence and what can still be saved. It is a city of contradictions, where prosperity and peril walk hand in hand, and the fate of Ushana hangs in the balance.</p>","summary":"Bern, the verdant jewel of Ushana, is a stark contrast to the sprawling deserts and dust seas that define much of the nation. Situated in a rare pocket of fertility, Bern is the only remaining truly fertile ground in…","sort":275000,"sourceJournal":"Ushana Dynasty"},{"name":"Easternesse","category":"Places","group":"Ushana Dynasty","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"easternesse","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Easternesse.webp","tags":["City","Capital","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Ushana","subtitle":"Radiant desert capital of the Ushanan Dynasty","meta":[{"label":"Population","value":"~720,000"},{"label":"Area","value":"92 square miles"},{"label":"Government","value":"Sultanic Dynastic Capital"},{"label":"Demonym","value":"Easternessian"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"Sultana Nyla Aramvek"},{"label":"Founded","value":"Early Post-Divergence Era"}],"lists":[{"label":"Notable Locations","items":[{"name":"The Sultana’s Palace","description":"Towering seat of dynastic rule, elegance, administration, and court intrigue."},{"name":"Gemflow Market District","description":"Easternesse’s major market district, full of food stalls, artisans, exotic goods, magical curiosities, and constant commerce."},{"name":"Sandshine Quarter","description":"The city’s largest entertainment district, known for dancer revues, taverns, theaters, inns, casinos, and spectacle."},{"name":"Azure Palace","description":"Opulent casino and performance complex occupying an entire city block in Sandshine Quarter."},{"name":"The Fighting Arenas","description":"Sand-and-stone coliseums hosting gladiatorial bouts, magical contests, beasts, and public spectacle."},{"name":"The Traders’ Courts","description":"Legal and ritual courts where commercial disputes are judged by priests of the Twin Traders."},{"name":"Eternal Lampways District","description":"Major streets lit through the night by enchanted lamps, giving the capital its ceaseless glow."},{"name":"Glass-Bright Districts","description":"Wealthy streets of stained glass, colored awnings, perfumed fountains, and polished stone."}]}],"content":"<p>Easternesse, the radiant capital of Ushana, rises from the desert like a mirage made manifest, a city of opulence and intrigue that stands as the heart of the wealthiest nation across Eilune. This bustling metropolis, under the ever-watchful eye of the Sultana, is a nexus of commerce, culture, and entertainment, where the dreams of fortune-seekers converge with the realities of desert life.</p><p>The city's architecture is a testament to Ushanan affluence, with buildings crafted from sun-baked brick and gleaming stained glass, reflecting the golden hues of the desert and the vibrant colors of the sky at dawn and dusk. The streets are laid out in a sprawling maze that teems with life at all hours, thanks to the eternally lit lamps that bathes the city in a never-ending glow. Marketplaces buzz with activity, offering goods from across the known world: spices that tickle the senses, fabrics soft as a whisper and rich in color, and artifacts imbued with the magic of distant lands.</p><p>At the heart of Easternesse's allure are its famed recreational venues, which draw visitors from every corner of Eilune. The fighting arenas, vast coliseums of sand and stone, host battles that range from gladiatorial combats to contests of magical prowess, thrilling spectators with displays of skill, strength, and sorcery. Dancer revues, held in opulent theaters adorned with silks and chandeliers, captivate audiences with performances that tell stories of love, adventure, and the mysteries of the desert. Gambling halls, meanwhile, offer a different kind of entertainment, where fortunes are won and lost over cards and dice, and every game is a dance with fate.</p><p>The worship of the twin Traders permeates every aspect of life in Easternesse. Shrines dedicated to these deities of commerce and cunning can be found at every marketplace and trading post, where merchants and buyers alike offer prayers and tributes in hope of favorable deals and prosperous ventures. The influence of the twin Traders is also evident in the city's robust economy, where trade agreements are sealed with ritualistic ceremonies and disputes are settled in courts presided over by priests of the twin deities.</p><p>Despite its grandeur, Easternesse is not without its shadows. The pursuit of wealth and power has bred a complex web of alliances and rivalries among the city's elite, with merchant princes, influential families, and ambitious adventurers all vying for influence within the opulent courts of the Sultana. The underbelly of the city harbors its own secrets, where thieves' guilds and clandestine societies operate in the margins, seeking to turn the tides of fortune in their favor through less savory means.</p><p>The Sultana herself, a figure of unparalleled elegance and authority, oversees this intricate tapestry of desert life from her palace, a marvel of architecture that towers over the cityscape. Her rule is marked by both benevolence and iron will, guiding Easternesse through times of prosperity and peril alike.</p><p>Easternesse, in all its complexity and contrast, stands as a jewel in the desert, a city where every street holds a promise, every shadow tells a story, and the dance of destiny plays out beneath an unchanging sky. It is a place of endless opportunity, where the bold may rise to unimaginable heights, and the sands of time continue to shift in the endless dance of the desert.</p>","summary":"Easternesse, the radiant capital of Ushana, rises from the desert like a mirage made manifest, a city of opulence and intrigue that stands as the heart of the wealthiest nation across Eilune. This bustling metropolis,…","sort":337500,"sourceJournal":"Ushana Dynasty"},{"name":"Sea of Dust","category":"Places","group":"Ushana Dynasty","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"sea-of-dust","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-SeaofDust.webp","tags":["Wilderness","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Ushana","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>The Sea of Dust, a mesmerizing expanse that lies at the heart of Ushana's desolate beauty, serves as a vivid reminder of the world's capacity for change. Transformed from a vast lake stretching across the continent into an endless desert sea during the cataclysmic events of the Divergence, its sands shift in hues of blues and violets under the relentless sun, creating a landscape both haunting and breathtaking. This unique terrain, composed of sand so fine and pervasive, poses a danger to the unwary, capable of engulfing the unfortunate much like the waters of the old world.</p><p>Orm, steadfast in its identity as a port city despite the world-altering events of the Divergence, stands as a beacon of adaptability and resilience. The city's ingenious inhabitants, refusing to surrender their maritime heritage to the whims of fate, reimagined their vessels and their livelihoods to thrive upon the dust. The sleek skiffs and grand galleons of Orm, now gliding effortlessly over the sea of dust, are a testament to Ushanan ingenuity, turning what many saw as a disaster into a new beginning.</p><p>The Sea of Dust, though it may seem a barren wasteland at first glance, teems with life peculiar to its conditions. Dustwhales, majestic creatures of the deep, traverse its expanses, their silhouettes occasionally breaking the surface in breathtaking displays. Fishermen, their techniques refined for this new world, cast their nets for dustshrimp, a staple that continues the tradition of harvest from the sea. It is a stark reminder that life, in all its forms, finds a way to endure and adapt.</p><p>The most coveted treasure of the Sea of Dust is undoubtedly ambergris. This rare substance, with its miraculous properties, is the heart of Ushana's prosperity. Said to cure any ailment and turn even the most mundane meal into a culinary delight, ambergris has become a symbol of wealth and wellbeing across Eilune. Its value is so great that its trade is strictly controlled within Ushanan cities, with regulations in place to prevent exploitation and ensure that the benefits of this precious commodity are shared by all.</p><p>The trade of ambergris has also woven a complex tapestry of diplomacy and economics throughout the region. Caravans braving the deserts and ships navigating the perilous routes between cities carry this treasure, binding the cities of Ushana and beyond in a network of mutual dependence and shared destiny. The pursuit of ambergris has led to alliances forged and conflicts ignited, as nations vie for control over this source of power and prosperity.</p>","summary":"The Sea of Dust, a mesmerizing expanse that lies at the heart of Ushana's desolate beauty, serves as a vivid reminder of the world's capacity for change. Transformed from a vast lake stretching across the continent into…","sort":400000,"sourceJournal":"Ushana Dynasty"},{"name":"Orm","category":"Places","group":"Ushana Dynasty","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"orm","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Orm.png","tags":["City","Border City","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Ushana","subtitle":"Dust-sea port of old Ushana","meta":[{"label":"Population","value":"~118,000"},{"label":"Area","value":"36 square miles"},{"label":"Government","value":"Chartered Port Governorship"},{"label":"Demonym","value":"Ormish"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"Harbormaster-Governor of Orm"},{"label":"Founded","value":"Pre-Divergence; rechartered after the Sea of Dust formed"}],"lists":[{"label":"Notable Locations","items":[{"name":"The Dust Docks","description":"Former waterfront docks now used by dust skiffs, sand galleons, expedition crews, and trade vessels."},{"name":"The Ambergris Exchange","description":"Wealthy trade house where precious dust-sea ambergris is weighed, auctioned, taxed, and exported."},{"name":"The Dustshrimp Market","description":"Lively food and trade market specializing in dustshrimp, preserved goods, spices, and expedition supplies."},{"name":"The Dewroof Cisterns","description":"Rooftop and underground water-collection system that helps the city survive dust storms and drought."},{"name":"The Sandglass Customs House","description":"Administrative port office inspecting goods, collecting duties, and registering expeditions."},{"name":"The Old Tide Shrine","description":"Former water shrine adapted into a place of prayer for dust sailors, traders, and storm-survivors."},{"name":"The Sea of Dust","description":"Vast desert of shifting sands that replaced the old lake during the Divergence."}]}],"content":"<p>Orm, standing resilient on the northern edge of the Sea of Dust, epitomizes the spirit of adaptation and survival. Before the Divergence, it was celebrated as a bustling port town, its docks teeming with vessels as the gateway to lower Ushana, its markets a kaleidoscope of cultures and commodities. However, when the Divergence transformed the vast lake into a desert of shifting sands, Orm faced an existential crisis that threatened to erase its identity and prosperity. Yet, far from succumbing to despair, the city reinvented itself, emerging as a unique maritime community in a world where the traditional meaning of \"sea\" no longer applied.</p><p>The architecture of Orm reflects its maritime heritage and its adaptation to the new conditions. Buildings that once looked out over water now face the vast expanse of dust, their designs incorporating both traditional maritime elements and adaptations to the desert environment. Rooftops are fashioned to collect dew and funnel it into underground cisterns, while walls are built high and thick to shield from dust storms. The city's layout, with its winding streets leading to what used to be the waterfront, now terminates at docks where dust skiffs and galleons are moored, ready to sail out into the Sea of Dust.</p><p>Orm's shipbuilders, once renowned for their waterfaring vessels, have become pioneers in the design and construction of ships capable of navigating the dust seas. These new skiffs and galleons, with their wide, flat bottoms and sails designed to catch the desert winds, are marvels of engineering, enabling Orm to maintain its status as a crucial trade hub. The shipyards of Orm are always abuzz with activity, as craftsmen and engineers work side by side, blending traditional skills with new knowledge to create vessels that are both practical and beautiful.</p><p>The economy of Orm has evolved to capitalize on its unique position. The city has become the primary departure point for expeditions into the Sea of Dust, whether for trade, exploration, or the harvesting of dustshrimp and ambergris. The latter, in particular, has brought immense wealth to Orm, as the city controls a significant portion of the trade in this precious substance. Markets in Orm are vibrant places where the treasures of the dust sea are bought and sold, alongside goods from across Eilune, making the city a melting pot of cultures and a center of commerce.</p><p>Despite the challenges posed by its environment, Orm has not lost its sense of community and identity. Festivals and celebrations, many of them holdovers from its days as a waterborne port, are frequent and lively, with music, dancing, and storytelling that recount the history of the city and its people's journey through adversity. The citizens of Orm are a testament to Ushanan resilience, proud of their heritage and their unique way of life in a world transformed.</p><p>Orm's relationship with the surrounding cities, particularly those within Ushana, is complex and multifaceted. As a vital economic hub, it plays a crucial role in the prosperity of the region, yet its strategic position also makes it a focal point in the geopolitical dynamics of the area. The city's leaders navigate these waters with a blend of diplomacy and shrewdness, ensuring Orm's continued prosperity and independence.</p><p>In the shifting sands of the Sea of Dust, Orm stands as a beacon of ingenuity and adaptability, a city that has not only survived the upheaval of the Divergence but has thrived, crafting a new identity and future from the very sands that sought to bury it.</p>","summary":"Orm, standing resilient on the northern edge of the Sea of Dust, epitomizes the spirit of adaptation and survival. Before the Divergence, it was celebrated as a bustling port town, its docks teeming with vessels as the…","sort":450000,"sourceJournal":"Ushana Dynasty"},{"name":"Tour-of-the-Kings","category":"Places","group":"Ushana Dynasty","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"tour-of-the-kings","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-TouroftheKings.webp","tags":["Ruins","City","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Ushana","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Tour-of-the-Kings, once the crowning glory of a bygone era, now lies in silent ruin, a poignant testament to the transience of power and the ravages of time. Situated within the heart of what is now Ushana's desert expanse, it was a city of unparalleled splendor, where the monarchs of old would gather to discuss the fate of the land, forge alliances, and celebrate their victories. Its majestic palaces, vast libraries, and opulent temples were marvels of architecture and centers of learning and culture, drawing scholars, artists, and dignitaries from distant corners of the world.</p><p>However, the Divergence heralded the end of this once-great capital. As Ushana was stripped of its natural water sources, the lifeblood of Tour-of-the-Kings dried up, leaving its fields barren and its rivers beds mere memories etched into the parched earth. The desert claimed the city, burying its grandeur under shifting sands, leaving only ghosts to roam its abandoned halls.</p><p>Today, the ruins of Tour-of-the-Kings stand as a haunting landscape of broken columns, crumbling facades, and doorways leading nowhere. Sand fills the streets where bustling markets once thrived, and the silence is broken only by the howl of the wind. Yet, even in decay, the city retains a certain majesty, its remnants a reminder of the might and ingenuity of its builders.</p><p>Adventurers and treasure hunters are drawn to Tour-of-the-Kings, enticed by tales of hidden chambers and lost artifacts buried beneath the sands. Scholars and historians venture into its ruins in search of knowledge, piecing together the story of a civilization that once was.</p><p>But Tour-of-the-Kings holds dangers as well. Darkangels, the undead beasts that roam the desert, are said to be particularly numerous among the ruins, preying on those who dare to uncover the city's secrets. And yet, the lure of uncovering the past and the promise of ancient treasures continue to attract the brave and the bold.</p><p>In the shadow of the once-great city, the story of Tour-of-the-Kings endures, a somber reminder of the impermanence of greatness and the enduring quest for knowledge and power amidst the sands of time.</p>","summary":"Tour-of-the-Kings, once the crowning glory of a bygone era, now lies in silent ruin, a poignant testament to the transience of power and the ravages of time. Situated within the heart of what is now Ushana's desert…","sort":500000,"sourceJournal":"Ushana Dynasty"},{"name":"Westernesse","category":"Places","group":"Ushana Dynasty","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"westernesse","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Westernesse.webp","tags":["City","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Ushana","subtitle":"Maritime sister-city of the Ushanan Dynasty","meta":[{"label":"Population","value":"~340,000"},{"label":"Area","value":"58 square miles"},{"label":"Government","value":"Sultanic Regency"},{"label":"Demonym","value":"Westernessian"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"Regent Seraphine Nereidal"},{"label":"Founded","value":"Early Post-Divergence Era"}],"lists":[{"label":"Notable Locations","items":[{"name":"The Regent’s Palace","description":"Seat of Regent Seraphine Nereidal’s rule, blending Ushanan grandeur with maritime elegance."},{"name":"The Coral Quays","description":"Main harbor district lined with coral-stone piers, sea-glass lamps, warehouses, and customs houses."},{"name":"The Great Shipyards","description":"Renowned shipbuilding yards producing trade vessels, exploration ships, and military craft."},{"name":"The Sea Glass Markets","description":"Coastal markets selling spices, maritime products, fabrics, elixirs, charms, and goods from across Ushana."},{"name":"The Tidewrights’ Quarter","description":"District of shipwrights, sailmakers, ropeworkers, navigators, and maritime engineers."},{"name":"The Elixir Docks","description":"Specialized docks where rare sea-creature materials are processed for medicines, dyes, perfumes, and potions."},{"name":"The Twin Traders’ Exchange","description":"Commercial court and ritual trading house where maritime contracts are blessed and disputed."},{"name":"The Western Nothing Coast","description":"Vast and dangerous sea frontier that sustains the city and threatens it in equal measure."}]}],"content":"<p>Westernesse, the sister city to Easternesse and a vital hub within the desert expanse of Ushana, emerges from the Ushanan desert, along the coast of the Western Nothing, like an oasis of innovation and tradition. This city, under the vigilant stewardship of the Sultana's regent, serves as both a testament to Ushana's maritime prowess and a guardian of the nation's wealth drawn from the nearby sea.</p><p>Architecturally, Westernesse contrasts its eastern counterpart by harmonizing the ancient with the innovative. Buildings crafted from coral and sea glass line the bustling port, reflecting the shimmering hues of the sea at sunrise and sunset. The city's design pays homage to its maritime heritage, with streets winding like the currents of the sea, leading explorers to hidden courtyards and bustling markets that smell of salt and spices.</p><p>The city's economy thrives on the trade of maritime products, a resource as valuable as it is unique. The Western Nothing , with its vast expanses and hidden depths, is home to a myriad of sea creatures whose existences are as enigmatic as they are essential to Ushana. The harvesting of these creatures, done with reverence and an understanding of balance, provides materials used in everything from luxurious clothing to potent elixirs, fueling Ushana's wealth and Westernesse's prominence.</p><p>Westernesse is also renowned for its shipyards, where vessels designed for both trade and exploration are constructed. These ships, capable of navigating the nearby treacherous waters of the Western Nothing , embody the city's spirit of adventure and its pursuit of horizons yet unseen. The shipwrights of Westernesse, heirs to generations of maritime knowledge, craft their vessels with a blend of artistry and engineering, ensuring that Ushana's fleets remain unmatched.</p><p>The city's relationship with the sea extends beyond commerce and into the realm of the spiritual. Worship of the twin Traders is complemented by reverence for lower deities of the sea and wind, believed to guide sailors through storms and lead fishermen to bountiful catches. Temples and shrines dot the nearby coastline, where ceremonies are performed to honor these gods, asking for their blessings and protection.</p><p>Yet, Westernesse is not without its challenges. The city's reliance and expertise on the Western Nothing has drawn the covetous eyes of other nations, leading to skirmishes on the high seas. The Sultana's regent, tasked with the city's defense, must navigate the delicate balance between protecting Westernesse's treasures and maintaining the peace that has allowed the city to flourish.</p><p>Despite these trials, Westernesse remains a vibrant, thriving city, a place where the past and future meet amid the endless dunes and the vast sea. It is a city of sailors and dreamers, where every wave tells a tale of adventure, and the horizon promises wonders yet to be discovered. In Westernesse, the spirit of Ushana is embodied in the resilient heart of its people and the boundless mystery of the sea that sustains them.</p>","summary":"Westernesse, the sister city to Easternesse and a vital hub within the desert expanse of Ushana, emerges from the Ushanan desert, along the coast of the Western Nothing, like an oasis of innovation and tradition. This…","sort":600000,"sourceJournal":"Ushana Dynasty"},{"name":"Twinwell","category":"Places","group":"Wisivashu","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"twinwell","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Twinwell.webp","tags":["City","Capital","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Wisivashu","subtitle":"","meta":[{"label":"Population","value":"~165,000"},{"label":"Area","value":"26 square miles"},{"label":"Government","value":"Scholarly Civic Capital under the Coliseum"},{"label":"Demonym","value":"Twinwellian"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"The Coliseum"},{"label":"Founded","value":"Pre-Divergence; expanded and formalized as Wisivashu’s capital in the modern era"}],"lists":[{"label":"Notable Locations","items":[{"name":"The Coliseum","description":"Great central seat of government where Wisivashu’s 99 elected officials convene."},{"name":"The Grand Cascade","description":"The immense waterfall that descends from the surrounding mountains and gives life to the city."},{"name":"The River of Twinwell","description":"Freshwater artery flowing through and beyond the city toward the island seas."},{"name":"The Archive Cloisters","description":"Vast repositories of protected manuscripts, historical records, and restricted state knowledge."},{"name":"The High Libraries","description":"Legendary libraries containing ancient lore, scholarship, magical theory, medicine, history, and philosophy."},{"name":"The Deliberative Halls","description":"Auxiliary chambers where committees, scholars, and officials debate policy and interpretation."},{"name":"The Observatory Towers","description":"High towers used for celestial study, atmospheric observation, and long-range recordkeeping."},{"name":"The Silent Residences","description":"Lesser-access library wings and administrative archives available to approved domestic researchers."}]}],"content":"<p>Twinwell, the enigmatic heart of Wisivashu, stands as a citadel of knowledge and governance, its existence veiled in secrecy and its streets walked by few outsiders. Nestled in a unique geographical marvel, Twinwell is cradled by towering mountains from which cascades a massive waterfall, the city’s lifeline. This waterfall not only graces Twinwell with a breathtaking spectacle but also supplies it with an abundance of fresh water, channeled from the mountains through a mainly unmapped river that snakes its way into the surrounding island seas. The strategic location of Twinwell, coupled with its natural defenses and resources, exemplifies the harmonious balance between Wisivashu's scholarly pursuits and its commitment to self-sufficiency and isolation.</p><p>At the core of Twinwell lies the Coliseum, not merely a structure but a symbol of Wisivashu's governing principles and intellectual foundations. This vast edifice, from which the nation’s ruling body derives its name, is more than a meeting place for the Coliseum's 99 members; it is the epicenter of Wisivashu's cultural and political identity. Surrounded by the hallowed halls of libraries and the intricate corridors of laboratories, the Coliseum stands as the guardian of Wisivashu's accumulated knowledge and the architectural embodiment of its dedication to learning and governance.</p><p>The libraries of Twinwell are legendary, rumored to contain volumes of ancient lore, cutting-edge research, and manuscripts that span the breadth of human understanding. These repositories of wisdom attract scholars from within Wisivashu, each contributing to the ever-growing expanse of knowledge that the nation prides itself on. The laboratories, equally revered, are the crucibles of innovation where the theoretical knowledge of the libraries is tested and applied. Together, these institutions form a symbiotic relationship that fuels Wisivashu's advancements in science, magic, and the arts.</p><p>Despite its significance as a center of learning and government, Twinwell remains an enigma to the outside world. The city's architecture is said to reflect the nation's reverence for knowledge, with buildings designed to facilitate the flow of ideas and information. Public squares are adorned with sculptures that celebrate intellectual achievements, while gardens and open spaces provide tranquil settings for contemplation and discussion.</p><p>Access to Twinwell is tightly controlled, preserving its isolation and ensuring that its secrets remain guarded. The few outsiders who have been granted entry speak of a city that operates with a quiet efficiency, its inhabitants moving with a purposeful grace among the towering shelves of libraries and the bustling activity of laboratories. The air is filled with the sound of the waterfall, a constant reminder of the natural beauty that surrounds and sustains the city.</p><p>Twinwell, in its seclusion and splendor, stands as a testament to Wisivashu's ideals. It is a city where governance is informed by scholarship, where knowledge is both the foundation of power and its ultimate expression. In the shadow of the Coliseum, amidst the whispering pages of libraries and the fervent experimentation of laboratories, Twinwell thrives as a beacon of enlightenment, its mysteries preserved by the mountains and the waterfall that both nurtures and shields it from the world beyond.</p>","summary":"Twinwell, the enigmatic heart of Wisivashu, stands as a citadel of knowledge and governance, its existence veiled in secrecy and its streets walked by few outsiders. Nestled in a unique geographical marvel, Twinwell is…","sort":0,"sourceJournal":"Wisivashu"},{"name":"Wisivashu Nation","category":"Places","group":"Wisivashu","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"wisivashu-nation","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/StainedGlass-Wisivashu.webp","tags":["Nation","Archipelago","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Wisivashu","subtitle":"Isolationist archipelago of scholars and guarded knowledge","meta":[{"label":"Population","value":"~1.2 million"},{"label":"Area","value":"~27,000 square miles"},{"label":"Government","value":"Isolationist Scholarly Republic"},{"label":"Demonym","value":"Wisivashun"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"The Coliseum"},{"label":"Founded","value":"Pre-Divergence; current isolationist order formalized after the mainland withdrawal"}],"lists":[{"label":"Neighbor Regions","items":[{"tag":"Ushana"}]}],"content":"<p>Wisivashu, a nation shrouded in mystery and marked by its deliberate isolation from the broader geopolitical landscape of Eilune, is a realm where knowledge is both sanctuary and power. Esteemed for its scholastic achievements and academic pursuits, Wisivashu stands as a beacon of learning and intellectual inquiry, its society deeply rooted in the pursuit of understanding the world's mysteries. However, this quest for knowledge is balanced by a stringent policy of isolationism, making the nation an enigma to outsiders and a fortress of untold secrets.</p><p>The nation's history of withdrawal, exemplified by the abandonment of a mainland city-state in the face of Efra Dorei aggression, underscores a philosophy that values the preservation of knowledge and cultural identity above territorial expansion or military conquest. This event, leading to the eventual rise of the Coskoreia Republic within Wisivashu's former domains, highlights the nation's readiness to forsake land and legacy rather than compromise its principles or engage in fruitless conflict.</p><p>Wisivashu's government, known as the Coliseum, epitomizes the nation's commitment to collective governance and scholarly oversight. Comprising 99 elected officials serving five-year terms, the Coliseum reflects the will and wisdom of the Wisivashun people, with mandatory voting ensuring widespread civic participation and accountability. This electoral system, emphasizing the importance of each citizen's voice, reinforces the nation's dedication to a democratic process, albeit within the context of its isolationist stance.</p><p>The Coliseum convenes in the capitol of Twinwell where the government deliberates and decides on matters of state, in a massive and elegant structure. This symbolic edifice, from which the Coliseum derives its name, stands as a testament to the unity and purpose of Wisivashu's leaders, embodying the collective pursuit of knowledge and the safeguarding of the nation's intellectual and cultural heritage.</p><p>Wisivashu's policy of controlled knowledge dissemination, wherein the unauthorized sharing of information with foreign entities is tantamount to treason, reinforces its isolationist posture. This approach, driven by a desire to observe and document history rather than actively shape it, has made Wisivashu a repository of untold wisdom and ancient lore. Scholars and historians from across Eilune whisper of the vast libraries and archives hidden within Wisivashu's borders, repositories of knowledge that remain tantalizingly out of reach to those beyond its confines.</p><p>Yet, despite its self-imposed isolation, Wisivashu is not without influence. The nation's academic and intellectual contributions, albeit selectively shared, have the potential to alter the course of research and thought across Eilune. Its scholars, though rarely venturing beyond their borders, are respected for their depth of knowledge and insight, making the occasional tidbits of Wisivashun wisdom that find their way into the wider world all the more valuable.</p><p>In the tapestry of Eilune's nations, Wisivashu stands apart, a realm where the thirst for knowledge governs all aspects of life and policy. Its isolationist stance, entwined with a rich scholarly tradition, ensures that Wisivashu remains an enigmatic presence on the continent, a nation that commands respect and curiosity in equal measure.</p>","summary":"Wisivashu, a nation shrouded in mystery and marked by its deliberate isolation from the broader geopolitical landscape of Eilune, is a realm where knowledge is both sanctuary and power. Esteemed for its scholastic…","sort":0,"sourceJournal":"Wisivashu"},{"name":"Dalon Marsh","category":"Places","group":"Wisivashu","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"dalon-marsh","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-DalonMarsh.webp","tags":["Marsh","Wilderness","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Wisivashu","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Dalon Marsh is a mysterious and enchanting expanse of wetlands that stretches across the heart of Wisivashu. Shrouded in mist and surrounded by dense forests, this vast marshland is a realm of ethereal beauty and hidden secrets.</p><p>The marsh is characterized by its labyrinthine network of winding waterways, where murky waters reflect the verdant canopy overhead. Tall reeds and cattails sway gently in the breeze, creating a hypnotic rhythm that echoes through the marsh.</p><p>Dalon Marsh is teeming with life, from the chorus of frogs and crickets that fill the air with their symphony, to the myriad of exotic birds that call the marsh home. Strange and otherworldly creatures lurk beneath the surface of the water, their eerie calls adding to the marsh's mystique.</p><p>Throughout the marsh, pockets of vibrant flora bloom in a riot of colors, creating a kaleidoscope of beauty against the backdrop of emerald green. Towering mangroves with twisted roots rise from the water, while delicate water lilies float serenely on the surface, their petals glistening with dew.</p><p>Despite its haunting beauty, Dalon Marsh can be a treacherous place for the unwary traveler. Quicksand pits and hidden sinkholes lurk beneath the surface, ready to ensnare those who stray from the beaten path. Thick mists often cloak the marsh in a veil of secrecy, obscuring landmarks and disorienting even the most experienced navigators.</p><p>Yet, for those who dare to venture into its depths, Dalon Marsh holds untold wonders and discoveries waiting to be uncovered. It is a place of both danger and fascination, where the boundary between the mundane world and the realm of the supernatural grows thin, and the whispers of ancient spirits linger on the wind.</p>","summary":"Dalon Marsh is a mysterious and enchanting expanse of wetlands that stretches across the heart of Wisivashu. Shrouded in mist and surrounded by dense forests, this vast marshland is a realm of ethereal beauty and hidden…","sort":100000,"sourceJournal":"Wisivashu"},{"name":"Green Haven","category":"Places","group":"Wisivashu","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"green-haven","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-GreenHaven.webp","tags":["City","Marsh","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Wisivashu","subtitle":"","meta":[{"label":"Population","value":"~92,000"},{"label":"Area","value":"19 square miles"},{"label":"Government","value":"Scholarly Civic Council under the Coliseum"},{"label":"Demonym","value":"Havener"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"The Green Haven Council"},{"label":"Founded","value":"Post-Divergence expansion of an older marsh settlement"}],"lists":[{"label":"Notable Locations","items":[{"name":"The Botanical Conservatories","description":"Controlled gardens and glasshouses preserving medicinal plants sourced from the Dalon Marsh and beyond."},{"name":"The Apothecaries’ Arcade","description":"Prestigious district of pharmacies, herbalists, compounders, and tincture-makers."},{"name":"The Elevated Boulevards","description":"Broad raised avenues lined with trees, linking the city’s major civic, academic, and medical districts."},{"name":"The Institute of Medical Sciences of Esivar","description":"Green Haven’s premier center for non-magical medical research, education, and applied study."},{"name":"The Great Clinics","description":"Major treatment halls providing some of the finest medical care in Wisivashu."},{"name":"The Marsh Laboratories","description":"Advanced research facilities specializing in non-magical medicine, tinctures, herbcraft, anatomy, disease study, and practical healing science."}]}],"content":"<p>Green Haven serves as a beacon of modernity and innovation within the ancient and mystical surroundings of the Dalon Marsh. Its sleek, regal architecture stands in stark juxtaposition to the wild, natural beauty of its surroundings, creating a captivating blend of old and new.</p><p>As a center for advancing non-magical medicine, Green Haven is renowned for its cutting-edge research facilities, state-of-the-art laboratories, and prestigious medical schools. The city attracts scholars, physicians, and alchemists from far and wide, drawn by the opportunity to push the boundaries of medicinal knowledge and develop groundbreaking potions and tinctures.</p><p>The streets of Green Haven bustle with activity, as citizens and visitors alike go about their daily lives amidst the city's polished surfaces reflecting the verdant hues of the marshlands. Wide boulevards lined with towering trees wind their way through the city, leading to bustling market squares and pristine parks. Modern amenities such as hospitals, pharmacies, and clinics dot the cityscape, offering top-notch medical care to those in need.</p><p>Despite its focus on non-magical medicine, Green Haven maintains a deep respect for the natural world and the ancient traditions of the Wisivashi people. The city's laboratories are filled with vials of exotic herbs and botanical specimens sourced from the marshlands, serving as the foundation for the development of new medicinal concoctions.</p><p>In Green Haven, the pursuit of scientific knowledge and the preservation of cultural heritage go hand in hand, creating a dynamic and harmonious society where tradition and innovation coexist. It is a place where the wonders of modern medicine meet the mystique of the natural world, forging a path towards a healthier and more prosperous future for all.</p>","summary":"Green Haven serves as a beacon of modernity and innovation within the ancient and mystical surroundings of the Dalon Marsh. Its sleek, regal architecture stands in stark juxtaposition to the wild, natural beauty of its…","sort":200000,"sourceJournal":"Wisivashu"},{"name":"Towershine","category":"Places","group":"Wisivashu","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"towershine","hero":"","tags":["City","Lighthouse","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Wisivashu","subtitle":"","meta":[{"label":"Population","value":"~18,000"},{"label":"Area","value":"7 square miles"},{"label":"Government","value":"Beacon Prefecture under the Coliseum"},{"label":"Demonym","value":"Towershinean"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"Beaconwarden Ilyra Voshen"},{"label":"Founded","value":"Pre-Divergence watchpost; expanded under Wisivashu’s isolationist order"}],"lists":[{"label":"Notable Locations","items":[{"name":"The High Lantern","description":"The great lighthouse-tower at the island’s highest point, watching the southern sea lanes."},{"name":"The Observatory of Tides and Stars","description":"Scholarly tower complex devoted to astronomy, weather, tides, currents, and maritime navigation."},{"name":"Beaconwarden’s Hall","description":"Administrative seat of Towershine’s prefecture and maritime scholars."},{"name":"The Saltglass Walk","description":"Clifftop promenade lined with sea-glass markers, lamps, and memorials to lost ships."},{"name":"The Listening Rooms","description":"Secure chambers where foreign rumors, ship reports, intercepted signals, and maritime records are compared."},{"name":"The Storm Bells","description":"Bell-towers warning of dangerous weather, unauthorized vessels, quarantine breaches, or sea emergencies."}]}],"content":"<p>Towershine is the southernmost island settlement of Wisivashu, a windswept beacon-island of lighthouses, observatories, quarantine halls, signal mirrors, and maritime archives. It is not the sole gateway into Wisivashu, for vessels may also attempt approaches from the waters near Bern, Westernesse, or other guarded coastlines. Instead, Towershine serves a more specific and vital purpose: it watches the southern sea lanes, where open water, distant island routes, and forgotten pre-Divergence paths meet the guarded edge of Wisivashun sovereignty.</p><p>The settlement takes its name from the High Lantern, the great lighthouse that rises from the island’s tallest cliff. Its light sweeps across the southern waters in disciplined intervals, guiding approved vessels toward safe anchorage and warning unknown ships away from restricted approaches. Around it stand lesser towers fitted with polished mirrors, lenses, lanterns, and signal mechanisms. By day, flashes of reflected light carry coded messages across the sea. By night, colored lamps answer one another in patterns understood only by trained readers.</p><p>Towershine is part of Wisivashu’s broader network of controlled access, not an invitation to enter. Foreign ships permitted to dock are brought first to the White Quarantine Halls, where physicians, scribes, and inspectors examine travelers, cargo, maps, texts, relics, illnesses, enchantments, and inconsistencies in testimony. Some visitors are granted temporary passage deeper into Wisivashu. Others are delayed for days or weeks. Many are politely resupplied at the Refusal Pier and sent away without ever setting foot beyond the harbor precinct.</p><p>The city’s scholars study the world from a distance. The Observatory of Tides and Stars records celestial movement, storms, currents, migratory patterns, sea temperatures, and the behavior of vessels crossing the southern horizon. The Archive of Passing Sails preserves accounts of every ship sighted, admitted, redirected, refused, or lost. To outsiders, such obsessive documentation may seem excessive. To Wisivashu, it is simply civic memory applied to the sea.</p><p>Though watchful, Towershine is not bleak. Its streets are pale, salt-bright, and carefully maintained, lined with sea-glass lamps, cliff gardens, lenswrights’ workshops, quiet residences, and clean stone stairways cut into the island’s slopes. The Saltglass Walk curves along the cliffs, offering views of open water and distant green islands. Residents live by the rhythm of bells, waves, lantern signals, and weather reports, their lives shaped by vigilance rather than fear.</p><p>Towershine is governed by the Beaconwarden, an official of the Coliseum charged with overseeing the island’s lighthouses, quarantine laws, maritime records, signal towers, harbor access, and sea-lane observation. The current Beaconwarden, Ilyra Voshen, is known for her immaculate courtesy, exacting patience, and refusal to be hurried by merchants, diplomats, captains, or foreign officials. Under her administration, Towershine remains what Wisivashu needs it to be: a light in the southern sea, a listening post at the edge of secrecy, and a closed door that speaks with perfect politeness.</p><p>To those who approach from the south, Towershine may appear welcoming at first: a golden light in the mist, a harbor beneath white towers, a promise of safety after open water. But every light is also a warning. Every harbor is also a question. Every arrival is entered into a ledger. In Towershine, Wisivashu does not hide from the world entirely. It watches, records, judges, and decides how close the world may come.</p>","summary":"Towershine is the southernmost island settlement of Wisivashu, a windswept beacon-island of lighthouses, observatories, quarantine halls, signal mirrors, and maritime archives. It is not the sole gateway into Wisivashu,…","sort":300000,"sourceJournal":"Wisivashu"},{"name":"Ember Hinterlands","category":"Places","group":"Ember Hinterlands","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"ember-hinterlands","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/StainedGlass-Hinterlands.webp","tags":["No Man's Land","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Ember Hinterlands","subtitle":"Blighted no man’s land between ice and desert","meta":[{"label":"Area","value":"~35,000 square miles"},{"label":"Government","value":"None region-wide"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"None"},{"label":"Founded","value":"Transformed during the Divergence"}],"lists":[{"label":"Notable Locations","items":[{"name":"Altar","description":"Largest and most stable settlement in the Ember Hinterlands, built atop a towering plateau and governed locally."},{"name":"Shade","description":"Shadewalker's base of operations"},{"name":"The Ribbon’s Fist","description":"Massive volcano that emerged after the cataclysm, dominating the region with ash, smoke, and perpetual fire."},{"name":"The Seven Lids","description":"Satellite craters surrounding the Ribbon’s Fist, each dangerous, unstable, and steeped in speculation."}]}],"content":"<p>The transformation of the Emerald Hinterlands into the Ember Hinterlands is a tale of beauty turned to desolation, a vivid example of the profound changes wrought by the cataclysmic events of the Ribbon and the Divergence. Once a lush expanse of forests, pastures, and vibrant grasslands, the land served as a natural divider between the might of Runvegr and the expanses of Ushana. The Emerald Hinterlands were a place of life and abundance, albeit one marked by the wild freedom of bandits, hermits, and hunters who called its verdant wilderness home.</p><p>However, the arrival of the Ribbon heralded the beginning of the end for this once-bountiful region. A mysterious poison seeped into the soil, water, and air, a creeping death that forced many of its inhabitants to flee for their lives. Animals, too, scattered, driven away by the blight that consumed their habitats. The once-lush landscapes withered and died, leaving behind only the echoes of their former beauty.</p><p>The Divergence only compounded the devastation. In a dramatic reshaping of the land, the majority of the remaining flora was obliterated, replaced by vast expanses of dark rock and sand that stretched as far as the eye could see. The transformation was so complete, so absolute, that the land became unrecognizable to those few who dared return.</p><p>The most striking symbol of this new, blighted landscape is the Ribbon's Fist, a massive volcano that emerged seemingly overnight, surrounded by the Seven Lids, its satellite craters. These geological phenomena dominate the Ember Hinterlands, their perpetual eruptions casting a shadow over the land. The ash and smoke they spew forth have poisoned the air, decreasing its quality and casting a pall over the sky. At sunrise and sunset, the light filters through this haze, painting everything in hues of red and orange, a somber beauty born from destruction.</p><p>This transformation has given the Ember Hinterlands its new name, a reflection of its current state. The land, now mostly uncharted and considered inhospitable, is a stark contrast to its past. Yet, despite its desolation, the Ember Hinterlands are not devoid of life. Hardy flora and fauna have adapted to the harsh conditions, and rumors persist of communities that have found ways to survive in this forbidding landscape, perhaps even harnessing the volcanic activity for their purposes.</p><p>Adventurers and scholars are drawn to the Ember Hinterlands, compelled by the desire to explore its mysteries and uncover the secrets of its transformation. The Ribbon's Fist and the Seven Lids, in particular, are subjects of fascination, with many speculating on their origins and the forces that continue to shape them.</p>","summary":"The transformation of the Emerald Hinterlands into the Ember Hinterlands is a tale of beauty turned to desolation, a vivid example of the profound changes wrought by the cataclysmic events of the Ribbon and the…","sort":0,"sourceJournal":"Ember Hinterlands"},{"name":"Altar","category":"Places","group":"Ember Hinterlands","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"altar","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Altar.webp","tags":["City","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Ember Hinterlands","subtitle":"Plateau city of storm, trade, and survival","meta":[{"label":"Population","value":"~64,000"},{"label":"Area","value":"22 square miles"},{"label":"Government","value":"Independent Councilorship with Tesseris Presence"},{"label":"Demonym","value":"Altaran"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"Councilor Maren Leifdottir"},{"label":"Founded","value":"Post-Divergence Era"}],"lists":[{"label":"Notable Locations","items":[{"name":"The Traveler’s Hearth","description":"Grand inn for adventurers, traders, and caravan travelers."},{"name":"Altar Academy of Rhythm and Wonder","description":"Dance studio run by Tatiana al-Noor, serving children, elders, and motion-impaired adults."},{"name":"Stormcatchers’ Fields","description":"Rainwater-capturing farm systems that sustain Altar’s agriculture."},{"name":"Grand Watchtower of the Tesseris","description":"Fortified Tesseris headquarters patrolled by Crimson Justicars."},{"name":"Council Hall","description":"Seat of Altar’s government, where Councilor Maren Leifdottir presides."}]}],"content":"<p>Altar, aptly named for its dramatic positioning atop a towering plateau of rock, emerges as a beacon of civilization within the desolate expanse of the Ember Hinterlands. This city, the largest settlement in a land characterized by its harsh conditions, stands as a testament to the resilience and adaptability of its inhabitants. Stretching across three distinct elevations, Altar's architecture and layout reflect the ingenuity required to thrive in such an unforgiving environment.</p><p>The city's unique location not only distinguishes it visually but also grants it a rare advantage in the Ember Hinterlands: access to stormy weather patterns. Unlike the arid stretches that define much of the surrounding region, Altar benefits from the precipitation brought by these storms, which provide a critical source of water. This natural boon allows for the existence of farmlands around the city's base, where hardy crops eke out a modest existence from the otherwise stingy soil. Though the yields are poor compared to more fertile regions, they are a vital resource for a city isolated by the vast, inhospitable terrain of the Hinterlands.</p><p>The strategic significance of Altar as a midpoint between the Ushana Dynasty and the Holy Empire of Runvegr has not gone unnoticed by merchants and traders. Recognizing the city's potential as a hub of commerce on the perilous journey between these two great powers, a diverse array of merchants have made Altar their home. The marketplaces of Altar buzz with activity, offering goods from both empires and beyond. Here, adventurers can equip themselves for the dangers that lie ahead, and travelers can find respite and replenishment. The variety of wares available, from mundane supplies to exotic artifacts, makes Altar an essential stop for anyone navigating the treacherous routes of the Ember Hinterlands.</p><p>The presence of the Tesseris in Altar lends the city an air of order and authority unusual for such a remote settlement. As the elite mages of Runvegr, their occasional sojourns in Altar serve as both rest and reconnaissance, ensuring that the city remains a loyal and orderly outpost on the empire's frontier. The Tesseris' presence acts as a deterrent to would-be troublemakers, maintaining peace and stability in a land where both can be scarce. Their visits also imbue the city with a sense of significance, reinforcing its role as a key point of connection between the disparate worlds of Ushana and Runvegr.</p><p>Despite its challenges, Altar thrives as a vibrant community where the spirit of cooperation and enterprise prevails. The city's inhabitants, a mix of hardy farmers, astute merchants, and daring adventurers, have forged a life on this unlikely altar of rock. Festivals and gatherings, often centered around the changing weather patterns and the arrival of traders or the Tesseris, punctuate the rhythm of daily life, bringing color and celebration to the stone streets.</p><p>Altar stands as a monument to tenacity, a city that has carved a place for itself on the edge of the known world. Its unique position, both geographically and culturally, makes it a focal point of commerce, diplomacy, and survival in the ever-changing landscape of the Ember Hinterlands.</p>","summary":"Altar, aptly named for its dramatic positioning atop a towering plateau of rock, emerges as a beacon of civilization within the desolate expanse of the Ember Hinterlands. This city, the largest settlement in a land…","sort":100000,"sourceJournal":"Ember Hinterlands"},{"name":"Ribbon's Eye","category":"Places","group":"Ember Hinterlands","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"ribbon-s-eye","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-RibbonsEye.png","tags":["Ribbon","Wilderness","Sea","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Ember Hinterlands","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>The Ribbon's Eye, a maritime marvel and a terror of the seas, looms ominously off the coast near where the Ribbon's Fist dominates the land. This massive whirlpool, perpetually churning in a dance of destruction and creation, serves as a natural barrier and a reminder of the untamed power that the Divergence unleashed upon the world. The maelstrom, with its voracious appetite and unpredictable nature, is feared by sailors and fishermen alike, a navigational nightmare that has claimed countless ships and lives.</p><p>Spanning several miles in diameter, the Ribbon's Eye is visible from a great distance, its swirling waters a hypnotic spectacle that belies the danger lurking within. The whirlpool's center, a fathomless abyss from which few have escaped, is said to hold secrets and treasures from the depths of the sea, swallowed along with the unfortunate vessels that ventured too close. Around its periphery, the waters boil and froth, creating a no-man's-land where the sea itself seems to wage war against any who dare to trespass.</p><p>Legends abound regarding the origin of the Ribbon's Eye. Some say it was formed in the same cataclysmic event that birthed the Ribbon's Fist, a sister scar upon the earth mirroring the volcanic fury found on land. Others whisper of ancient, forgotten magics unleashed without heed to their consequences, binding the whirlpool to the land's fate. Whatever its origins, the Ribbon's Eye is inextricably linked to the mysteries and anomalies that define the post-Divergence world.</p><p>Despite its peril, the Ribbon's Eye draws the brave, the desperate, and the curious. Adventurers and treasure hunters, lured by tales of sunken riches and ancient artifacts lost beneath the waves, venture near its waters, hoping to glimpse its secrets without falling prey to its grasp. Scholars and mages study it from afar, speculating on its nature and the forces that sustain its endless churn.</p><p>The Ribbon's Eye also plays a significant role in the lore and superstitions of those who live in its shadow. It is considered a gatekeeper by some, guarding the entrance to realms beyond human ken. Sailors pay homage to it through rituals and offerings, hoping to appease any spirits or entities that might reside within its depths. To the people of the Ember Hinterlands and the surrounding regions, the Ribbon's Eye is both a curse and a wonder, a symbol of the world's chaos and majesty.</p><p>Navigating the waters near the Ribbon's Eye requires a blend of skill, respect for the sea's power, and no small amount of luck. The maelstrom's influence on currents and weather patterns makes the surrounding seas treacherous, yet the routes it guards remain tempting paths for those seeking to explore what lies beyond.</p>","summary":"The Ribbon's Eye, a maritime marvel and a terror of the seas, looms ominously off the coast near where the Ribbon's Fist dominates the land. This massive whirlpool, perpetually churning in a dance of destruction and…","sort":175000,"sourceJournal":"Ember Hinterlands"},{"name":"Ribbon's Fist","category":"Places","group":"Ember Hinterlands","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"ribbon-s-fist","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-RibbonsFist.webp","tags":["Volcano","Western Eilune","Wilderness","Ribbon"],"mainTag":"Ember Hinterlands","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>The Ribbon's Fist, a towering volcano that serves as the heart of the Ember Hinterlands, is a monument to the chaotic power unleashed by the Divergence. Its sudden emergence, along with the Seven Lids—its attendant craters—has reshaped the landscape and the lives of those who dare to dwell within its shadow. The Fist is not merely a geological feature; it is a symbol of the new world order, a constant reminder of the forces that lie just beneath the surface, ready to erupt in violence and beauty.</p><p>Dominating the horizon, the Ribbon's Fist can be seen from nearly every vantage point within the Ember Hinterlands, its presence both awe-inspiring and ominous. It rises from the dark rock and sand like a beacon, its peak often shrouded in smoke and ash. The perpetual lava flows that snake down its sides illuminate the night, casting a fiery glow that can be seen for miles around.</p><p>The area surrounding the Ribbon's Fist is one of constant turmoil. The ground trembles with frequent eruptions, spewing forth not only lava and ash but also creatures from The Ribbon nearby. These monsters, drawn to the power of the Fist, make the vicinity a deadly place for the unwary. Bands of adventurers and scholars who venture too close often find themselves facing unimaginable horrors sprung from the depths of the volcano.</p><p>Despite the danger, life has found a way to thrive in this inhospitable environment. Fire crabs, with their hardened, heat-resistant shells, roam the rocky terrain, feeding on the minerals in the lava flows. Lava golems, creatures of molten rock animated by the volcanic magic, wander the landscape, embodying the raw, destructive nature of their home. These beings, and others like them, have adapted to the extreme conditions of the Ribbon's Fist, creating an ecosystem as deadly as it is fascinating.</p><p>For those brave or foolish enough to explore the Ribbon's Fist and its surrounding craters, the rewards can be great. Rare minerals and magical essences, forged in the heart of the volcano, draw treasure hunters and mages seeking to harness the power of the Divergence. Tales of ancient artifacts, buried beneath layers of ash or hidden within the lava tubes that riddle the volcano's interior, circulate among those who frequent the Ember Hinterlands.</p><p>Yet, the true nature of the Ribbon's Fist remains shrouded in mystery. Scholars speculate that the volcano and its craters may be a nexus of magical energy, a focal point for the forces that caused the Divergence. Some believe that within its depths lies the key to understanding the cataclysmic events that reshaped the world, while others fear that tampering with its power could lead to further disaster.</p><p>The Ribbon's Fist stands as a challenge to the denizens of the Ember Hinterlands and beyond, a call to adventure and discovery that few can resist. It is a place of danger and beauty, destruction and creation, where the legacy of the past and the possibilities of the future are entwined in the molten heart of the earth.</p>","summary":"The Ribbon's Fist, a towering volcano that serves as the heart of the Ember Hinterlands, is a monument to the chaotic power unleashed by the Divergence. Its sudden emergence, along with the Seven Lids—its attendant…","sort":187500,"sourceJournal":"Ember Hinterlands"},{"name":"Seven Lids","category":"Places","group":"Ember Hinterlands","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"seven-lids","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-SevenLids.webp","tags":["Volcano","Western Eilune","Wilderness","Ribbon"],"mainTag":"Ember Hinterlands","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>The Seven Lids, an enigmatic constellation of craters born from the tumult of the Divergence, encircle the Ribbon's Fist like sentinels guarding a profound secret. Each Lid, topped with a colossal, glowing red crystal, presents a mystery as impenetrable as the crystals themselves. These natural phenomena stand as a testament to the unfathomable forces unleashed during the cataclysm, their origins and purpose subjects of intense speculation and awe.</p><p>Unlike any known geological formation, the craters beneath the glowing crystals do not conform to the expected patterns of volcanic activity. Instead, they seemingly serve as windows to other realms, offering fleeting glimpses into lands beyond comprehension. The vistas revealed beneath the Seven Lids are ever-changing, as unpredictable in their appearance as they are in their nature. One moment, an observer might witness a scene of idyllic beauty, verdant and teeming with life; the next, the same crater may unveil a landscape of desolation and torment, a vision of realms best left unexplored.</p><p>The proximity of the Seven Lids to the Ribbon's Fist and the volatile magic of the Ribbon itself poses significant risks to any who would seek to study these phenomena closely. The area is fraught with danger, not only from the constant volcanic activity of the Fist but also from the monstrous entities that emerge from its depths and, perhaps, from the Lids themselves.</p><p>Despite the hazards, the Seven Lids have captivated the imaginations of scholars and adventurers alike. The crystals that cap the craters, impervious to damage and radiating with an inner light, hint at the possibility of powers or knowledge yet untapped. Some theorize that these crystals are not mere natural formations but are instead keys of a sort, locking away the potential for planar travel or serving as a barrier between worlds. The shifting vistas beneath the crystals tantalize with the promise of undiscovered lands, perhaps even offering a pathway back to Eilune's original plane of existence, lost since the time of the Divergence.</p><p>Yet, for all the speculation, the Seven Lids remain shrouded in mystery. Efforts to crack the crystals or harness their power have met with failure, leaving many to wonder whether the secrets of the Lids are meant to be uncovered or if they are simply beyond the reach of mortal understanding. Theories abound regarding the true nature of the crystals and the lands they reveal, ranging from windows into parallel universes to visions conjured by the Ribbon's magic to test or tantalize those who gaze upon them.</p>","summary":"The Seven Lids, an enigmatic constellation of craters born from the tumult of the Divergence, encircle the Ribbon's Fist like sentinels guarding a profound secret. Each Lid, topped with a colossal, glowing red crystal,…","sort":193750,"sourceJournal":"Ember Hinterlands"},{"name":"Shade","category":"Places","group":"Ember Hinterlands","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"shade","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Shade.png","tags":["City","Western Eilune","Shadewalkers"],"mainTag":"Ember Hinterlands","subtitle":"Hidden underground sanctuary of the Wastes","meta":[{"label":"Population","value":"~34,000"},{"label":"Area","value":"12 square miles mapped; deeper ruins unknown"},{"label":"Government","value":"Local Sanctuary Council"},{"label":"Demonym","value":"Shadeweller"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"The Lantern Council"},{"label":"Founded","value":"Post-Divergence refuge; built within ancient dwarvish ruins"}],"lists":[{"label":"Notable Locations","items":[{"name":"The Council Lamps","description":"Civic chamber of the Lantern Council, lit by suspended lake-glass lanterns."},{"name":"The Gloamlake","description":"Bioluminescent underground lake at the heart of Shade, source of light, water, fish, and civic rhythm."},{"name":"The Lantern Market","description":"Main commercial district selling scavenged goods, survival supplies, underground produce, maps, relics, and guide contracts."},{"name":"The Shadewalker Concourse","description":"Gathering place where Shadewalkers rest, resupply, compare routes, and negotiate passage across or around the Ribbon."},{"name":"The Lakefront Arcades","description":"Warmly lit walkways, shops, taverns, and residences built along the glowing water."},{"name":"The Salvage Bazaar","description":"Market for goods recovered from the Wastes, old ruins, abandoned caravans, and Ribbon-scarred sites."},{"name":"The Silent Span","description":"Great bridge or causeway crossing part of the cavern, often used for processions, meetings, and quiet deals."}]}],"content":"<p>Shade, a beacon of resilience and ingenuity nestled in the heart of the Wastes, stands as a testament to the unyielding spirit of those who refuse to be vanquished by their environment. This subterranean city, thriving in defiance of the harsh conditions that ravage the surface, has managed to carve out an existence in one of the most inhospitable regions of the world. Built within the labyrinthine depths of an ancient dwarvish ruin, Shade has transformed from a mere refuge into a bustling hub of commerce and sanctuary.</p><p>The city's survival through the ages, amid the relentless Sorrow Storms and the dangers spilling forth from the Ribbon, is a marvel of adaptation and fortitude. The decision to build beneath the earth, utilizing the dwarves' forgotten halls and chambers, has shielded its inhabitants from the countless perils that roam above. The underground lake at the heart of Shade is not only a source of water but also a natural luminary, thanks to the bioluminescent plankton that inhabit its waters. This glowing lake bathes the city in a soft, ethereal light that waxes and wanes, mirroring the day and night cycle of the world above and providing a semblance of normalcy to the city's rhythm of life.</p><p>The aquatic ecosystem supported by the lake ensures a continuous supply of food, with fish and other edible creatures thriving in its illuminated depths. This self-sustaining environment has allowed Shade to develop a degree of autonomy rare in the Wastes, making it a vital stop for travelers and a permanent home for those seeking refuge from the harshness of the surface.</p><p>Merchants and innkeepers form the backbone of Shade's economy, catering to the needs of the city's diverse population and the adventurers, traders, and refugees that find their way to its hidden gates. The marketplaces of Shade are a curious blend of the exotic and the essential, offering goods scavenged from the ruins above, traded goods from distant lands, and the unique produce of the underground itself. Inns and taverns provide warm beds and hearty meals, their walls echoing with the tales of those who have braved the Wastes and the Ribbon.</p><p>The entrance to Shade is a closely guarded secret, known only to its inhabitants and the Shadewalkers who traverse the Wastes. These guides, adept at navigating the dangers of the Ribbon and the storms that plague the land, are integral to the city's connection with the world outside. The pathways leading to and from Shade are protected by both cunning engineering and the vigilance of its guardians, ensuring that the city remains a sanctuary for those fortunate enough to know its location.</p><p>Despite its isolation, Shade is a city of remarkable diversity, its population comprised of individuals from various backgrounds and races, each with their own reasons for seeking the city's shelter. Here, in the depths of the earth, a unique community has flourished, bound together by the shared challenge of survival and the collective endeavor to maintain a beacon of hope in a land otherwise forsaken.</p><p>Shade's existence is a story of endurance, a narrative of life persisting in the shadow of desolation. It is a city that defies the desolate landscape it inhabits, proving that even in the darkest of places, light can be found and life can thrive.</p>","summary":"Shade, a beacon of resilience and ingenuity nestled in the heart of the Wastes, stands as a testament to the unyielding spirit of those who refuse to be vanquished by their environment. This subterranean city, thriving…","sort":250000,"sourceJournal":"Ember Hinterlands"},{"name":"The Wastes","category":"Places","group":"Ember Hinterlands","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"the-wastes","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-TheWastes.jpg","tags":["Wilderness","No Man's Land","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Ember Hinterlands","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>The Wastes, a name as desolate as the landscape it describes, stretch out to the east of Runvegr, a vast expanse of desolation and decay. This region, once perhaps thriving with cities and life, now serves as a stark reminder of the cataclysmic forces unleashed during the Divergence. The ruins of ancient Runvegr cities lie scattered across the Wastes, their broken spires and crumbling walls a testament to the devastation that reshaped the land.</p><p>The terrain of the Wastes is as inhospitable as any on the continent. Barren lands extend as far as the eye can see, devoid of vegetation and life, with the earth itself scarred by the events of the past. Massive cracks in the ground, remnants of earthquakes and upheavals, mar the landscape, making travel perilous. Dust storms also sweep across the land with alarming frequency, obscuring vision and erasing tracks, disorienting even the most seasoned travelers.</p><p>Dragons, the last inhabitants of the Wastes, reign supreme in this forsaken land. These formidable creatures, perhaps drawn to the desolation or perhaps remnants of a world that once was, patrol the skies and the ruins, fiercely protective of their territory. Encounters with these dragons are often fatal, adding another layer of danger to the already perilous journey across the Wastes.</p><p>For those seeking to cross the Ribbon from the west, the Wastes represent a formidable barrier. Shadewalkers, guides known for their ability to navigate the treacherous paths of the Ribbon, often choose to part ways with their charges upon reaching the edge of the Wastes. The reasons are many—some cite the dangers of the land, while others simply adhere to the limits of their contract—leaving travelers to face the remainder of their journey alone. It is here, in the shadow of the ruins and under the watchful gaze of dragons, that many journeys come to an untimely end, not at the hands of the Ribbon, but swallowed by the vastness of the wasteland.</p><p>Yet, some Shadewalkers, whether driven by extra payment or a rare sense of duty, agree to guide their parties through the Wastes, all the way to the relative safety of Daybreak. These journeys are fraught with danger, requiring not only knowledge of the land but also the ability to navigate its many hazards. Such treks are expensive and fraught with peril, but for those determined to reach their destination, they represent the only glimmer of hope in a land otherwise abandoned to despair.</p>","summary":"The Wastes, a name as desolate as the landscape it describes, stretch out to the east of Runvegr, a vast expanse of desolation and decay. This region, once perhaps thriving with cities and life, now serves as a stark…","sort":275000,"sourceJournal":"Ember Hinterlands"},{"name":"Wraithwater Lagoon","category":"Places","group":"Ember Hinterlands","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"wraithwater-lagoon","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Wraithwater.webp","tags":["Wilderness","Western Eilune"],"mainTag":"Ember Hinterlands","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Wraithwater Lagoon is a mystical body of water located between the western and eastern continents of Eilune. It lies directly off the coast of the Wastes to the west and is bordered by the Caaddorret Wilds to the east. The lagoon is characterized by its eerie, phosphorescent glow and the ethereal mist that perpetually hovers above its surface. It is said to be a place where the veil between the material world and the spirit realm is thin, allowing for occasional glimpses of ghostly figures and fleeting whispers of the past.</p><p>The water of Wraithwater Lagoon is allegedly imbued with arcane properties, believed to have been affected by the magical energies released during the Divergence. Those who venture into the lagoon's depths or drink from the water often report strange visions and encounters with restless spirits. Others who drink of the water seemingly vanish, leaving not a trace behind. The lagoon is both feared and revered by those who live near its shores, who consider it a place of power and mystery.</p>","summary":"Wraithwater Lagoon is a mystical body of water located between the western and eastern continents of Eilune. It lies directly off the coast of the Wastes to the west and is bordered by the Caaddorret Wilds to the east.…","sort":300000,"sourceJournal":"Ember Hinterlands"},{"name":"Bright Plains","category":"Places","group":"Coskoreia Republic","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"bright-plains","hero":"assets/Background-BrightPlains.png","tags":["Wilderness","Eastern Eilune"],"mainTag":"Coskoreia","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>The transformation of the Bright Plains from a once-majestic forest into the unique and vibrant expanse it is today is a tale of resilience and rebirth. This land, at the southern tip of the eastern continent, carries the scars of its past and the promise of its future in equal measure. The original greatwood, a vast and ancient forest claimed by a Wisivashun nation state, bore witness to centuries of history until an Efra Dorei invasion set off a chain of events that would forever alter its destiny.</p><p>The arrival of the Ribbon, a cataclysmic event shrouded in mystery, marked the beginning of the greatwood's demise. Disease and decay spread like wildfire through the once-lush canopy, leaving behind a poisoned wasteland bathed in perpetual dusk. The once-vibrant ecosystem was reduced to a shadow of its former self, a stark reminder of the fragility of nature.</p><p>However, the Divergence heralded a new era for this beleaguered land. The dying woods, succumbing to disease, transformed as if by magic. Ashes gave way to rolling hills carpeted with pale pink grass, a stark contrast to the dark decay that preceded it. The remnants of the forest erupted in a kaleidoscope of colors, with trees displaying hues of bright and pastel shades previously unimaginable. This miraculous transformation turned the Bright Plains into a wonderland of color and light.</p><p>Perhaps the most striking change was the sky itself. Gone were the familiar blues of day and the dark canvas of night, replaced by a perpetual twilight of rose and orange hues. This ever-changing sky casts the Bright Plains in an eternal glow, creating a land where darkness seems banished and the concept of time blurs. The absence of the sun, moons, and stars since the Divergence has left the inhabitants of this land under a sky unlike any other, where the light plays across the landscape in endless variations.</p><p>Beneath the vibrant surface of the Bright Plains lie deposits of \"brightglass,\" a remarkable substance born from the turmoil of the Divergence. This strong, rigid, and translucent material possesses unique properties, including the ability to store magic without the risk of unleashing destructive forces. The Coskoreia Republic, a nation that rose from the ashes of the old world, has harnessed the potential of brightglass in their ambitious endeavors to fuse magic and technology. Their experiments have led to advancements that push the boundaries of what is possible, positioning the Coskoreia Republic at the forefront of a new age of innovation.</p><p>The Bright Plains, with its stunning landscapes, magical skies, and the pioneering spirit of its people, stands as a testament to the power of transformation. It is a land of endless day, where the past is interwoven with the present, and the future is being written by those who dare to dream. The Coskoreia Republic thrives in this unique environment, a beacon of progress in a world that has known much darkness. Here, in the Bright Plains, the sun never sets, and the possibilities are as limitless as the ever-changing hues of the sky above.</p>","summary":"The transformation of the Bright Plains from a once-majestic forest into the unique and vibrant expanse it is today is a tale of resilience and rebirth. This land, at the southern tip of the eastern continent, carries…","sort":0,"sourceJournal":"Coskoreia Republic"},{"name":"Coskoreia Republic","category":"Places","group":"Coskoreia Republic","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"coskoreia-republic","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/StainedGlass-Republic.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"Coskoreia","subtitle":"","meta":[{"label":"Population","value":"~3.2 million"},{"label":"Area","value":"60,000 square miles"},{"label":"Government","value":"Federal Republic with Rotating Capital"},{"label":"Demonym","value":"Coskoreian"},{"label":"Ruler","value":"The Dominant of the Republic"},{"label":"Founded","value":"c. 150–250 PD"}],"lists":[{"label":"Notable Locations","items":[{"name":"Roseate Groves","description":"Northern boundary forest of Coskoreian territory; a natural and symbolic threshold"},{"name":"Bright Plains","description":"The Republic’s defining brightglass-rich region; center of extraction, identity, and conflict"},{"name":"The Ribbon Frontier","description":"Dangerous northern/western edge shaped by mists, isolation, and external threat"},{"name":"Reclaimed Wisivashu Cities","description":"Ancient urban foundations repurposed into thriving republican centers"},{"name":"Primary Republican Cities","description":"The major cities among which the seat of the Dominant rotates"},{"name":"Brightglass Mines","description":"Industrial and economic lifeblood of the Republic","icon":"assets/Background-Brightglass.webp"},{"name":"Laboratories and Workshops","description":"Centers of technological development powered by brightglass innovation"},{"name":"Border with Efra Dorei","description":"A growing flashpoint as Efra Dorei presses into brightglass territory"}]}],"content":"<p>Nestled beyond the chaotic mists of the Ribbon, the Coskoreia Republic stands as a bastion of unity and innovation amidst a world teeming with threats both known and unfathomable. Born from the necessity of survival and the desire for mutual protection, this conglomerate of independent territories has forged a society unlike any other, characterized by its resilience, ingenuity, and the remarkable substance at the heart of its advancement: brightglass.</p><p>The foundation of the Republic was laid on the remnants of the Wisivashu civilization, whose sprawling cities were left to time and the elements following their evacuation of the continent. These architectural marvels, once symbols of a fallen empire, have been claimed and revitalized by the citizens of the Republic. What were once silent, empty streets now thrum with the energy of a people determined to carve out a place for themselves in this new world. The cities, each a testament to the Republic's adaptive spirit, are continuously reshaped to meet the needs and ambitions of their inhabitants.</p><p>The Coskoreia Republic is a land where light is perpetual in the sky, an eternal a perpetual twilight of rose and orange hues that serves as a constant reminder of their separation from \"the Old World.\" This unyielding light has influenced the society in profound ways, fostering a culture of ceaseless activity and innovation. The majority of Coskoreians have found their calling in the mines, extracting the luminous brightglass, or in laboratories and workshops, pushing the boundaries of what their crystalline technology can achieve. This technology, powered by the magical properties of brightglass, has propelled the Republic into a new era of prosperity and power.</p><p>The governance of the Republic is as unique as the land itself. Eschewing the notion of a static capital, the leadership, known as the Dominant of the Republic, is a position of high honor and responsibility that rotates among the primary cities. This system ensures that power is distributed evenly and that each city has a stake in the management and future of the Republic. The Dominant is democratically elected, a reflection of the Republic's commitment to fairness and communal decision-making.</p><p>However, the peace and progress of the Republic are under threat. The Efra Dorei, with motives as murky as the Ribbon itself, have begun encroaching upon the Republic's territories. Their eyes are set on the brightglass, seeking to monopolize this resource for reasons yet unknown. This aggression has stirred unease within the Republic, as the brightglass is not just a source of energy but a symbol of their identity and achievements.</p><p>As tensions mount, the Coskoreia Republic finds itself at a crossroads, facing an external threat that could unravel the very fabric of their society. The citizens, united by their shared history and the light of the brightglass, must navigate these turbulent times with the same courage and ingenuity that gave birth to their nation. In the face of adversity, the Coskoreia Republic stands ready to defend its freedom, its advancements, and the future that they have worked so tirelessly to build.</p>","summary":"Nestled beyond the chaotic mists of the Ribbon, the Coskoreia Republic stands as a bastion of unity and innovation amidst a world teeming with threats both known and unfathomable. Born from the necessity of survival and…","sort":0,"sourceJournal":"Coskoreia Republic"},{"name":"Akh Afh","category":"Places","group":"Coskoreia Republic","type":"text","slug":"akh-afh","hero":"assets/Background-AfkAfh.webp","tags":["Coskoreia Republic"],"mainTag":"Coskoreia","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table><tbody><tr><td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Background-AfkAfh.webp\"/></td><td><p><strong>Region: </strong>Coskoreia</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>Afk Afh, nestled within the towering peaks of a mountain range adorned with deep red rock, stands as a testament to the resilience and ingenuity of the people of the Coskoreia Republic. The city emerges from the rugged landscape like a beacon of civilization amidst the untamed wilderness.</p><p>As with the rest of the Coskoreia Republic, Afk Afh basks in the perpetual daylight that bathes the land in an otherworldly glow. The sun, a mysterious and unyielding presence, never seems to dip below the horizon, casting the sky in a perpetual dance of shifting colors. In perpetuity, the heavens above are adorned with hues of orange, pink, and gold, creating a mesmerizing spectacle that captivates all who behold it.</p><p>At the heart of Afk Afh lies the lifeblood of the region: the Brightglass mines. Carved deep into the heart of the mountains, these mines are the source of the precious material that fuels the economy of the entire continent. Here, miners toil day and night, extracting Brightglass from the veins of the earth with painstaking precision. The air is heavy with the scent of minerals and machinery, and the sound of pickaxes and drills echoes through the cavernous tunnels.</p><p>But Afk Afh is more than just a mining town; it is a center of innovation and discovery. Artificers and alchemists from across Eilune flock to the city, drawn by the promise of unlocking the secrets of Brightglass and harnessing its power. In workshops and laboratories scattered throughout the city, these scholars push the boundaries of magic and technology, seeking new ways to fuse the two into revolutionary inventions.</p><p>Despite its bustling industry and bustling streets, Afk Afh remains a close-knit community, bound together by the shared challenges of living in proximity to the Ribbon. The constant threat of Sorrow Storms and the Wild Hunt looms large, casting a shadow over daily life. In response, the people of Afk Afh have forged bonds of camaraderie and mutual support, standing together in the face of adversity.</p><p>As the sun casts its warm glow over the city, illuminating the towering peaks and winding streets below, the spirit of resilience and determination that defines Afk Afh shines bright. It is a city of contrasts, where the beauty of the natural world collides with the ingenuity of mortal endeavor, creating a tapestry of life unlike any other in Eilune.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>","summary":"Region: Coskoreia Afk Afh, nestled within the towering peaks of a mountain range adorned with deep red rock, stands as a testament to the resilience and ingenuity of the people of the Coskoreia Republic. The city…","sort":2000,"sourceJournal":"Coskoreia"},{"name":"Sy Araeng","category":"Places","group":"Coskoreia Republic","type":"text","slug":"sy-araeng","hero":"assets/Background-SyAraeng.webp","tags":["Coskoreia Republic"],"mainTag":"Coskoreia","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<table><tbody><tr><td><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/Background-SyAraeng.webp\"/></td><td><p><strong>Region: </strong>Coskoreia</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>Sy Araeng, nestled in a forest of towering trees with pale pink grass and leaves, is a city-state known for its stunning natural beauty. The buildings are constructed from the wood of the surrounding trees, blending seamlessly with the environment. The streets are lined with colorful flowers, and the air is filled with the sweet fragrance of blossoms.</p><p>The city is renowned for its skilled artisans, who craft exquisite works from the unique materials found in the forest. Woodworkers create intricate furniture and carvings, while weavers produce delicate textiles from the fibers of rare plants. Alchemists and herbalists gather rare plants and fungi from the forest, using them to create potent medicines.</p><p>Not just dedicated to the arts, Sy Araeng is also a center of learning, with scholars and sages studying the mysteries of brightglass, using previously abandoned Wisivashu laboratories and libraries. The city's libraries are filled with various texts and scrolls, detailing the history of the Bright Plains post-Divergence.</p><p>The city is governed by a council of elders, chosen for their wisdom and knowledge of the forest. They ensure that the city maintains a balance with nature, protecting the delicate ecosystem that sustains them. Sy Araeng is a peaceful city, dedicated to preserving the beauty of its surroundings and living in harmony with the natural world.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>","summary":"Region: Coskoreia Sy Araeng, nestled in a forest of towering trees with pale pink grass and leaves, is a city-state known for its stunning natural beauty. The buildings are constructed from the wood of the surrounding…","sort":3000,"sourceJournal":"Coskoreia"},{"name":"Caaddorret Wilds","category":"Places","group":"Caaddorret Wilds","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"caaddorret-wilds","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/StainedGlass-Wilds.webp","tags":[],"mainTag":"The Wilds","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>The Caaddoret Wilds stretch as far as the eye can see, a boundless sea of golden and green grasses that sway gently in the breeze. This expanse of untamed grassland, known for its rolling hills and deep valleys, holds within it the ancient echoes of the Efra Dorei and Wisivashu civilizations, whose outposts now lie in crumbling ruin, overtaken by the relentless embrace of nature. These stone remnants, covered in vines and moss, serve as a somber reminder of the fleeting dominion of empires over the wilds and of the wars past.</p><p>Beneath the fertile soil of the Caaddoret Wilds lies a wealth of sulfur, giving the earth a distinct yellow hue in certain areas and a pungent smell after rains. This mineral-rich ground has the potential to revolutionize agriculture, promising bountiful yields to those who dare to cultivate it. However, the promise of prosperity is curtailed by a significant challenge—the scarcity of clean, fresh water. The few streams and ponds that dot the landscape are often tainted by sulfur and other minerals, making the water unsuitable for consumption or irrigation without significant purification.</p><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-CaaddorretWilds.webp\"/><p>The harsh conditions have discouraged permanent human settlement, turning the Caaddoret Wilds into a land of nomads and wanderers. Tribes of hardy folk roam the grasslands, following the elusive paths of underground water sources and seasonal rains. They live in harmony with the land, moving with the cycles of nature, and have developed unique methods to filter and conserve water.</p><p>The Wilds are also home to a diverse array of wildlife, some of which are uniquely adapted to the sulfur-rich environment. Herds of bison-like creatures with metallic-hued fur roam the plains, grazing on the sulfur-infused grasses that give their meat a distinct flavor, sought after by gourmet chefs and alchemists alike. Predators, like the sulfur-winged hawks, circle the skies, their golden plumage gleaming in the sunlight, a testament to the wild's untamed beauty.</p><p>Adventurers and treasure hunters are drawn to the Caaddoret Wilds by tales of ancient artifacts buried within the ruins and the promise of undiscovered resources. However, they quickly learn that the Wilds are not easily tamed. The land is guarded by natural defenses, from quicksand pits hidden among the tall grasses to sudden, violent thunderstorms fueled by the sulfur-charged air.</p><p>The Caaddoret Wilds, with their untamed beauty and hidden dangers, stand as a testament to the resilience of the natural world and the mysteries that await those brave enough to explore them.</p>","summary":"The Caaddoret Wilds stretch as far as the eye can see, a boundless sea of golden and green grasses that sway gently in the breeze. This expanse of untamed grassland, known for its rolling hills and deep valleys, holds…","sort":100000,"sourceJournal":"Caaddorret Wilds"},{"name":"Daybreak","category":"Places","group":"Caaddorret Wilds","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"daybreak","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Daybreak.webp","tags":["City","Eastern Eilune","Shadewalkers","Ribbon"],"mainTag":"The Wilds","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Nestled precariously on the cusp of civilization and untamed wilderness, Daybreak stands as a beacon of respite and resourcefulness. This last major outpost, straddling the border between the desolate expanse of The Wastes and the verdant sprawl of the Caaddoret Wilds, serves as a crucial waypoint for travelers daring to navigate The Ribbon.</p><p>In Daybreak, the air is filled with a sense of rugged determination. Here, amidst a landscape dotted with structures that tell a story of ambition cut short, the town thrives against all odds. Wisivashun architectural marvels, characterized by their elegant lines and sophisticated design, stand in silent testimony to a dream unfulfilled. These half-completed edifices, abandoned when Wisivashu relinquished control amid escalating conflicts, now blend with a patchwork of buildings erected by those who came after. The result is a town with a unique aesthetic, where every street corner tells a tale of convergence—a melting pot of cultures from across Eilune finding common ground in survival and commerce.</p><p>Though Daybreak may lack the sprawling markets or arcane libraries of a capital city, it compensates with a vibrant marketplace alive with the sounds of haggling, the scent of exotic spices, and the sight of goods from all corners of the world. Inns and taverns, each with its own story and character, offer warm beds and hearty meals to weary travelers. While magical or enchanted items are a rare sight, the town's shops are well-stocked with practical wares and provisions essential for survival in the harsh environments that lie beyond its borders.</p><p>The population of Daybreak is as diverse as the architecture. Among the population, one can find Shadewalkers, the elusive guides of The Ribbon. While most use Daybreak merely as a pit stop, replenishing supplies before plunging back into the shadowy realms they traverse, a few have chosen to call this outpost home. These permanent residents contribute to the town's defenses and share their knowledge of the lands beyond with those brave enough to explore them.</p><p>Despite its origin as an abandoned project, Daybreak has grown into something far greater, a testament to resilience and adaptability. Its inhabitants, drawn from all races and walks of life, have imbued the town with a spirit of camaraderie and mutual support. Daybreak is not just a place to rest or resupply; it's a community that stands as a frontier of hope and a bulwark against the encroaching chaos of the surrounding lands. In the evening, as the sun dips below the horizon, casting a golden glow over the wilds and wastes alike, Daybreak lives up to its name.</p>","summary":"Nestled precariously on the cusp of civilization and untamed wilderness, Daybreak stands as a beacon of respite and resourcefulness. This last major outpost, straddling the border between the desolate expanse of The…","sort":300000,"sourceJournal":"Caaddorret Wilds"},{"name":"Mahdorei","category":"Places","group":"Caaddorret Wilds","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"mahdorei","hero":"","tags":["Eastern Eilune","City","Efra Dorei"],"mainTag":"The Wilds","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Mahdorei is an Efra Dorei town and the farthest western known village of their nation. Little is known of the interior to outsiders as it is protected by a variety of mundane and magical defenses.</p><p>Recently, the Coskoreia Republic has begun to feel unease as the town appears to grow larger and there are some fears of a possible invasion.</p>","summary":"Mahdorei is an Efra Dorei town and the farthest western known village of their nation. Little is known of the interior to outsiders as it is protected by a variety of mundane and magical defenses. Recently, the…","sort":400000,"sourceJournal":"Caaddorret Wilds"},{"name":"Sulfur Lake","category":"Places","group":"Caaddorret Wilds","type":"simple-quest.location","slug":"sulfur-lake","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-SulfurLake.webp","tags":["Lake","Eastern Eilune","Wilderness"],"mainTag":"The Wilds","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Sulfur Lake, once a vibrant oasis teeming with life, now stands as a haunting testament to the transformative power of the Divergence. Situated amidst a landscape that starkly contrasts with its current desolation, this lake was renowned for its crystal-clear waters and the abundance of fish that darted beneath its surface. Families and fishermen from nearby settlements would spend days by its banks, basking in the serene beauty and bounty it offered. However, the cataclysmic events of the Divergence irrevocably altered its fate.</p><p>The soil, rich in sulfur, began a slow and relentless assault on the lake's purity following the upheaval. Over time, the sulfur seeped into the waters, turning them from a vibrant blue to a murky, yellowish hue. The once-abundant fish populations dwindled and disappeared, leaving the lake lifeless. Vegetation along the banks withered, and the air became thick with the choking smell of sulfur. What was once a place of gathering and joy has since been shunned, a noxious reminder of the world's fragility.</p><p>Despite its forbidding appearance, Sulfur Lake has given rise to legends and rumors, the most persistent of which involves a mysterious settlement said to exist at its northernmost point. Old maps, crafted with painstaking detail, mark this location with symbols of habitation, yet none bear a name for this enigmatic place. Many have speculated on the nature of this settlement: a lost civilization untouched by the Divergence, a secret enclave of scholars studying the lake's transformation, or perhaps a mere cartographic error, a ghost town that never was.</p><p>Adventurers and explorers, drawn by tales of the unnamed settlement and the allure of uncovering its secrets, have ventured to Sulfur Lake's northern shores. Yet, all such expeditions have returned empty-handed, with no evidence of habitation past or present. The lake's poisonous waters and the treacherous terrain surrounding it pose significant challenges, deterring all but the most determined or foolhardy.</p><p>Whispers among the local populace suggest that the settlement's absence is no mere accident but the result of deliberate obfuscation. Some speak of protective enchantments cast by the settlement's inhabitants to shield themselves from the outside world. Others hint at darker forces at play, suggesting that the lake itself guards the secrets of the vanished town, swallowing any evidence of its existence.</p><p>Sulfur Lake, with its dead waters and the mystery of the lost settlement, continues to captivate the imagination of many. It stands as a somber monument to change and loss, yet also a beacon for those who seek the unknown. The true nature of the settlement and the reasons for its disappearance remain shrouded in mystery, a puzzle that waits to be solved by those brave enough to face the lake's deadly embrace.</p>","summary":"Sulfur Lake, once a vibrant oasis teeming with life, now stands as a haunting testament to the transformative power of the Divergence. Situated amidst a landscape that starkly contrasts with its current desolation, this…","sort":500000,"sourceJournal":"Caaddorret Wilds"},{"name":"Cataclysm","category":"Bestiary","group":"Bestiary","type":"simple-quest.creature","slug":"cataclysm","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/beasts/Ribbonborn%20Cataclysm.webp","tags":["Abberation"],"mainTag":"Ribbonborn","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[{"label":"Properties","items":[{"name":"Height","value":"18-22 feet"},{"name":"Weight","value":"6-9 tons"}]}],"content":"<p>The Ribbonborn Cataclysm is a rare and terrifying aberration, born not from the natural echoes of a Sorrow Storm but from its failure. When two Ribbonborn Laments are torn apart and violently re-fused by unstable vril currents, the result is a towering monstrosity of jagged crystal and storm-forged wrath. Its body is a chaotic lattice of glass and obsidian, fissures glowing with an unstable teal-blue light that pulses like a fractured heartbeat.</p><p>Unlike the mournful grace of the Lament, the Cataclysm is violent chaos given form — its movements are sudden and discordant, its form splitting and reforming in bursts of stormlight as though reality itself struggles to contain it. Its voice is not a howl but a shriek of breaking glass and thunder, a sound that reverberates deep into the bones of its prey.</p><p>Legends claim the Cataclysm is not truly alive but a violent reaction — a storm’s attempt to correct its own imbalance. When slain, its body detonates in a catastrophic burst of shards and vril, as though the storm itself is reclaiming the mistake. The explosion leaves behind no corpse, only fields of glass-like fragments humming faintly with the memory of the storm.</p><p>Few who have faced a Cataclysm survived long enough to speak of it, and those who did describe it as a herald of inevitability: the Ribbon’s reminder that even sorrow has depths yet unexplored.</p>","summary":"The Ribbonborn Cataclysm is a rare and terrifying aberration, born not from the natural echoes of a Sorrow Storm but from its failure. When two Ribbonborn Laments are torn apart and violently re-fused by unstable vril…","sort":-100000,"sourceJournal":"Bestiary Journal"},{"name":"Chocobo","category":"Bestiary","group":"Bestiary","type":"simple-quest.creature","slug":"chocobo","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/lore/Background-Chocobos.webp","tags":["Mount"],"mainTag":"Beast","subtitle":"Kweh!","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Chocobos are large, bird-like creatures that mysteriously appeared in Eilune after the Divergence. With their bright feathers and swift speed, they quickly became a common sight across the continent. Domesticated much like horses, chocobos are now integral to life in Eilune, serving as mounts for travelers and laborers alike.</p><p>Their friendly nature and adaptability make them ideal companions, and they are often used for tasks ranging from plowing fields to racing across the countryside.</p><p>Chocobos are deeply ingrained in Eilune's culture, revered for their beauty, speed, and utility, and their appearance post-Divergence remains a mystery that has sparked much speculation and wonder.</p><p>In Eilune, chocobos are primarily domesticated for transport, farming, and war, but they can still be found in the wild in specific regions. Wild chocobos thrive in environments that provide open space, vegetation for grazing, and natural defenses against predators.</p><hr/><p><strong>Wild Chocobo Habitats in Eilune</strong></p><p><strong>Caaddorret Wilds</strong></p><ul><li><p>A vast, untamed region near the Wastes, filled with rolling hills and patches of dense forest.</p></li><li><p>Known for flocks of wild chocobos, particularly the hardy yellow variety, which adapt well to the rugged terrain.</p></li><li><p>Rare sightings of black chocobos have been reported here, often in deeper, more dangerous areas.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Ember Hinterlands</strong></p><ul><li><p>Near Altar, wild chocobos occasionally roam the rocky outcroppings and sparse vegetation.</p></li><li><p>These chocobos are smaller and more agile, adapted to climbing and navigating the challenging terrain.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Avaric Plains</strong></p><ul><li><p>The warmer, desert region in southern Eilune, known for its golden chocobos.</p></li><li><p>These chocobos are renowned for their endurance and speed, making them prized if captured and tamed.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Highlands of Runvegr</strong></p><ul><li><p>In the colder northern territories, wild chocobos with thicker feathers can be found.</p></li><li><p>They are more solitary and territorial, living in small groups near hot springs or sheltered valleys.</p></li></ul>","summary":"Chocobos are large, bird-like creatures that mysteriously appeared in Eilune after the Divergence. With their bright feathers and swift speed, they quickly became a common sight across the continent. Domesticated much…","sort":-93750,"sourceJournal":"Bestiary Journal"},{"name":"Flickerwolf","category":"Bestiary","group":"Bestiary","type":"simple-quest.creature","slug":"flickerwolf","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/beasts/Flickerwolf.webp","tags":["Beast"],"mainTag":"Vril-Touched","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>Born from the unstable resonance of <strong data-end=\"136\" data-start=\"121\">vril echoes</strong>, <strong>Flickerwolves</strong> are canines twisted by reality-warping energies. Drawn inexplicably to regions where vril echoes linger, these creatures prowl the shifting boundaries of existence, their forms flickering in and out of alignment with the material plane. Their bodies seem to stutter through space, appearing feet away from where they last stood, leaving behind ephemeral afterimages that dissolve into nothingness.</p><p data-end=\"1006\" data-start=\"553\">Flickerwolves are <strong data-end=\"614\" data-start=\"571\">not wholly present in any single moment</strong>, existing in a state of quantum uncertainty that makes them both elusive and terrifying. Their movements are erratic;one second, they lunge at prey, only to blink away before the counterattack lands. When they hunt, they do so with eerie silence, their distorted forms momentarily phasing through obstacles before solidifying with a snap of jaws that can tear through flesh and time alike.</p><p data-end=\"1408\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"1008\">Some scholars theorize that Flickerwolves are not just vril-twisted beasts but <strong data-end=\"1126\" data-start=\"1087\">beings caught between two realities</strong>, forever struggling to anchor themselves. Wherever they appear, signs of vril instability are not far behind. Their presence is a <strong data-end=\"1296\" data-start=\"1257\">harbinger of fractures in the world</strong>, a warning that something deeper lurks beneath the veil of reality, something that, like them, should not exist.</p>","summary":"Born from the unstable resonance of vril echoes , Flickerwolves are canines twisted by reality-warping energies. Drawn inexplicably to regions where vril echoes linger, these creatures prowl the shifting boundaries of…","sort":-87500,"sourceJournal":"Bestiary Journal"},{"name":"Frostvein Remorhaz","category":"Bestiary","group":"Bestiary","type":"simple-quest.creature","slug":"frostvein-remorhaz","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/beasts/Remorhaz.webp","tags":["Beast"],"mainTag":"Monstrosity","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[{"label":"Properties","items":[{"name":"Avg Length","value":"21-42 feet"},{"name":"Avg Weight","value":"10,000 lbs"}]},{"label":"Immunities & Vulnerabilities","items":[{"tag":"Fire"},{"tag":"Cold"}]}],"content":"<p>The <strong>Frostvein Remorhaz</strong> is a primordial predator born of the age when Eilune’s tectonic shell buckled beneath vrilic storms. This serpentine horror coils through ice caverns and frozen chasms with unnatural grace, its vast, plated body shifting in rippling waves of cerulean chitin. Beneath its armor, molten vril circulates in glowing channels, veins of living flame that pulse with each breath it draws.</p><p>Its crown of spined frills can flare wide like frostbitten wings, scattering sparks of crystallized heat that hiss against the snow. When it rises to strike, the air distorts in a halo of shimmering cold and blistering warmth, as if the creature cannot choose whether it belongs to fire or ice.</p><p>The Remorhaz hunts by sensing vibrations through permafrost and glacier walls, emerging in an eruption of steam and cracking ice. Those who witness it describe a keening shriek, metal bending, stone tearing, and something ancient roaring beneath it all. Its fiery dorsal plates burn hot enough to melt steel, while its fangs drip with freezing venom, the paradox of its nature embodied in every attack.</p><p>When threatened, the Frostvein Remorhaz coils into a defensive spiral, heating its armor to a white-hot blaze that can melt weapons and ignite the very breath of the air around it. Few creatures in Eilune embody the world’s paradoxes as completely: frost and flame, stillness and violence, ancient instinct warped by vril into something both magnificent and monstrously wrong.</p>","summary":"The Frostvein Remorhaz is a primordial predator born of the age when Eilune’s tectonic shell buckled beneath vrilic storms. This serpentine horror coils through ice caverns and frozen chasms with unnatural grace, its…","sort":-68750,"sourceJournal":"Bestiary Journal"},{"name":"Frostwail Lupin","category":"Bestiary","group":"Bestiary","type":"simple-quest.creature","slug":"frostwail-lupin","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/beasts/FrostwailLupin.webp","tags":["Beast"],"mainTag":"Vril-Touched","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p><strong>Frostwail Lupins</strong> are a rare, frostborn strain of wolf, touched by ancient vril storms that once swept across the north. Larger than common wolves, their bodies are lean and wiry, cloaked in thick silver-white fur that seems almost translucent in the right light, blending seamlessly with snow and mist. Their eyes glow faintly with a soft, ghostly blue, and their breath frosts the air even in the heart of winter.</p><p>What makes them truly feared, however, is their song - a mournful, almost melodic howl that carries for miles, warping in pitch and echoing strangely across the open plains. It's said the Frostwail is not just a call, but a way to disorient prey, confusing travelers into straying from their path or circling back into ambushes. Superstition among northern folk holds that hearing the Frostwail three times is an omen of death or great change.</p>","summary":"Frostwail Lupins are a rare, frostborn strain of wolf, touched by ancient vril storms that once swept across the north. Larger than common wolves, their bodies are lean and wiry, cloaked in thick silver-white fur that…","sort":-62500,"sourceJournal":"Bestiary Journal"},{"name":"Hellhound","category":"Bestiary","group":"Bestiary","type":"simple-quest.creature","slug":"hellhound","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/beasts/Wild%20Hunt%20Hellhound.webp","tags":["Undead"],"mainTag":"Wild Hunt","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>The Wild Hunt <strong>Hellhound</strong> is a fearsome fiend, forged in the infernal fires of Tialana’s hunt. Its charred, sinewy frame is wreathed in perpetual flames, the embers flickering and dancing with each deliberate movement. Twin orbs of molten crimson serve as its eyes, glowing with a malevolent intelligence that belies its beastly form. The air around the hellhound ripples with intense heat, and the acrid scent of sulfur and burnt earth announces its arrival long before it strikes.</p><p>Known for its devastating fire breath and relentless pursuit of prey, the Wild Hunt Hellhound thrives in chaos, spreading destruction in its wake. Its bite sears both flesh and spirit, leaving scars that linger long after the wounds have healed. Though deadly alone, these hellhounds are at their most dangerous in pairs or packs, their infernal instincts honed by Tialana’s command.</p><p>Those lucky enough to survive an encounter recount the chilling sound of their growls, akin to the crackling of a blazing pyre. Upon their defeat, the flames of these hellhounds gutter out, leaving behind scorched earth and the faint echo of their infernal howls.</p>","summary":"The Wild Hunt Hellhound is a fearsome fiend, forged in the infernal fires of Tialana’s hunt. Its charred, sinewy frame is wreathed in perpetual flames, the embers flickering and dancing with each deliberate movement.…","sort":-50000,"sourceJournal":"Bestiary Journal"},{"name":"Husk","category":"Bestiary","group":"Bestiary","type":"simple-quest.creature","slug":"husk","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/beasts/Vril-TouchedHusk.webp","tags":["Undead"],"mainTag":"Vril-Touched","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>The <strong data-end=\"101\" data-start=\"80\">Vril-Touched Husk</strong> is a semi-corporeal remnant of a being consumed by unstable vril magic. Its warped form flickers in and out of existence, fractured between moments, as if reality itself struggles to decide whether it still belongs. Hollow eyes glow dimly with residual energy, and its limbs stretch and contract unnaturally, leaving behind ghostly afterimages that dissolve like echoes. When it moves, space distorts around it, warping the air in brief, impossible bends. Those who encounter a Husk often mistake it for a lost spirit, until its claws carve into flesh, severing the boundary between the material and the unreal.</p>","summary":"The Vril-Touched Husk is a semi-corporeal remnant of a being consumed by unstable vril magic. Its warped form flickers in and out of existence, fractured between moments, as if reality itself struggles to decide whether…","sort":75000,"sourceJournal":"Bestiary Journal"},{"name":"Lament","category":"Bestiary","group":"Bestiary","type":"simple-quest.creature","slug":"lament","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/beasts/Ribbonborn%20Lament.webp","tags":["Abberation"],"mainTag":"Ribbonborn","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[{"label":"Properties","items":[{"name":"Height","value":"7 feet"},{"name":"Weight","value":"350 lbs"}]}],"content":"<p>The <strong>Ribbonborn Lament</strong> is a twisted aberration birthed from the chaotic energies of a <strong>Sorrow Storm</strong>. Its jagged, glass-like form shimmers with an eerie glow, veins of iridescent vril pulsing beneath its fractured surface. The creature moves with haunting grace, its reflective eyes showing fleeting glimpses of its prey’s deepest fears.</p><p>Known for its mournful howl and sharp crystalline claws, the Lament <strong>embodies the sorrow and chaos of the Ribbon’s influence</strong>. Survivors of its attacks speak of its body shattering into harmless shards upon defeat, leaving behind a faint trace of its otherworldly origin.</p>","summary":"The Ribbonborn Lament is a twisted aberration birthed from the chaotic energies of a Sorrow Storm . Its jagged, glass-like form shimmers with an eerie glow, veins of iridescent vril pulsing beneath its fractured…","sort":200000,"sourceJournal":"Bestiary Journal"},{"name":"Morbol","category":"Bestiary","group":"Bestiary","type":"simple-quest.creature","slug":"morbol","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/beasts/Morbol.webp","tags":["Monstrosity"],"mainTag":"Plantkind","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>The <strong data-end=\"91\" data-start=\"81\">Morbol</strong> is a nightmarish, carnivorous plant that thrives in swamps, deep forests, and stagnant wetlands. Its bloated mass of writhing vines conceals a gaping maw lined with jagged, yellowed teeth, constantly dripping with a vile, acidic secretion. Numerous tendrils, thick with thorns and rot, lash out to ensnare prey, pulling them into its crushing jaws.</p><p data-end=\"720\" data-start=\"444\">Infamous for its <strong data-end=\"475\" data-start=\"461\">Bad Breath</strong>, the Morbol expels a cloud of noxious fumes potent enough to blind, poison, and disorient even the most seasoned adventurers. The ground around an active Morbol is often strewn with the remains of creatures that succumbed to its toxic stench.</p><p data-end=\"951\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-start=\"722\">While not as rare or as overwhelmingly powerful as its Tyrant kin, the Morbol remains a formidable predator. Scholars of Plantkind warn that encountering one alone is dangerous enough, but where there is one, more may lurk nearby.</p>","summary":"The Morbol is a nightmarish, carnivorous plant that thrives in swamps, deep forests, and stagnant wetlands. Its bloated mass of writhing vines conceals a gaping maw lined with jagged, yellowed teeth, constantly dripping…","sort":300000,"sourceJournal":"Bestiary Journal"},{"name":"Morbol Tyrant","category":"Bestiary","group":"Bestiary","type":"simple-quest.creature","slug":"morbol-tyrant","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/beasts/MorbolTyrant.webp","tags":["Monstrosity"],"mainTag":"Plantkind","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>The <strong data-end=\"121\" data-start=\"81\">Morbol Tyrant</strong> is an ancient horror lurking in the deepest swamps and festering forests, a monstrous evolution of lesser Morbols. Its bloated, writhing form is a tangled mass of venomous vines, swollen roots, and gaping maws that ooze toxic ichor. Thick tendrils lash out like grasping limbs, spreading the Tyrant’s corruption wherever they touch.</p><p data-end=\"736\" data-start=\"459\">Legends speak of its infamous <strong data-end=\"503\" data-start=\"489\">Bad Breath</strong>, a noxious miasma capable of rotting flesh, searing eyes, and crippling the mind with hallucinations. Even the air around it carries a putrid taint, making prolonged encounters with the beast a test of endurance as much as battle.</p><p data-end=\"946\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-start=\"738\">Those who encounter a Morbol Tyrant rarely escape unscathed—if at all. The land it claims becomes a cursed mire, teeming with its smaller spawn and the husks of those who failed to resist its insidious decay.</p>","summary":"The Morbol Tyrant is an ancient horror lurking in the deepest swamps and festering forests, a monstrous evolution of lesser Morbols. Its bloated, writhing form is a tangled mass of venomous vines, swollen roots, and…","sort":350000,"sourceJournal":"Bestiary Journal"},{"name":"Oathhounds","category":"Bestiary","group":"Bestiary","type":"simple-quest.creature","slug":"oathhounds","hero":"https://assets.forge-vtt.com/6147b3e1d18c221528c79324/worlds/eilune/beasts/Oathhound.webp","tags":["Construct"],"mainTag":"Tesseris Construct","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>The Tesseris Oathhounds, often called Frostmaiden's Hounds by frightened villagers, are terrifying creatures bred and conditioned by the Tesseris to hunt oathbreakers, rogue mages, deserters, and enemies of Runvegr. Their pale fur allows them to vanish into snowstorms, while their unsettling red brightglass eyes shimmer with faint vril energy.</p><p>Oathhounds are not simple beasts. They are trained to track emotional residue, blood traces, and lingering vril signatures. Stories claim an Oathhound can follow a target across an entire mountain range once it has tasted their blood.</p>","summary":"The Tesseris Oathhounds, often called Frostmaiden's Hounds by frightened villagers, are terrifying creatures bred and conditioned by the Tesseris to hunt oathbreakers, rogue mages, deserters, and enemies of Runvegr.…","sort":400000,"sourceJournal":"Bestiary Journal"},{"name":"Whisperwings","category":"Bestiary","group":"Bestiary","type":"simple-quest.creature","slug":"whisperwings","hero":"assets/Background-WhisperWings.webp","tags":["Construct"],"mainTag":"Tesseris Construct","subtitle":"","meta":[],"lists":[],"content":"<p>In the shadowed strongholds of Runvegr, where secrecy weighs heavier than steel, the Tesseris have crafted a chilling marvel: the Whisperwing.</p><p>At first glance, a Whisperwing seems like a creature of myth: a great owl with feathers as pale as snowfall, silent wings, and piercing, almost humanlike eyes. But a closer look reveals the truth - embedded deep into their brows is a Mirrorstone, black as midnight and fused to bone and flesh through secret rites.</p><p>The Mirrorstone, polished and veined with silver, serves as both a receiver and transmitter of thought. Using vril manipulation, the Tesseris forge a permanent connection between bird and stone, binding the creature’s life and mind to its function.</p><p>When tasked with a message, a Tesseris agent simply speaks into a paired stone and across any distance, the Whisperwing is compelled to deliver the memory. Upon reaching its intended target, the owl locks its gaze onto the recipient, and the Mirrorstone pulses, transferring the stored thought or image directly into their mind.</p><p>Whisperwings are utterly loyal, incapable of betraying their purpose. They do not hunt. They do not speak. They exist only to serve the will of their masters.</p><p>Among commonfolk, Whisperwings are viewed with a mixture of awe and dread. In the wild, one does not simply approach a Whisperwing; it approaches you, and you must hope you were the intended target.</p><p>It is said that some Whisperwings, especially those who outlive their handlers, become twisted echoes of their former selves, roaming the mountains like ghost-laden harbingers, still seeking to deliver messages long since forgotten.</p>","summary":"In the shadowed strongholds of Runvegr, where secrecy weighs heavier than steel, the Tesseris have crafted a chilling marvel: the Whisperwing. At first glance, a Whisperwing seems like a creature of myth: a great owl…","sort":500000,"sourceJournal":"Bestiary Journal"}]};
